#### 510",Uses an incorrect conversion factor between hours and seconds,51 km/h * 1000 m/km * 1 h/3000 s = 17 m/s.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,seconds,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""First, we convert the speed from kilometers per hour to meters per second by multiplying by 1000/3600.\n51 km/h * 1000 m/km * 1 h/3600 s = 14.16667 m/s.\nThen, we calculate the distance traveled by multiplying the speed (in m/s) by the time (in seconds).\n14.16667 m/s * 30 s = 425 meters.\n#### 425"", ""original_answer"": 425.0, ""transformed_answer"": 510.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 makes an incorrect unit conversion, changing the denominator for converting kilometers per hour to meters per second from 3600 seconds (correct value representing the number of seconds in an hour) to 3000 seconds, which results in an increased speed from 14.16667 m/s to 17 m/s in the transformed_solution. This mistake then affects the subsequent related step 2, which changes the final answer from 425 meters in the original_solution to 510 meters in the transformed_solution. This is consistent with only considering one step of unit conversion error, so the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:048da1a0f69ddbc9,full,calculation_error,A train 440 meters long is running with a speed of 60 kmph . in what time will it pass a man who is running at 6 kmph in the direction opposite to that in which the train is going ?,"The relative speed of the train and the man is 60 + 6 = 66 kmph = 66*(5/18) m/s = 55/3 m/s.
