#### 34.4",Uses the wrong given average value in the equation,(5a + 8) / 2 = 90,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The average of 2a + 16 and 3a - 8 is (2a + 16 + 3a - 8) / 2 = 5a + 8 / 2 = (5a + 8) / 2\n(5a + 8) / 2 = 94\n5a + 8 = 94 * 2\n5a + 8 = 188\n5a = 188 - 8\n5a = 180\na = 180 / 5\na = 36\n#### 36"", ""original_answer"": 36.0, ""transformed_answer"": 34.4, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 references 94 in the question as 90 wrongly, and calculates (5a + 8) / 2 = 90 instead of (5a + 8) / 2 = 94. Its subsequent related steps, step 3, 4, 5, 6, and 7, will be affected. Step 3 changes from 94 * 2 = 188 to 90 * 2 = 180, step 4 changes from 5a + 8 = 188 to 5a + 8 = 180, step 5 changes from 188 - 8 = 180 to 180 - 8 = 172, step 6 changes from 180 / 5 = 36 to 172 / 5 = 34.4, and step 7 changes from the final answer a = 36 to a = 34.4. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the subsequent related steps of this erroneous step will only inherit its erroneous result and be calculated correctly except for the step referenced incorrectly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
