#### 9",Uses the wrong multiplier to determine a quantity from a comparison,Andy has 6 x 5 = 30 white socks.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Andy has 6 x 4 = 24 white socks.\nHe loses 24/2 = 12 white socks.\nHe still has 12 - 6 = 6 white socks more than black socks.\n#### 6"", ""original_answer"": 6, ""transformed_answer"": 9, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 4 in the question as 5 wrongly, and calculates 6*5=30 instead of 6*4=24. Its subsequent related step, step 2, will be affected, calculating 30/2=15 instead of 24/2=12. The subsequent related step, step 3, will inherit the error from step 2, calculating 15-6=9 instead of 12-6=6. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 2 and step 3 still reference 24 and 12 in the question correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:089247cf540f8d37,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"sarah is driving to the airport . after driving at 50 miles per hour for one hour , she realizes that if she continues at that same average rate she will be an hour late for her flight . she then travels 100 miles per hour for the rest of the trip , and arrives 30 minutes before her flight departs . how many miles did she drive in all ?","She drove 50 miles in the first hour because 50 x 1 = 50
