3x = 2x + 13",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the three consecutive even numbers be x, x+2, and x+4\n3x = 2(x+4) + 7\n3x = 2x + 8 + 7\n3x = 2x + 15\nx = 15\nThe third number is x + 4 = 15 + 4 = 19\n#### 19"", ""original_answer"": 19.0, ""transformed_answer"": 17.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references the number 15 as 13 and incorrectly changes 3x = 2x + 8 + 7 to 3x = 2x + 13. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <3x = 2x + 8 + 7> should be the same as step 3 in the original_solution <3x = 2x + 8 + 7> and calculates its result correctly. Step 4 affects the subsequent steps 5 and 6 related to it. Step 5 incorrectly determines x as 13 (instead of the correct 15), and step 6 incorrectly calculates the third number as 17 (instead of the correct 19). The remaining calculations for steps 5 and 6 are correct based on the erroneous value obtained in step 4. Since only one error needs to be considered, all other steps that reference this result number still reference this number correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:0e1232e6d99921aa,full,referencing_context_value_error,Aaron will jog from home at 3 miles per hour and then walk back home by the same route at 6 miles per hour. How many miles from home can Aaron jog so that he spends a total of 3 hours jogging and walking?,"Let x be the distance from home that Aaron can jog at 5 miles per hour.
It takes x/5 hours for Aaron to jog from home at 5 miles per hour, so it will take x/3 hours to walk back home at 6 miles per hour.
Total time is x/5 + x/(6) = 3
Multiplying through by 30 gives us 6x + 5x = 90
Combining like terms gives us 11x = 90
Dividing both sides by 11 gives us x = 90/11
#### 8.181818181818182",Uses incorrect speeds instead of the stated rates,Let x be the distance from home that Aaron can jog at 5 miles per hour.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the distance from home that Aaron can jog at 3 miles per hour.\nIt takes x/3 hours for Aaron to jog from home at 3 miles per hour, so it will take x/3 hours to walk back home at 6 miles per hour.\nTotal time is x/3 + x/(6) = 3\nMultiplying through by 6 gives us 2x + x = 18\nCombining like terms gives us 3x = 18\nDividing both sides by 3 gives us x = 6\n#### 6"", ""original_answer"": 6.0, ""transformed_answer"": 8.181818181818182, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 3 in the question as 5 wrongly, and calculates the time based on x/5 instead of x/3. This error affects subsequent steps, leading to a wrong equation 6x + 5x = 90 instead of the correct 2x + x = 18. Dividing by the right coefficient to solve for x gives us 90/11 instead of 18/3. All other steps correctly reference the numbers from the question, except the step where the erroneous reference is made."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:0e5d019813d3ba97,full,counting_error,"reeya obtained 55, 67, 76, 82 and 55 out of 100 in different subjects, what will be the average?","The total of marks obtained by reeya is 55 + 67 + 76 + 82 + 55 = 335
