#### 83.75",Counts the number of observations incorrectly when computing the average,The total number of subjects is 4,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total of marks obtained by reeya is 55 + 67 + 76 + 82 + 55 = 335\nThe total number of subjects is 5\nThe average marks obtained by reeya is 335 / 5 = 67\n#### 67"", ""original_answer"": 67.0, ""transformed_answer"": 83.75, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 erroneously counts the number of subjects as 4 instead of 5. This counting error results in the incorrect calculation of the average in step 3, which changes from 335 / 5 = 67 to 335 / 4 = 83.75. The rest of the steps in the transformed_solution and the calculations done before the wrong step in the original_solution are correct, which keeps the error isolated to a single instance."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:0e6ff71ef0102833,full,referencing_context_value_error,"Three siblings are born 5 years apart, each. If the eldest child is 20 years old now, what's the total of the ages of the three siblings 10 years from now?","Ten years from now, the elder child will be 20+10 = 30 years old.
If the elder child is 20 years old now, the second born is 25-5 = 20 years old, 5 years younger than the firstborn.
The second-born will be 20+10 = 30 years old ten years from now.
