Time taken with new speed: 70 / 65 = 1.077 hours
#### 1.077 hours",Uses an incorrect distance value when calculating time,Time taken with new speed: 70 / 65 = 1.077 hours,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Convert 65 min to hours: 65 / 60 = 1.083 hours\nCalculate the distance: 60 x 1.083 = 65 km\nNew speed is 60 + 5 = 65 km/hr\nTime taken with new speed: 65 / 65 = 1 hour\n#### 1 hour"", ""original_answer"": ""1 hour"", ""transformed_answer"": ""1.077 hours"", ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references the increased average speed as 70 km/hr from the previous step instead of 65 km/hr and changes 65 / 65 = 1 hour to 70 / 65 = 1.077 hours. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <New speed is 60 + 5 = 65 km/hr> should be the same as the step 3 in the original_solution <New speed is 60 + 5 = 65 km/hr> and calculates its result 65 km/hr correctly. The erroneous step 4 results in a miscalculated time taken with the new speed, but since we only consider one step error, all other steps that reference these numbers still reference them correctly. Furthermore, the transformed_answer should be different from the original_answer, which is achieved with the mistake in referencing."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:144e0467ca1f0346,full,calculation_error,"Lidia has a collection of books. Her collection is four times bigger than the collection which her friend Susan has. In total Susan and Lidia, both have 3000 books. How many books does Susan have in her collection?","Let x be the number of books in Susan's collection.
