eic,eic:171b7038d0a6b251,full,referencing_context_value_error,"In a group of dogs and people, the number of legs was 28 more than twice the number of heads. How many dogs were there? [Assume none of the people or dogs is missing a leg.]","Let d be the number of dogs and p be the number of people.
Each dog has 4 legs and each person has 2 legs, so the total number of legs is 4d + 2p.
The total number of heads is d + p.
4d + 2p = 26 + 2(d + p)
4d + 2p = 26 + 2d + 2p
2d = 26
d = 13
#### 13",Uses the wrong constant in the stated relationship,4d + 2p = 26 + 2(d + p),ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let d be the number of dogs and p be the number of people.\nEach dog has 4 legs and each person has 2 legs, so the total number of legs is 4d + 2p.\nThe total number of heads is d + p.\n4d + 2p = 28 + 2(d + p)\n4d + 2p = 28 + 2d + 2p\n2d = 28\nd = 14\n#### 14"", ""original_answer"": 14.0, ""transformed_answer"": 13.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 references 28 in the question as 26 wrongly, and calculates 26 + 2(d + p) instead of 28 + 2(d + p). Its subsequent related step will be affected, resulting in 2d being equal to 26 instead of 28. This leads to the incorrect calculation of d = 13 instead of d = 14 in step 6. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 5 still references the correct relationship 4d + 2p = 28 + 2d + 2p."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:17825f65b3576709,full,operator_error,Guadalupe owns 2 rectangular tracts of land. One is 300m by 500m and the other is 250m by 630m. The combined area of these 2 tracts is how many square meters?,"The area of the first tract is 300 x 500 = 150000 square meters.
