eic,eic:1e2f7c37890597c0,full,confusing_formula_error,a sixth grade teacher asked her students to draw rectangles with positive integer length and a perimeter of 42. the difference between the largest and smallest possible areas of the rectangles that the students could have come up with is ?,"The perimeter formula for a rectangle is 2(length + width) = 42
