#### 7.41",Miscounts the occurrences of different daily quantities when calculating a total,The total number of hours Sheila works in a week is 8 + 8 + 6 + 6 + 6 = 34 hours,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total number of hours Sheila works in a week is 8 + 8 + 8 + 6 + 6 = 36 hours\nShe earns $252 per week\nTo find her hourly rate: 252 / 36 = 7\n#### 7"", ""original_answer"": 7.0, ""transformed_answer"": 7.41, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 erroneously counts the hours worked on Wednesday as 6 hours instead of 8 hours, changing the total number of hours worked from 36 to 34. As a result, step 3 changes from 252 / 36 = 7 to 252 / 34 = 7.41. This error in counting the hours for one day created an error in the transformed_answer which should be different from the original_answer. The subsequent step is affected by the changed total, while the previous step and unrelated steps remain the same."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
