#### -32.5",Adds the constant incorrectly when rearranging an equation,"20x = 130 or -20x + 10 = 110
x = 6.5 or -20x = 100",ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""|20x - 10| = 110\n20x - 10 = 110 or -(20x - 10) = 110\n20x = 120 or -20x + 10 = 110\nx = 6 or -20x = 100\nx = 6 or x = -5\nProduct of the values of x is 6 * -5 = -30\n#### -30"", ""original_answer"": -30.0, ""transformed_answer"": -32.5, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references 120 in the equation 20x = 120 wrongly as 130, and calculates 20x = 130 instead of 20x = 120. Its subsequent related steps will be affected, but the calculation of the step related to the error will still be correct. So step 4 becomes x = 6.5 instead of x = 6 and the final product becomes 6.5 * -5 = -32.5 instead of 6 * -5 = -30."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:26bd53f4c4d5ff5d,full,referencing_context_value_error,"in the coordinate plane , points ( x , 1 ) and ( 18 , y ) are on line k . if line k passes through the origin and has slope 1 / 2 , then x + y =","The line passes through the origin, so its equation is y=1/2x.
Using point (x,1), 1=1/2x. Multiplying both sides by 2, we get 2= x.
