#### 310",Includes an unprovided quantity in the calculation,Derek also had to pay a school fee of 50 dollars,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Amount spent on textbooks is 960/2 = 480 dollars.\nAmount spent on school supplies is 480/4 = 120 dollars.\nAmount Derek has left 960-480-120 = 360 dollars.\n#### 360"", ""original_answer"": 360.0, ""transformed_answer"": 310.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Derek also had to pay a school fee of 50 dollars>, resulting in step 3 changing from 960-480-120 = 360 dollars in the original_solution to 960-480-120-50 = 310 dollars in the transformed_solution. The additional irrelevant information of paying a school fee affects the final calculation of the money Derek has left. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:27afbb7cc237c6e2,full,operator_error,"At a convention, 16 of 36 delegates arrived with pre-printed name badges. Half of the remaining delegates made their own, hand-written name badges. How many delegates were not wearing name badges?","There were 36-16=20 without pre-printed name badges.
