#### -20",Uses multiplication instead of finding half of a quantity,Then 20*2=40 made hand-written badges,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,half,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""There were 36-16=20 without pre-printed name badges.\nThen 20/2=10 made hand-written badges\nThere were 20-10=10 with no name badge.\n#### 10"", ""original_answer"": 10.0, ""transformed_answer"": -20.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""This example changes the division in step 2 into multiplication, turning 20/2=10 into 20*2=40. This results in an incorrect number of delegates making hand-written badges, which further affects step 3, changing 20-10=10 to 20-40=-20 for the number of delegates with no name badge. The operator change leads to an incorrect result for step 2, which then causes the subsequent step to be affected, although the calculations in step 3 are technically correct given the incorrect information from step 2."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:2874cd56598f2240,full,missing_step,"In a group of dogs and people, the number of legs was 28 more than twice the number of heads. How many dogs were there? [Assume none of the people or dogs is missing a leg.]","Let d be the number of dogs and p be the number of people.
The total number of legs is 4d + 2p.
