#### 9.5",Uses the wrong difference when forming an increased quantity,"On Sunday, Bill ran x + 6 miles",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the number of miles Bill ran on Saturday\nOn Sunday, Bill ran x + 4 miles\nJulia ran 2 * (x + 4) = 2x + 8 miles on Sunday\nThe total number of miles ran on Saturday and Sunday is x + (x + 4) + (2x + 8) = 4x + 12\nWe know the total was 32, so 4x + 12 = 32\n4x = 20\nx = 5\nBill ran x + 4 = 5 + 4 = 9 miles on Sunday\n#### 9"", ""original_answer"": 9.0, ""transformed_answer"": 9.5, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""The counting error is introduced in step 2 by changing the number of extra miles Bill ran on Sunday from 4 to 6. This affects all subsequent calculations related to the mileage on Sunday (steps 3, 4, and 7), resulting in a different total and individual mileage. The rest of the solution remains the same, and only this single change was made, affecting the related steps but not the unrelated ones, leading to a new transformed answer of 9.5 miles."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:293fe548706009c2,full,operator_error,"A cistern can be filled by a tap in 3 hours while it can be emptied by another tap in 8 hours. If both the taps are opened simultaneously, then after how much time will the cistern get filled?","The combined rate of both taps is 1/3 + 1/8 = 11/24 cistern/hour
