#### 5.5625",Uses the wrong quantity per group when calculating the total.,Troy bakes 2 x 15 = 30 brownie pieces.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Troy bakes 2 x 16 = 32 brownie pieces.\n75% of one pan is 16 x 0.75 = 12 pieces.\nGuests eat 16 + 12 = 28 pieces.\nThis many guests eat the brownies ala mode 28 - 4 = 24.\nThis many scoops are eaten by the guests 24 x 2 = 48.\nThe guests eat this many tubs 48 / 8 = 6 tubs.\n#### 6"", ""original_answer"": 6.0, ""transformed_answer"": 5.5625, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 16 in the question as 15 wrongly, and calculates 2 x 15 = 30 instead of 2 x 16 = 32. Its subsequent related steps, step 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6, will be affected by this error but still calculated correctly based on the erroneous result from step 1. Step 2 uses 15 in the calculation, resulting in 15 x 0.75 = 11.25. Step 3 uses the incorrect values from steps 1 and 2 to compute 15 + 11.25 = 26.25. Step 4 incorrectly derives 26.25 - 4 = 22.25 from the previous total. Step 5 then uses the wrong number of guests to calculate scoops as 22.25 x 2 = 44.5. Step 6 finally divides the incorrect number of scoops by 8 to get 44.5 / 8 = 5.5625 tubs. Please note that you should only consider one error, so all other references to 16 in other steps are correct except for the step that references it incorrectly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
