#### 130",Uses perimeter instead of area to calculate the covered amount,The perimeter of the carpet is 4 + 4 + 9 + 9 = 26 square feet,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,covered,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The area of the carpet is 4 * 9 = 36 square feet\nSince the carpet covers 20% of the living room floor, the total area of the living room floor is 36 / 0.2 = 180 square feet\n#### 180"", ""original_answer"": 180.0, ""transformed_answer"": 130.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 confuses the area and perimeter of a rectangle. The question requires that the area of the rectangle to be solved be equal to the length multiplied by width, rather than the length plus length plus width plus width, which is equivalent to the perimeter of the rectangle, resulting in 4 * 9 = 36 square feet in the original_solution changed to 4 + 4 + 9 + 9 = 26 square feet in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent step 2, changing from 36 / 0.2 = 180 square feet to 26 / 0.2 = 130 square feet. Note that the language description of step 1 < The area of the carpet is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. It should be also noted that you need to only consider one step of confusing formula error, and the other calculation process is still correct. In this example, only step 1 mistakenly uses the formula of rectangular area, while the other calculation process is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
