#### -1",Subtracts sales from an unsupported stock value instead of combining purchases and sales,He now has 30-31=-1 more than at Friday's opening.,ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,stock,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""He sold 10+12+9=31 bicycles.\nHe bought 15+8+11=34 bicycles.\nHe now has 34-31=3 more than at Friday's opening.\n#### 3"", ""original_answer"": 3.0, ""transformed_answer"": -1.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 mistakenly references 34 as 30 from step 2 and changes 34-31=3 to 30-31=-1. It should be noted that step 2 in the transformed_solution <He bought 15+8+11=34 bicycles.> should be the same as the step 2 in the original_solution <He bought 15+8+11=34 bicycles.> and calculates its result 34 correctly. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct. In addition, the transformed_answer should be different from the original_answer, which is why it is now -1 instead of 3."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:2d67d78ff8f54fd6,full,referencing_context_value_error,John's dog has a litter of 8 puppies. He gives away half of them. He keeps one of the remaining puppies. He then takes the remaining puppies and sells them each for $600. He had to give the owner of the stud $300. How much money does he profit?,"He had 8/2=4 left after giving some puppies away
