#### 1200",Uses an incorrect price when calculating total sales revenue,That means he made 3*500=$1500,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""He had 8/2=4 left after giving some puppies away\nHe then keeps one so he sells 4-1=3 puppies\nThat means he made 3*600=$1800\nSo his profit was 1800-300=$1500\n#### 1500"", ""original_answer"": 1500.0, ""transformed_answer"": 1200.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references 600 in the question as 500 wrongly, and calculates 3*500=$1500 instead of 3*600=$1800. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 1500-300=$1200 instead of 1800-300=$1500 in step 4. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 4 still references 300 in the question correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:2dbe8defb006456f,full,adding_irrelevant_information,A train 360 m long is running at a speed of 45 km/hr. In what time will it pass a bridge 240 m long?,"First convert the speed from km/hr to m/s: 45 km/hr x (1000 m/1 km) x (1 hr/3600 s) = 12.5 m/s
