#### 2",Uses a previous operand instead of the current second operand,"Then, 4 ø 2 = 2 ^ 4 / 2 ^ 3 = 16 / 8 = 2",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""3 ø 1 = 2 ^ 3 / 2 ^ 1 = 8 / 2 = 4\nThen, 4 ø 2 = 2 ^ 4 / 2 ^ 2 = 16 / 4 = 4\n#### 4"", ""original_answer"": 4.0, ""transformed_answer"": 2.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 wrongly references the power of 2 as 3 instead of 2, and calculates 2 ^ 4 / 2 ^ 3 = 16 / 8 = 2 instead of 2 ^ 4 / 2 ^ 2 = 16 / 4 = 4. All other steps that reference power of 2 correctly remain unaffected by this mistake."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:313ec73025c67d17,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,James takes 5 oranges and breaks each orange into 8 pieces. He splits the pieces between 4 people. If an orange has 80 calories how many calories does each person get?,"He makes 5*8=40 pieces
