#### 69",Adds an unsupported extra quantity to the calculation,"Because there was an unexpected donation to the shelter, an additional 3 cats were brought in.",ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,8,"{""original_solution"": ""15/3=5 cats were adopted out of 15\nThere were 15-5 = 10 cats left\n5*2=10 more cats were added.\nThis makes 10+10=20 cats in the shelter.\n20*2=40 dogs came into the shelter.\nThere are now 20+40=60 animals in the shelter.\n#### 60"", ""original_answer"": 60.0, ""transformed_answer"": 69.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because there was an unexpected donation to the shelter, an additional 3 cats were brought in>, resulting in step 3 changing from 10+10=20 in the original_solution to 10+10+3=23 in the transformed_solution. The other steps after step 3 also accommodate this change, notably the calculation of the number of dogs. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:33068cbc3fe4ab81,full,counting_error,"A factory produces 5500 toys per week. If the workers at this factory work 5 days a week and if these workers make the same number of toys everyday, how many toys are produced each day?","The total number of toys produced per week is 5500
