#### 40",Uses an incorrect given quantity when calculating the total.,Carlos read 28 books + 32 books = 60 books.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Carlos read 28 books + 30 books = 58 books.\nHe needed to read 100 books - 58 books = 42 books in June.\n#### 42"", ""original_answer"": 42.0, ""transformed_answer"": 40.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 30 books in the question as 32 books wrongly, and calculates 28 books + 32 books = 60 books instead of 28 books + 30 books = 58 books. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 100 books - 60 books = 40 books instead of 100 books - 58 books = 42 books in step 2."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:36845d31d1116b65,full,referencing_context_value_error,"Of 70 players on a football team, 28 are throwers. The rest of the team is divided so one third are left-handed and the rest are right-handed. Assuming that all throwers are right-handed, how many right-handed players are there total?","The number of throwers is 28 and the total number of players is 60, so the number of non-throwers is 60 - 28 = 32.
The number of left-handed players is 32 / 3 = 10.67, approximately 11 when rounded to the nearest whole number.
The number of right-handed non-throwers is 32 - 11 = 21.
The number of right-handed players in the team is 21 (non-throwers) + 28 (throwers) = 49.
#### 49",Uses an incorrect total when calculating the non-throwers,"the total number of players is 60, so the number of non-throwers is 60 - 28 = 32.",ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The number of throwers is 28 and the total number of players is 70, so the number of non-throwers is 70 - 28 = 42.\nThe number of left-handed players is 42 / 3 = 14.\nThe number of right-handed non-throwers is 42 - 14 = 28.\nThe number of right-handed players in the team is 28 (non-throwers) + 28 (throwers) = 56.\n#### 56"", ""original_answer"": 56.0, ""transformed_answer"": 49.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 70 in the question as 60 wrongly, and calculates 60 - 28 = 32 instead of 70 - 28 = 42. Its subsequent related steps, step 2, 3, and 4, will be affected. Step 2 changes from 42 / 3 = 14 to 32 / 3 = approximately 11 when rounded to the nearest whole number. Step 3 changes from 42 - 14 = 28 to 32 - 11 = 21. Step 4 changes from 28 (non-throwers) + 28 (throwers) = 56 to 21 (non-throwers) + 28 (throwers) = 49. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the subsequent related steps of this erroneous step will only inherit its erroneous result and be calculated correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
