#### 100",Uses an incorrect conversion factor between hours and minutes,There are 50 minutes in an hour,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,6,"{""original_solution"": ""The old machine makes 100 bolts per hour and the new machine makes 150 bolts per hour.\nTogether, they make 100 bolts/hour + 150 bolts/hour = 250 bolts per hour.\nTo make a total of 500 bolts, it will take 500 bolts / 250 bolts/hour = 2 hours.\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour, so it will take 2 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 120 minutes for the two machines to make a total of 500 bolts.\n#### 120"", ""original_answer"": 120, ""transformed_answer"": 100, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 4 makes an incorrect unit conversion, which erroneously suggests there are 50 minutes in an hour instead of 60 minutes, resulting in 2 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 120 minutes in the original_solution becoming 2 hours * 50 minutes/hour = 100 minutes in the transformed_solution. This changes the original_answer from 120 minutes to 100 minutes, introducing a unit conversion error. The error is isolated to just this single wrong step, while the other steps' computations remain correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
