#### 400",Makes an arithmetic error when halving a total,there are 300/2 = 100 elephants,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If there are 200 lions in the park, which is twice the number of leopards in the park, there are 200/2 = 100 leopards in the park.\nThe total population of lions and leopards in the park is 200 lions + 100 leopards = 300\nThe number of elephants in the park is 1/2 the total population of lions and leopards; thus, there are 300/2 = 150 elephants in the park.\nThere are a total of 150+300 = 450 animals in the park.\n#### 450"", ""original_answer"": 450, ""transformed_answer"": 400, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed solution, the 300/2 calculation in step 3 has been incorrectly changed to 100 instead of 150. Subsequently, step 4 inherits the error from step 3, modifying the formula of the total number of animals from 150+300 = 450 to 100+300 = 400. The preceding steps 1 and 2 remain unaffected, along with their descriptions and calculations. The transformed answer becomes 400 instead of the original 450."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:3a1e725f809242df,full,operator_error,"4 mat-weavers can weave 4 mats in 4 days. At the same rate, how many mats would be woven by 12 mat-weavers in 12 days?","One mat-weaver can weave 1 mat in 4 days because 4 / 4 = 1
