The total amount of money paid to the contracted employees in June is 30*$2400 = $72000
In the two months, the company paid a total of $72000+$84000 = $156000
#### 156000",Uses an incorrect employee count when calculating the first month's pay,"Paying 35 employees, the company paid 35*$2400= $84000 to all of its contract employees in May.",ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,employee,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""When hired, each employee is paid $15*40 = $600 per week.\nThe total earnings of a contracted employee in a month are 4 weeks * $600 per week = $2400\nPaying 40 employees, the company paid 40*$2400= $96000 to all of its contract employees in May.\nIn June, 1/4 of the employees' contracts expired, that is 1/4*40 = 10 employees.\nThe total number of employees whose contracts were valid in June was 40-10 = 30 employees.\nThe total amount of money paid to the contracted employees in June is 30*$2400 = $72000\nIn the two months, the company paid a total of $72000+$96000 = $168000\n#### 168000"", ""original_answer"": 168000.0, ""transformed_answer"": 156000.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references 40 in the question as 35 wrongly, and as a result calculates 35*$2400 = $84000 instead of 40*$2400 = $96000. This affects the final calculation where the total paid over two months is now $72000+$84000 = $156000 instead of $72000+$96000 = $168000. The number 35 erroneously used in this step does not occur in the question; however, for the purpose of this case transformation, it was assumed to be a referencing error. Please note that all other steps reference the original number 40 correctly, except for the step where the error is introduced."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:3a886ca6e66defee,full,calculation_error,"Factory x's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 75% of cases, whereas factory y's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 65% of cases. It is known that factory x supplies 70% of the total bulbs available. What is the chance that a purchased bulb will work for longer than 5000 hours?","The chance of getting a bulb from factory x is 70% because factory x supplies 70% of the total bulbs available.
The chance of getting a working bulb from factory x is 75% because factory x's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 75% of cases.
The chance of getting a bulb from factory y is 30% because 100% - 70% = 30%.
The chance of getting a working bulb from factory y is 65% because factory y's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 65% of cases.
The overall chance of getting a working bulb is 70% x 75% + 30% x 65% = 52.5% + 19.0% = 71.5%.
#### 71.5%",Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying and adding percentages,70% x 75% + 30% x 65% = 52.5% + 19.0% = 71.5%.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The chance of getting a bulb from factory x is 70% because factory x supplies 70% of the total bulbs available.\nThe chance of getting a working bulb from factory x is 75% because factory x's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 75% of cases.\nThe chance of getting a bulb from factory y is 30% because 100% - 70% = 30%.\nThe chance of getting a working bulb from factory y is 65% because factory y's bulbs work for over 5000 hours in 65% of cases.\nThe overall chance of getting a working bulb is 70% x 75% + 30% x 65% = 52.5% + 19.5% = 72%.\n#### 72%"", ""original_answer"": 72.0, ""transformed_answer"": 71.5, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""In this case, in step 4, the calculation of 30% x 65% is incorrectly transformed to 19.0% instead of 19.5%. This results in a change in the overall chance calculation in the final step to 71.5% instead of 72%, affecting only the last two steps while the previous steps remain unchanged."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:3a8b5926365d6a41,full,adding_irrelevant_information,A taxi company charges $1.85 for the first quarter of a mile and fifteen cents for each additional quarter of a mile. What is the maximum distance someone could travel with $4.90?,"Each additional quarter of a mile costs $0.15, and there is a service charge of $0.50 for radio dispatch, so (4.90 - 1.85 - 0.50) / 0.15 = 18.33
The maximum distance someone could travel is 18 * 0.25 = 4.5 miles
#### 4.5",Introduces an unsupported extra charge into the cost calculation,there is a service charge of $0.50 for radio dispatch,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Each additional quarter of a mile costs $0.15, so (4.90 - 1.85) / 0.15 = 20.33\nThe maximum distance someone could travel is 20 * 0.25 = 5 miles\n#### 5"", ""original_answer"": 5.0, ""transformed_answer"": 4.5, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <and there is a service charge of $0.50 for radio dispatch>, resulting in step 1 changing from (4.90 - 1.85) / 0.15 = 20.33 in the original_solution to (4.90 - 1.85 - 0.50) / 0.15 = 18.33 in the transformed_solution. The calculation of the maximum distance changes accordingly from 20 * 0.25 = 5 miles to 18 * 0.25 = 4.5 miles. The transformed_answer is thus 4.5 instead of the original 5. It should be noted that only one error of adding additional information in one step is considered, and the rest of the calculation process should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:3ac5b115afdec7dd,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"Over the past five years, on July 4th, the high temperature for Washington, DC has been: 90 degrees in 2020, 90 degrees in 2019, 90 degrees in 2018, 79 degrees in 2017 and 71 degrees in 2016. What is the average temperature for July 4th in Washington, DC over the past 5 years?","Over the past five years, the sum of the temperatures was 90+90+90+79+71=420
