#### 100",Subtracts the fixed charge incorrectly when isolating the variable,This simplifies to $0.25G = $25,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let G stand for the number of GB billed, so the total bill is $0.25G + $45 flat rate charge = $65 total bill.\nNow we will solve for G. $0.25G + $45 flat rate - $45 = $65 -$45. This simplifies to $0.25G = $20\n$0.25G/$0.25 = $20/$0.25\nG = 80 GB were charged on this bill.\n#### 80"", ""original_answer"": 80.0, ""transformed_answer"": 100.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 mistakenly references 20 as 25 from step 2 and changes $0.25G = $20 to $0.25G = $25. It should be noted that step 2 in the transformed_solution <Now we will solve for G. $0.25G + $45 flat rate - $45 = $65 -$45. This simplifies to $0.25G = $20> should be the same as the step 2 in the original_solution <Now we will solve for G. $0.25G + $45 flat rate - $45 = $65 -$45. This simplifies to $0.25G = $20> and calculates its result 20 correctly. And step 4 is affected by step 3 and changes $20/$0.25 to $25/$0.25 leading to a wrong result of 100 GB instead of 80 GB. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:3b0f3ac2563a2790,full,calculation_error,Leo has to write a 400-word story for his literature class. 10 words fit on each line of his notebook and 20 lines fit on each page. Lucas has filled one and a half pages. How many words does he have left to write?,"Half a page is 20 / 2 = 10 lines.
