eic,eic:3cb0e27acbb83f4a,full,referencing_context_value_error,"Mary, Jess, and Christina want to decorate a party room with balloons. Each person inflates balloons at different speeds, and they only have 30 minutes to inflate as many balloons as possible. Mary inflates 10 balloons per minute, Jess inflates 7 balloons per minute and Christina came 15 minutes late and was the slowest one inflating 4 balloons per minute. How many balloons can they inflate before running out of time?","Mary will inflate a total of 11 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 330 balloons
Jess will inflate a total of 7 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 210 balloons
Christina will inflate a total of 4 balloons/minute x 15 minutes = 60 balloons
Combining all balloons, they made 330 balloons + 210 balloons + 60 balloons = 600 balloons#### 600",Uses a rate different from the stated rate,Mary will inflate a total of 11 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 330 balloons,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,different,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Mary will inflate a total of 10 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 300 balloons\nJess will inflate a total of 7 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 210 balloons\nChristina will inflate a total of 4 balloons/minute x 15 minutes = 60 balloons\nCombining all balloons, they made 300 balloons + 210 balloons + 60 balloons = 570 balloons#### 570"", ""original_answer"": 570.0, ""transformed_answer"": 600.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 10 in the question as 11 wrongly, and calculates 11 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 330 balloons instead of 10 balloons/minute x 30 minutes = 300 balloons. Its subsequent related step, step 4, will be affected, calculating 330 balloons + 210 balloons + 60 balloons = 600 balloons instead of 300 balloons + 210 balloons + 60 balloons = 570 balloons."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:3cb85da96d307d41,full,counting_error,"Sheila works 8 hours per day on Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, and 6 hours per day on Tuesday and Thursday. She does not work on Saturday and Sunday. She earns $432 per week. How much does she earn in dollars per hour?","On Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, Sheila works a total of 8 * 2 = 16 hours
On Tuesday and Thursday, she works a total of 6 * 2 = 12 hours
In a week, she works a total of 16 + 12 = 28 hours
She earns $432 per week
So, she earns $432 / 28 = $15.43 per hour
#### 15.43",Miscounts how many times a daily amount applies,"On Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, Sheila works a total of 8 * 2 = 16 hours",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""On Monday, Wednesday, and Friday, Sheila works a total of 8 * 3 = 24 hours\nOn Tuesday and Thursday, she works a total of 6 * 2 = 12 hours\nIn a week, she works a total of 24 + 12 = 36 hours\nShe earns $432 per week\nSo, she earns $432 / 36 = $12 per hour\n#### 12"", ""original_answer"": 12.0, ""transformed_answer"": 15.43, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 erroneously counts Monday, Wednesday, and Friday as 2 days instead of 3 days, resulting in an 8 * 3=24 becoming 8 * 2=16. This affects the subsequent related step 3, changing the total number of hours worked from 24 + 12=36 to 16 + 12=28, and finally changing the calculation in step 5 from $432 / 36 = $12 to $432 / 28 = $15.43 per hour. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of counting error, and the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:3cceb43ebeffe5c6,full,calculation_error,"A manufacturer produces a certain men's athletic shoe in integer sizes from 8 to 17. For this particular shoe, each unit increase in size corresponds to a 1/5-inch increase in the length of the shoe. If the largest size of this shoe is 20% longer than the smallest size, how long, in inches, is the shoe in size 15?","The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17-8 = 9
The increase in length is 9 x (1/5) = 9/5 inches
The length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x
The length of size 17 is x + 9/5
So, 1.2x = x + 9/5
0.2x = 9/5
x = (9/5) / 0.2 = 9
The length of size 8 is 9 inches, and size 15 is 9 + 7/5 = 11.4 inches
#### 11.4",Makes an arithmetic error when adding a whole number and fraction,9 + 7/5 = 11.4 inches,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17-8 = 9\nThe increase in length is 9 x (1/5) = 9/5 inches\nThe length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x\nThe length of size 17 is x + 9/5\nSo, 1.2x = x + 9/5\n0.2x = 9/5\nx = (9/5) / 0.2 = 9\nThe length of size 8 is 9 inches, and size 15 is 9 + 7/5 = 10.4 inches\n#### 10.4"", ""original_answer"": 10.4, ""transformed_answer"": 11.4, ""wrong_step"": 8, ""explanation"": ""The error occurs at step 8 where the original addition of size 15's additional length should be 9 + (7 * (1/5)) = 9 + 7/5 = 10.4 inches. Instead, the transformed solution adds incorrectly to get 9 + 7/5 = 11.4 inches. The value in step 2 of the transformed_solution is correct, and all other steps use the correct values from the previous steps in their calculations. Only step 8's arithmetic is incorrect, while steps 1 to 7 are accurately transferred from the original_solution and lead to the correct intermediate results."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:3cd3e30850f9015b,full,operator_error,Three-quarters of the oil from a 4000-liter tank (that was initially full) was poured into a 20000-liter capacity tanker that already had 3000 liters of oil. How many more liters of oil would be needed to make the large tanker half-full?,"Three-quarters of oil from the initially full 4000-liter tank would be 4000*(3/4)= 3000 liters
