#### 5",Makes an arithmetic subtraction error when calculating the discounted price,So the smartphone from store B will only cost $130 - $13 = $120.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Store A has a $125 x 8/100 = $10 discount.\nSo the smartphone from store A will only cost $125 - $10 = $115.\nStore B has a $130 x 10/100 = $13 discount.\nSo the smartphone from store B will only cost $130 - $13 = $117.\nThus, store A's smartphone is $117 - $115 = $2 cheaper than that of store B.\n#### 2"", ""original_answer"": 2.0, ""transformed_answer"": 5.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed solution, the calculation in step 4 of the original solution is changed. The original correct calculation of $130 - $13 = $117 is improperly calculated as $130 - $13 = $120. This results in an incorrect final answer. The subsequent step 5 uses this incorrect price from store B ($120 instead of $117) to compute the difference, $120 - $115 = $5, leading to an incorrect transformed answer of $5 instead of the original answer of $2. Steps 1, 2, and 3 remain unchanged as they are not affected by the modification in step 4. The error is only introduced at step 4."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
