Total score for students who took the exam on the make-up date: 36 x 70% = 25.2
Total score for the entire class: 32.4 + 25.2 = 57.6
Average score for the entire class: 57.6 / 90 = 0.64
Average score for the entire class as a percentage: 64%
#### 64%",Uses an average score as the proportion of students in a group,Students who took the exam on the assigned day: 90 x 60% = 54,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,"score, students",True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Students who took the exam on the assigned day: 90 x 70% = 63\nStudents who took the exam on the make-up date: 90 - 63 = 27\nTotal score for students who took the exam on the assigned day: 63 x 60% = 37.8\nTotal score for students who took the exam on the make-up date: 27 x 70% = 18.9\nTotal score for the entire class: 37.8 + 18.9 = 56.7\nAverage score for the entire class: 56.7 / 90 = 0.63\nAverage score for the entire class as a percentage: 63%\n#### 63%"", ""original_answer"": ""63%"", ""transformed_answer"": ""64%"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 70% in the question as 60% wrongly, and calculates 90 * 60% = 54 instead of 90 * 70% = 63. Its subsequent related steps, step 2, 3, 4, and 5, will be affected. Step 2 changes from 90 - 63 = 27 to 90 - 54 = 36, step 3 changes from 63 x 60% = 37.8 to 54 x 60% = 32.4, step 4 changes from 27 x 70% = 18.9 to 36 x 70% = 25.2, and step 5 changes from 37.8 + 18.9 = 56.7 to 32.4 + 25.2 = 57.6. Step 6 and 7 then calculate the average score for the entire class based on the erroneous total score, resulting in an average score of 64%. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the step subsequent to the erroneously referenced step will be affected by the erroneous result but still be calculated correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:436082285bbd2f1d,full,unit_conversion_error,"A person crosses a 600 m long street in 5 minutes, what is his speed in km per hour?","First, convert 600 meters to kilometers: 600 m * 0.001 km/m = 0.6 km.
