#### 76",Adds an unprovided bonus before computing the average,Add all the marks including 5 extra credit points in biology: 76+65+82+67+85+5=380,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Add all the marks: 76+65+82+67+85=375\nDivide the total by the number of subjects: 375/5=75\n#### 75"", ""original_answer"": 75.0, ""transformed_answer"": 76.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <including 5 extra credit points in biology>, resulting in step 1 changing from 76+65+82+67+85=375 in the original_solution to 76+65+82+67+85+5=380 in the transformed_solution. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5096787d2d5a2583,full,counting_error,"September's temperature fluctuated severely in 1 week. They started off with 40 degrees on Sunday then hit 50 on Monday, 65 on Tuesday, 36 on Wednesday, 82 on Thursday, 72 on Friday and ended the week at 26 on Saturday. What was the average temperature for that week?","When you add up the temperature for the entire week, it comes to 40+50+65+36+82+72+26 = 371
These temperatures were over 6 days so the average temperature was 371/6 = 61.83 degrees
#### 61.83",Divides the total by the wrong number of observations,These temperatures were over 6 days so the average temperature was 371/6 = 61.83 degrees,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""When you add up the temperature for the entire week, it comes to 40+50+65+36+82+72+26 = 371\nThese temperatures were over 7 days so the average temperature was 371/7 =53 degrees\n#### 53"", ""original_answer"": 53.0, ""transformed_answer"": 61.83, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 mistakenly counts Sunday through Saturday as 6 days instead of 7 days, which leads to the transformation of <These temperatures were over 7 days so the average temperature was 371/7 =53 degrees> in the original_solution into <These temperatures were over 6 days so the average temperature was 371/6 = 61.83 degrees> in the transformed_solution. The miscounting changes the divisor from 7 to 6, which consequently alters the average temperature. It should be noted that only one counting error is introduced, while the summation of temperatures is correctly carried over from the original solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:50a0e7e168170454,full,calculation_error,"Fred had 236 dollars to spend on 6 books. After buying them, he had 14 dollars. On average, how much did each book cost?","Fred spent $236 - $14 = $222 on books.
