It also has a 6-2=4 inch height
Finally, it has a 4-2=2 inch depth
So the inner volume of one box is 2*(3+4+3+4)+2*(3*4)=40 cubic inches
So in total the inner volume of the 3 boxes is 3*40=120 cubic inches
#### 120",Uses a surface-area expression instead of multiplying all three dimensions for volume,So the inner volume of one box is 2*(3+4+3+4)+2*(3*4)=40 cubic inches,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The walls subtract 2*1=2 inches from each dimension\nSo each box has 5-2=3 inch width\nIt also has a 6-2=4 inch height\nFinally, it has a 4-2=2 inch depth\nSo the inner volume of one box is 4*3*2=24 cubic inches\nSo in total the inner volume of the 3 boxes is 3*24=72 cubic inches\n#### 72"", ""original_answer"": 72.0, ""transformed_answer"": 120.0, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 5 confuses the volume and surface area of a cuboid. The question requires that the volume of the cuboid to be solved be equal to the length multiplied by width multiplied by height, rather than 2*(width+height+width+height)+2*(length*width), which is equivalent to the surface area of a cuboid, resulting in 4*3*2=24 in the original_solution becoming 2*(3+4+3+4)+2*(3*4)=40 in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent step 6, changing from 3*24=72 to 3*40=120. Note that the language description of step 5 <So the inner volume of one box is> in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. It should also be noted that you need to only consider one step of confusing formula error, and the other calculation processes are still correct. In this example, only step 5 mistakenly uses the formula of cuboid volume, while the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:528581028ea581ec,full,missing_step,"There are 8 students. 4 of them are men and 4 of them are women. If 4 students are selected from the 8 students, what is the probability that the number of men is equal to that of women?","The number of ways to choose 2 men out of 4 is C(4,2) = 6
The number of ways to choose 2 women out of 4 is also C(4,2) = 6
So, the total number of favorable outcomes is 6 x 6 = 36
The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes, which is 36/C(8,4)
#### 36/70",,"The probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes, which is 36/C(8,4)
#### 36/70",label_conflict,ok,,0,True,True,False,,True,0,"{""original_solution"": ""The total number of ways to choose 4 students out of 8 is C(8,4) = 70\nThe number of ways to choose 2 men out of 4 is C(4,2) = 6\nThe number of ways to choose 2 women out of 4 is also C(4,2) = 6\nSo, the total number of favorable outcomes is 6 x 6 = 36\nThe probability is the number of favorable outcomes divided by the total number of outcomes, which is 36/70\n#### 18/35"", ""original_answer"": ""18/35"", ""transformed_answer"": ""36/70"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""This example removes step 1, which is the calculation of the total number of ways to choose 4 students out of 8. In the original solution, steps 2 and 3 calculate the number of ways to choose 2 men and 2 women respectively, which do not depend on the total number of choices directly, so they are not changed. However, step 4, which calculates the total number of favorable outcomes, and step 5, which calculates the probability, do depend on the total number of outcomes. Thus step 4 remains unchanged, but in step 5, the direct calculation of the total outcomes using C(8,4) has been replaced with the expression it stands for, so the solution incorrectly tries to divide 36 by the expression C(8,4) rather than its result, 70. This makes the wrong step 1 for referencing an expression instead of its result, converting the error forward into the transformed_solution and leading to a different answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""missing_step"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:52a5c49c90a9d093,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"Bob is tilling a plot of his garden. The plot is 110 feet wide by 120 feet long. His tiller digs a swath two feet wide, and he can till 1 foot of ground in about 2 seconds. How long will it take him to till this plot of land, in minutes?","If Bob goes along the side that's 120 feet long, he will till 110 / 2 = 55 rows.
