#### 264",Uses an incorrect conversion factor when converting seconds to minutes,"13,200 seconds is 13,200 / 50 = 264 minutes",ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,seconds,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If Bob goes along the side that's 120 feet long, he will till 110 / 2 = 55 rows.\nEach of these rows are 120 feet long, so he will push the tiller a total of 120 * 55 = 6,600 feet.\nHe tills 1 linear foot of ground every 2 seconds, so it will take him 2 * 6,600 = 13,200 seconds to till this plot\n13,200 seconds is 13,2000 / 60 = 220 minutes\n#### 220"", ""original_answer"": 220.0, ""transformed_answer"": 264.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references the number of minutes per hour as 50 instead of 60 from step 3 and changes 13,200 / 60 = 220 minutes to 13,200 / 50 = 264 minutes. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <He tills 1 linear foot of ground every 2 seconds, so it will take him 2 * 6,600 = 13,200 seconds to till this plot> should be the same as the step 3 in the original_solution <He tills 1 linear foot of ground every 2 seconds, so it will take him 2 * 6,600 = 13,200 seconds to till this plot> and calculates its result 13,200 correctly. The language and calculation for step 3 were not altered; only the division factor in step 4 was erroneously changed. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:53041ef03c3b0b81,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,jane and thomas are among the 9 people from which a committee of 4 people is to be selected. how many different possible committees of 4 people can be selected from these 9 people if at least one of either jane or thomas is to be selected?,"Total possible committees of 4 from 9 people = 9 choose 4 = 9! / (4! * (9-4)!) = 126
