eic,eic:538eac9c609c3fdf,full,unit_conversion_error,circular gears p and q start rotating at the same time at constant speeds. Gear p makes 10 revolutions per minute and gear q makes 40 revolutions per minute. How many seconds after the gears start rotating will gear q have made exactly 15 more revolutions than gear p?,"The key to solve the problem is that the difference in number of revolutions will be the same at all times.
In 1 minute, the difference in revolutions is 40 - 10 = 30.
So, after 15/30 = 0.5 minutes, or 0.5 * 50 = 25 seconds, gear q will have made exactly 15 more revolutions than gear p.
#### 25",Uses an incorrect conversion factor when converting minutes to seconds,0.5 * 50 = 25 seconds,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,seconds,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""The key to solve the problem is that the difference in number of revolutions will be the same at all times.\nIn 1 minute, the difference in revolutions is 40 - 10 = 30.\nSo, after 15/30 = 0.5 minutes, or 30 seconds, gear q will have made exactly 15 more revolutions than gear p.\n#### 30"", ""original_answer"": 30.0, ""transformed_answer"": 25.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 makes an incorrect unit conversion. While converting 0.5 minutes into seconds, the conversion wrongly uses 50 seconds equalling 1 minute instead of 60 seconds equalling 1 minute. Therefore, 0.5 minutes is converted to 25 seconds in the transformed_solution instead of the correct 30 seconds in the original_solution. This is the single step in the solution process that introduces the error, and it directly affects the final result, leading to a transformed_answer of 25 seconds instead of the original 30 seconds."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:53b1d0f59e5d2fcb,full,counting_error,"Terese thinks that running various distances throughout the week can make one healthy.  On Monday, she runs 4.2 miles;  Tuesday, 3.8 miles; Wednesday, 3.6 miles; and on Thursday, 4.4 miles.  Determine the average distance Terese runs on each of the days she runs.","The total distance Terese runs is 4.2 + 3.8 + 4.4 + 3.6 = 16 miles.
