#### 49.75",Divides the sum by the wrong number of values,The average of the prime numbers is 199/4 = 49.75.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The prime numbers between 30-50 are 31, 37, 41, 43, and 47.\nThe sum of the prime numbers is 31+37+41+43+47 = 199.\nThe average of the prime numbers is 199/5 = 39.8.\n#### 39.8"", ""original_answer"": 39.8, ""transformed_answer"": 49.75, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 erroneously counts the number of prime numbers as 4 instead of 5, changing the division from 199/5 to 199/4 and affecting the average calculation. The counting error does not affect the sum of the prime numbers determined in the earlier steps, and the sum is calculated correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
