Probability = 9/5 = 1.8
#### 1.8",Uses an incorrect denominator for the total number of selections,Total ways to select 4 from 6 = 5C4 = 5,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Total ways to select 4 from 6 = 6C4 = 15\nWays to select 2 women from 3 = 3C2 = 3\nWays to select 2 girls from 3 = 3C2 = 3\nTotal favorable outcomes = 3 * 3 = 9\nProbability = 9/15 = 3/5\n#### 3/5"", ""original_answer"": ""3/5"", ""transformed_answer"": ""1.8"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 6 total people in the question as 5 wrongly, and calculates 5C4=5 instead of 6C4=15. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 9/5=1.8 instead of 9/15=3/5 in step 5. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 2 and 3 still reference 3 correctly in the question when calculating 3C2=3."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5a990fda2da7ea6b,full,adding_irrelevant_information,Scout delivers groceries on the weekends. His base pay is $10.00 an hour. He also earns a $5.00 tip per customer that he delivers groceries to. On Saturday he worked 4 hours and delivered groceries to 5 people. Sunday he worked 5 hours and delivered groceries to 8 people. How much did he make over the weekend?,"He worked 4 hours on Saturday and 5 hours on Sunday for a total of 4+5 = 9 hours
His base pay is $10.00 an hour and he worked 9 hours for a total of 10*9 = $90.00
He delivered groceries to 5 people on Saturday and 8 people on Sunday for a total of 5+8 = 13 deliveries
Because he received a special promotion bonus of $10.00 for exceeding 10 deliveries in a weekend, he makes $5.00 per delivery and he delivered to 13 people so he made 5*13 + 10 = $75.00
His base pay is $90.00 and he made $75.00 in tips and bonuses for a total of 90+75 = $165.00
#### 165",Adds an unsupported bonus to the calculation,Because he received a special promotion bonus of $10.00 for exceeding 10 deliveries in a weekend,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""He worked 4 hours on Saturday and 5 hours on Sunday for a total of 4+5 = 9 hours\nHis base pay is $10.00 an hour and he worked 9 hours for a total of 10*9 = $90.00\nHe delivered groceries to 5 people on Saturday and 8 people on Sunday for a total of 5+8 = 13 deliveries\nHe makes $5.00 per delivery and he delivered to 13 people so he made 5*13 = $65.00\nHis base pay is $90.00 and he made $65.00 in tips for a total of 90+65 = $155.00\n#### 155"", ""original_answer"": 155.0, ""transformed_answer"": 165.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because he received a special promotion bonus of $10.00 for exceeding 10 deliveries in a weekend>, resulting in step 4 changing from 5*13 = $65.00 in the original_solution to 5*13 + 10 = $75.00 in the transformed_solution. The calculation of the tip is now affected by this added irrelevant information. The final total pay has also been accordingly changed from $155.00 to $165.00 in the transformed_answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:5acab2851c715a08,full,referencing_context_value_error,"For homework, Brooke has 15 math problems, 6 social studies problems, and 10 science problems. He can answer each math problem for 2 minutes while answering each social studies problem takes him 30 seconds. If he can answer each science problem in 1.5 minutes, how long will it take Brooke to answer all his homework?","Brooke will take 15 x 2 = 30 minutes to answer all math problems.
It will take him 6 x 20 seconds = 120 seconds to answer all social studies problems.
In minutes, this is equal to 120/60 = 2 minutes.
It will take him 10 x 1.5 minutes = 15 minutes to answer all science problems.
Therefore, Brooke will take 30 + 2 + 15 = 47 minutes to finish his homework.
#### 47",Uses an incorrect per-item time in the multiplication,It will take him 6 x 20 seconds = 120 seconds to answer all social studies problems.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Brooke will take 15 x 2 = 30 minutes to answer all math problems.\nIt will take him 6 x 30 seconds = 180 seconds to answer all social studies problems.\nIn minutes, this is equal to 180/60 = 3 minutes.\nIt will take him 10 x 1.5 minutes = 15 minutes to answer all science problems.\nTherefore, Brooke will take 30 + 3 + 15 = 48 minutes to finish his homework.\n#### 48"", ""original_answer"": 48.0, ""transformed_answer"": 47.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 references 30 seconds in the question as 20 seconds wrongly, and calculates 6 x 20 seconds = 120 seconds instead of 6 x 30 seconds = 180 seconds. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 120/60 = 2 minutes instead of 180/60 = 3 minutes in step 3. The final step will also be affected, calculating 30 + 2 + 15 = 47 minutes instead of 30 + 3 + 15 = 48 minutes in step 5. Please note that you should only consider one error, so all other steps that reference 30 seconds still do so correctly except for the step referenced incorrectly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:5ae371629edc8eba,full,confusing_formula_error,"a larger cube has 8 cubic inch as a volume and in the cube there are 8 smaller cubes such that their volume is 1 cubic inch. What is the difference between the surface areas’ sum of the 8 smaller cubes and the surface area of the larger cube, in square inch?","The side length of the larger cube is 2 inches (cubic root of 8).
The volume of the larger cube is 2*2*2=8 cubic inches.
The side length of the smaller cube is 1 inch (cubic root of 1).
The surface area of one smaller cube is 1+1+1+1+1+1=6 square inches.
The sum of the surface areas of the 8 smaller cubes is 8*6=48 square inches.
The difference between the surface areas’ sum of the 8 smaller cubes and the volume of the larger cube is 48-8=40 square inches.
#### 40",Subtracts the larger cube’s volume instead of its surface area,The difference between the surface areas’ sum of the 8 smaller cubes and the volume of the larger cube is 48-8=40 square inches.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"cube, larger, surface",True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The side length of the larger cube is 2 inches (cubic root of 8).\nThe surface area of the larger cube is 6*2*2=24 square inches.\nThe side length of the smaller cube is 1 inch (cubic root of 1).\nThe surface area of one smaller cube is 6*1*1=6 square inches.\nThe sum of the surface areas of the 8 smaller cubes is 8*6=48 square inches.\nThe difference between the surface areas’ sum of the 8 smaller cubes and the surface area of the larger cube is 48-24=24 square inches.\n#### 24"", ""original_answer"": 24.0, ""transformed_answer"": 40.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 4 confuses the surface area and the edge length of the cube. The question requires that the surface area of the cube to be solved be equal to 6 times the square of the side length, but step 4 uses the edge length sum formula, which is equivalent to the sum of all edges, resulting in 6*1*1=6 in the original_solution being changed to 1+1+1+1+1+1=6 in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent related step 5, which calculates the sum of the surface areas of the 8 smaller cubes correctly but creates an incorrect understanding that the result should be compared with the volume of the larger cube in step 6. Note that the language description of step 4 < The surface area of one smaller cube is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. The transformation is made without modifying any words in the language description and ensures the correct use of formulas in other steps. Furthermore, the transformed_answer is different from the original_answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5af642571c226faf,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"Sally received the following scores on her math quizzes: 50, 80, 80, 60, 40, 90, 100, 70, and 60. Find her mean score.","Sally's total score is 50 + 80 + 80 + 60 + 40 + 90 + 100 + 70 + 60 = 630.
Her mean score is 630 / 8/quizzes = 78.75/quiz.
#### 78.75",Uses the wrong number of values when computing the mean,Her mean score is 630 / 8/quizzes = 78.75/quiz.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Sally's total score is 50 + 80 + 80 + 60 + 40 + 90 + 100 + 70 + 60 = 630.\nHer mean score is 630 / 9/quizzes = 70/quiz.\n#### 70"", ""original_answer"": 70.0, ""transformed_answer"": 78.75, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 mistakenly references 9 quizzes as 8 from step 1 and changes 630 / 9/quizzes = 70/quiz to 630 / 8/quizzes = 78.75/quiz. It should be noted that step 1 in the transformed_solution <Sally's total score is 50 + 80 + 80 + 60 + 40 + 90 + 100 + 70 + 60 = 630.> should be the same as the step 1 in the original_solution <Sally's total score is 50 + 80 + 80 + 60 + 40 + 90 + 100 + 70 + 60 = 630.> and calculates its result 630 correctly. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct, and the related previous step remains unchanged while only the erroneous reference is adjusted in the following step."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:5b7af28f5d91de20,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,Amy had two eyeshadow palettes with four colors each and three makeup sets that came with six eyeshadow colors each. Her sister steals one of the palettes. Amy uses up half of the colors from one makeup set. How many eyeshadow colors does she have left?,"Amy had 2 * 4 + 3 * 6 = 8 + 18 = 26 eyeshadow colors to start.
Her sister stole one palette of 4 colors, leaving Amy with 26 - 4 = 22 colors.
Half the colors from one makeup set are 6 / 2 = 3 colors.
Thus, Amy has 20 - 3 = 17 eyeshadow colors left.
#### 17",Subtracts from an incorrect intermediate total,"Thus, Amy has 20 - 3 = 17 eyeshadow colors left.",ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,from,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Amy had 2 * 4 + 3 * 6 = 8 + 18 = 26 eyeshadow colors to start.\nHer sister stole one palette of 4 colors, leaving Amy with 26 - 4 = 22 colors.\nHalf the colors from one makeup set are 6 / 2 = 3 colors.\nThus, Amy has 22 - 3 = 19 eyeshadow colors left.\n#### 19"", ""original_answer"": 19.0, ""transformed_answer"": 17.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references 22 as 20 from step 3 and changes 22 - 3 = 19 to 20 - 3 = 17. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <Half the colors from one makeup set are 6 / 2 = 3 colors.> should be the same as the step 3 in the original_solution <Half the colors from one makeup set are 6 / 2 = 3 colors.> and calculates its result 3 correctly. There is only one error to consider, which is the reference to the previous step, so all other steps should still be consistent and correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
