#### 320",Adds an unstated expense to the calculation,Derek also has to pay a locker fee of 40 dollars,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""Amount spent on textbooks is 960/2 = 480 dollars.\nAmount spent on school supplies is 480/4 = 120 dollars.\nAmount Derek has left 960-480-120 = 360 dollars.\n#### 360"", ""original_answer"": 360.0, ""transformed_answer"": 320.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 integrates additional information not mentioned in the question statement <Derek also has to pay a locker fee of 40 dollars>, directly affecting the final amount Derek has left. This additional expense leads to a change, where the step 3 calculation changes from 960-480-120 = 360 dollars in the original_solution to 960-480-120-40 = 320 dollars in the transformed_solution. The extra cost is not separated into its own step but is included in the existing calculation process."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:5bbebc4db6fb6dc6,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"Gabriel is looking at her marble sets. She sees that in the first set 10% of her marbles are broken. In the second set, 20% of the marbles are broken. The first set contains 50 marbles. The second set contains 60. How many marbles are broken in total?","In the first set there are 5 broken marbles because 50 x .1 = 5
