#### 15",Uses an incorrect intermediate result when computing the total,In the second set there are 10 broken marbles because 60 x .2 = 12,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""In the first set there are 5 broken marbles because 50 x .1 = 5\nIn the second set there are 12 broken marbles because 60 x .2 = 12\nThere are 17 broken marbles in total because 5 + 12 = 17\n#### 17"", ""original_answer"": 17.0, ""transformed_answer"": 15.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 mistakenly references 12 as 10 from step 1 and changes 60 x .2 = 12 to 60 x .2 = 10. It should be noted that step 1 in the transformed_solution <In the first set there are 5 broken marbles because 50 x .1 = 5> should be the same as the step 1 in the original_solution <In the first set there are 5 broken marbles because 50 x .1 = 5> and calculates its result 5 correctly. Step 3, as the subsequent related step of the wrong step 2, is now 5 + 10 = 15. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct, aside from the error introduced in step 2."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:5c239e7d139484b3,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"On a certain test, Bill scored 20 more points than John, but half as many points as Sue. If the sum of the scores of the 3 students was 160 points, how many points did Bill receive?","Let x be the number of points John scored.
