x = 17.5.
Bill scored 17.5 + 20 = 37.5 points.
#### 37.5",Adds an unstated bonus to the total,"Because they received a group bonus for teamwork of 10 points each, their total score including the bonus is",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the number of points John scored.\nBill scored x + 20 points.\nSue scored 2*(x+20) = 2x + 40 points.\nTheir total score is x + (x+20) + (2x+40) = 160.\n4x + 60 = 160.\n4x = 100.\nx = 25.\nBill scored 25 + 20 = 45 points.\n#### 45"", ""original_answer"": 45.0, ""transformed_answer"": 37.5, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because they received a group bonus for teamwork of 10 points each>, resulting in step 4 changing from x + (x+20) + (2x+40) = 160 to x + (x+20) + (2x+40) + 3*10 = 160 in the transformed_solution. This alters the equation to 4x + 90 = 160 instead of 4x + 60 = 160, and as a result, the value of x changes and thus the score of Bill changes to 37.5 points from the original 45 points. This is the first and only introduced error in the transformed_solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5c2af6f0aebd1578,full,missing_step,"a, b and c enter into partnership. a invests 3 times as much as b and b invests two-third of what c invests. at the end of the year, the profit earned is rs. 5500. what is the share of b?","Let the capital invested by c be x
Then the capital invested by b = 2/3*x
