#### 60",Uses the wrong percentage for a decrease,The revenues in 1999 were 0.6x because they fell by 40 percent.,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the revenues in 1998.\nThe profits in 1998 were 0.1x.\nThe revenues in 1999 were 0.7x because they fell by 30 percent.\nThe profits in 1999 were 0.1 * 0.7x = 0.07x.\nThe profits in 1999 were 70 percent of the profits in 1998 because (0.07x / 0.1x) * 100 = 70\n#### 70"", ""original_answer"": 70.0, ""transformed_answer"": 60.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references the percent decrease in revenues as 40 percent instead of 30 percent, and calculates the revenues in 1999 as 0.6x instead of 0.7x. This wrong percentage directly affects the calculation of the profits for 1999 and the final percentage comparison between profits of 1999 and 1998. The correct calculation using 30 percent should yield 70 percent, but because of the incorrect percentage used in step 3, the transformed solution yields 60 percent. Since this is the only error, subsequent steps reflect the results of the change correctly despite the erroneous input in step 3. All other steps that reference the original numbers from the question do so correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5c977d00b3af8507,full,referencing_context_value_error,"4 mat-weavers can weave 4 mats in 4 days. At the same rate, how many mats would be woven by 12 mat-weavers in 12 days?","One mat-weaver can weave 1 mat in 4 days because 4 / 4 = 1
