#### 24 seconds",Uses an incorrect value from a previous calculation,Time = Distance / Speed = 480 m / 20 m/s = 24 s,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,4,"{""original_solution"": ""First, convert the speed from km/hr to m/s: 72 km/hr x (1000 m/km) x (1 hr/3600 s) = 20 m/s\nTotal distance to cover = length of the train + length of the bridge = 360 m + 140 m = 500 m\nTime = Distance / Speed = 500 m / 20 m/s = 25 s\n#### 25 seconds"", ""original_answer"": 25.0, ""transformed_answer"": 24.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 mistakenly references the correct total distance of 500 m as 480 m from step 2 and changes the calculation from 500 m / 20 m/s = 25 s to 480 m / 20 m/s = 24 s. It should be noted that step 2 in the transformed_solution <Total distance to cover = length of the train + length of the bridge = 360 m + 140 m = 500 m> should be the same as step 2 in the original_solution and calculates its result 500 m correctly. The transformed_solution incorrectly uses 480 m for the distance in the calculation of step 3, leading to a transformed_answer of 24 seconds instead of the original 25 seconds. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct except for the error introduced in step 3."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:5def6f9d53f3581e,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"Olivia gave William 10 napkins. Amelia also gives William twice the number of napkins Olivia gave him. If William had 15 napkins before, how many napkins does he have now?","After Olivia gave William 10 napkins and an extra 5 she found in her bag, he ends up with 15+10+5= 30 napkins.
