#### 1520",Miscounts the number of working days in the week,The total number of days the workers work per week is 3 days,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total number of toys produced per week is 4560\nThe total number of days the workers work per week is 4 days\nThe number of toys produced each day is 4560 / 4 = 1140 toys\n#### 1140"", ""original_answer"": 1140.0, ""transformed_answer"": 1520.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 erroneously counts the number of days the workers work per week as 3 days instead of 4 days, resulting in the equation 4560 / 4 = 1140 becoming 4560 / 3 = 1520 in the transformed_solution. It should be noted that only one counting error is considered, and the division calculation process is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:61ea3d8617a65c02,full,calculation_error,"in some quantity of ghee , 60 % of pure ghee and 40 % of is vanaspati . if 10 kg of pure ghee is added , then the strength of vanaspati ghee becomes 20 % . the original quantity was ?","Let the original quantity of ghee be x kg.
