Total amount of ghee = x
After adding 10 kg of pure ghee, the total amount of ghee becomes (x+10)
0.4x / (x+10) = 20%
0.4x = 0.2(x+10)
0.4x = 0.2x + 4
0.2x = 4
x = 20
The original quantity of ghee was 20 kg.
#### 20",,"0.4x = 0.2(x+10)
0.4x = 0.2x + 4
0.2x = 4
x = 20",label_conflict,ok,,0,True,True,False,,True,0,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the original quantity of ghee be x kg.\nAmount of pure ghee = 0.6x\nAmount of vanaspati ghee = 0.4x\nTotal amount of ghee = x\nAfter adding 10 kg of pure ghee, the total amount of ghee becomes (x+10)\n0.4x / (x+10) = 20%\n0.4x = 0.2(x+10)\n0.4x = 0.2x + 2\n0.2x = 2\nx = 10\nThe original quantity of ghee was 10 kg.\n#### 10"", ""original_answer"": 10.0, ""transformed_answer"": 20.0, ""wrong_step"": 8, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the wrong calculation is introduced at step 8, where the term \""0.2x + 2\"" is incorrectly changed to \""0.2x + 4\"". This error is then inherited by the following steps. Step 9 changes the subtraction result to \""0.2x = 4\"", and step 10 gives us the incorrect answer \""x = 20\"" instead of the correct \""x = 10\"". Only this single error has been made, and it propagates through to the final answer, resulting in a transformed answer of 20 kg instead of the correct original answer of 10 kg."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:6238b12783716665,full,missing_step,"A train crosses a platform of 250 m in 20 sec, the same train crosses another platform of length 640 m in 40 sec. Then find the length of the train?","Let the length of the train be x
