Because another friend, Alex, joined them and caught 10 pieces of candy, all together, Tabitha caught 22 pieces, Stan had 13, Julie had 11, Carlos had 26, and Alex had 10, so there were a total of 22+13+11+26+10 = 82 pieces of candy
#### 82",Adds an unmentioned quantity to the total,"Because another friend, Alex, joined them and caught 10 pieces of candy",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""Julie caught half the amount of Tabitha's 22 pieces so 22/2 = 11 pieces of candy caught by Julie\nCarlos caught twice the amount of candy as Stan's 13 pieces so 2 * 13 = 26 pieces of candy caught by Carlos\nAll together, Tabitha caught 22 pieces, Stan had 13, Julie had 11 and Carlos had 26, so there were a total of 22+13+11+26 = 72 pieces of candy\n#### 72"", ""original_answer"": 72.0, ""transformed_answer"": 82.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because another friend, Alex, joined them and caught 10 pieces of candy>, resulting in step 3 changing from 22+13+11+26 = 72 pieces of candy in the original_solution to 22+13+11+26+10 = 82 pieces of candy in the transformed_solution. The additional information led to a change in the final count of pieces of candy, altering the original_answer from 72 to the transformed_answer 82."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:64c8919806a27457,full,operator_error,"A conference center has six rooms. Each room can hold up to 80 people. Today, the conference center is only 2/3 full. How many people are in the conference center?","The conference center can hold up to 80 x 6 = 480 people.
Today, there are 480 - 2/3 = 479.3333 people in the conference center.
#### 479.3333",Subtracts a fraction from a total instead of multiplying by that fraction,"Today, there are 480 - 2/3 = 479.3333 people in the conference center.",ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The conference center can hold up to 80 x 6 = 480 people.\nToday, there are 480 x 2/3 = 320 people in the conference center.\n#### 320"", ""original_answer"": 320.0, ""transformed_answer"": 479.3333, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""This example converts the multiplication in step 2 into subtraction, changing 480 x 2/3 = 320 to 480 - 2/3 = 479.3333 by changing x to -. Its subsequent step 2 related to it inherits its result, the transformed answer becomes 479.3333. It should be noted that step 2 only changes the operator of the formula, but still correctly calculates its result. Step 2 only inherits the result of step 1, but its calculation is correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:64cf3492f77e118d,full,confusing_formula_error,"Bob is building a garden on his land, and he wants it to be fenced in to keep out varmints. The garden is a rectangular plot 225 feet long by 125 feet wide. He also wants to have a small 3-foot wide gate to walk through and a larger 10-foot wide gate to move his gardening equipment through. How much fencing is Bob going to need to fence in his garden, taking into account the two gates?","The area of the garden is 225 * 125 = 28125 square feet.
Minus the two gates, he will need at least 28125 - 3 - 10 = 28112 feet of fencing.
#### 28112",Uses area instead of perimeter when calculating fencing,The area of the garden is 225 * 125 = 28125 square feet.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,fencing,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The perimeter of the garden is 2 * 225 + 2 * 125 = 450 + 250 = 700 feet.\nMinus the two gates, he will need at least 700 - 3 - 10 = 687 feet of fencing.\n#### 687"", ""original_answer"": 687.0, ""transformed_answer"": 28112.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 confuses the perimeter of rectangle with the area of rectangle. The question requires that the perimeter of the rectangle to be solved be equal to 2 times the length plus 2 times the width, rather than the length multiplied by width, which is equivalent to the area of the rectangle, resulting in 2 * 225 + 2 * 125 = 700 in the original_solution being changed to 225 * 125 = 28125 in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent step 2, changing from 700 - 3 - 10 = 687 to 28125 - 3 - 10 = 28112. Note that the language description of step 1 < The perimeter of the garden is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. It should be also noted that you need to only consider one step of confusing formula error, and the other calculation processes are still correct. In this example, only step 1 mistakenly uses the formula for the area of rectangle, while the following subtraction in step 2 is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:64d815278b269a46,full,counting_error,"every day daniel drives 100 miles back from work. on sunday, daniel drove all the way back from work at a constant speed of x miles per hour. on monday, daniel drove the first 32 miles back from work at (2x) miles per hour, and the rest of the way at (x/2) miles per hour. the time it took daniel to drive back from work on monday is longer than the time it took him to drive back from work on sunday by what percent?","On Sunday, the time it takes to drive 100 miles is 100 / x
On Monday, the time it takes to drive the first 32 miles at 2x mph is 32 / (2 * x) and the time it takes to drive the remaining 68 miles at x / 2 mph is 68 / (x / 2)
The total time on Monday is 32 / (2 * x) + 68 / (x / 2) = 16 / x + 136 / x = 152 / x
The total time on Sunday is 100 / x
The difference in time is 152 / x - 100 / x = 52 / x
To find the percentage increase, we take the difference (52 / x) and incorrectly divide by half the original time (50 / x), then multiply by 100 to get the percentage increase
(52 / 50) * 100 = 104%
#### 104%",Divides the change by half the original amount when calculating percentage increase,incorrectly divide by half the original time (50 / x),ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""On Sunday, the time it takes to drive 100 miles is 100 / x\nOn Monday, the time it takes to drive the first 32 miles at 2x mph is 32 / (2 * x) and the time it takes to drive the remaining 68 miles at x / 2 mph is 68 / (x / 2)\nThe total time on Monday is 32 / (2 * x) + 68 / (x / 2) = 16 / x + 136 / x = 152 / x\nThe total time on Sunday is 100 / x\nThe difference in time is 152 / x - 100 / x = 52 / x\nTo find the percentage increase, we take the difference (52 / x) and divide by the original time (100 / x), then multiply by 100 to get the percentage increase\n(52 / 100) * 100 = 52%\n#### 52%"", ""original_answer"": 52.0, ""transformed_answer"": 104.0, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed solution, the error occurs in step 5 where the original time is mistakenly divided by half its value, 50/x, instead of the correct value, 100/x. This results in an incorrect percentage increase calculation, with the difference (52/x) being divided by (50/x) instead of (100/x), leading to (52/50)*100 = 104% instead of the correct answer 52%."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
