#### 38.4",Uses an incorrect number of minutes in an hour for conversion,There are 50 minutes in an hour.,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Each picture will take 2 minutes to process. 2 x 960 = 1,920 minutes\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour. To find the hours, divide the minutes by 60. 1,920 / 60 = 32 hours\n#### 32"", ""original_answer"": 32.0, ""transformed_answer"": 38.4, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 hour is wrongly stated as having 50 minutes instead of the correct 60 minutes, resulting in 1,920 minutes being divided by 50 instead of 60. Thus, 1,920 / 60 = 32 hours in the original_solution changes to 1,920 / 50 = 38.4 hours in the transformed_solution. The wrong step only affects the unit conversion and subsequent division step; the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:6554b3905dde86f1,full,unit_conversion_error,"If Tina is driving at 55 miles per hour and is currently 7.5 miles behind Loe, who is driving at 40 miles per hour in the same direction, then in how many minutes will Tina be 15 miles ahead of Loe?","Tina is gaining on Loe at a rate of 55 - 40 = 15 miles per hour.
