#### 70",Uses an incorrect value instead of the previously calculated distance,Time = Distance / Speed = 350 m / 5 m/s = 70 s,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Convert the speed of the train from km/hr to m/s: 27 km/hr * (1000 m / 1 km) * (1 hr / 3600 s) = 7.5 m/s\nConvert the speed of the jogger from km/hr to m/s: 9 km/hr * (1000 m / 1 km) * (1 hr / 3600 s) = 2.5 m/s\nCalculate the relative speed of the train to the jogger: 7.5 m/s - 2.5 m/s = 5 m/s\nCalculate the distance the train needs to cover to pass the jogger: 240 m + 120 m = 360 m\nTime = Distance / Speed = 360 m / 5 m/s = 72 s\n#### 72"", ""original_answer"": 72.0, ""transformed_answer"": 70.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references 360 as 350 from step 3 and changes 360 m / 5 m/s = 72 s to 350 m / 5 m/s = 70 s. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <Calculate the distance the train needs to cover to pass the jogger: 240 m + 120 m = 360 m> should be the same as the step 3 in the original_solution <Calculate the distance the train needs to cover to pass the jogger: 240 m + 120 m = 360 m> and calculates its result 360 correctly. Step 5 as the subsequent step related to step 4, is affected by step 4 and changes the division from 360/5 to 350/5 resulting in a calculation of 70 seconds instead of 72 seconds. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all other steps is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
