#### 180",Adds an unstated extra time to the calculation,Because Carlos has to do an additional 15 minutes of prep work,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""First multiply the number of loads by the time per load to find the washing time: 2 loads * 45 minutes/load = 90 minutes\nThen add that time to the drying time to find the total laundry time: 90 minutes + 75 minutes = 165 minutes\n#### 165"", ""original_answer"": 165.0, ""transformed_answer"": 180.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because Carlos has to do an additional 15 minutes of prep work before starting the wash cycles>, resulting in step 2 changing from 90 minutes + 75 minutes = 165 minutes in the original_solution to 90 minutes + 15 minutes = 105 minutes and then 105 minutes + 75 minutes = 180 minutes in the transformed_solution. The final result is affected by this added piece of information, which changes the transformed_answer to 180 minutes compared to the original_answer of 165 minutes."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:6817f551e6d0cb38,full,calculation_error,"a straight line in the xy-plane has a slope of 4 and a y-intercept of 4. On this line, what is the x-coordinate of the point whose y-coordinate is 800?","The equation of the line is y = 4x + 4
