eic,eic:6cb2077e09295049,full,confusing_formula_error,"Jerry needs to shingle 3 roofs. Each roof is made of two slanted rectangular sides measuring 20 feet by 40 feet. If he needs 8 shingles to cover one square foot of roof, how many shingles does he need total?","First find the perimeter of one side of a roof: 20 feet + 40 feet + 20 feet + 40 feet = 120 feet
Then multiply that number by 2 to find the total area of both sides of the roof: 120 feet/side * 2 sides = 240 feet
