eic,eic:6d943eaca757d3dc,full,referencing_context_value_error,An alloy of copper and zinc contains copper and zinc in the ratio 5 : 3. Another alloy of copper and zinc contains copper and zinc in the ratio 1 : 7. In what ratio should the two alloys be mixed so that the resultant alloy contains equal proportions of copper and zinc?,"Let the first alloy be mixed in the ratio 5x and 3x and the second alloy be mixed in the ratio 1y and 7y.
