#### 42",Uses an incorrect original amount when calculating the discount,The dress was $60 and 30% off so 60*.30 = $18 discount price,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The dress was $50 and 30% off so 50*.30 = $15 discount price\nThe dress cost $50 minus $15 (30% off discount) so 50-15 = $35\n#### 35"", ""original_answer"": 35.0, ""transformed_answer"": 42.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 50 in the question as 60 wrongly, and calculates 60*.30=$18 instead of 50*.30=$15. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 60-18=$42 instead of 50-15=$35 in step 2. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 2 still references the correct 30% discount from the question."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:708a0251b13b2d02,full,referencing_context_value_error,"the length of rectangle is thrice its breadth and its perimeter is 88 m , find the area of the rectangle ?","Let the breadth be x.
The length is 3x.
Perimeter = 2(length + breadth)
88 = 2(3x + x)
88 = 2(4x)
88 = 2*6x
x = 7.33 (approximately)
Length = 3*7.33 = 22 (approximately)
Breadth = 7.33
Area = length x breadth = 22 * 7.33 = 161.26 (approximately)
#### 161.26",Makes an arithmetic error when simplifying the perimeter equation,"88 = 2(4x)
88 = 2*6x",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the breadth be x.\nThe length is 3x.\nPerimeter = 2(length + breadth)\n88 = 2(3x + x)\n88 = 2(4x)\n88 = 8x\nx = 11\nLength = 33\nBreadth = 11\nArea = length x breadth = 33 x 11 = 363\n#### 363"", ""original_answer"": 363.0, ""transformed_answer"": 161.26, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Step 5 references the relationship between length and breadth (3x+x) incorrectly as 2*6x instead of 2*4x. Its subsequent related step is affected, calculating 88=2*6x instead of 88=2*4x and thus wrongfully obtaining x=7.33 instead of x=11. Length is then wrongly calculated as 3*7.33=22 instead of 3*11=33, and breadth remains as incorrectly calculated 7.33 instead of 11. Finally, the area calculation inherits these errors, yielding 22*7.33=161.26 instead of 33*11=363. All other numbers in the problem are referenced correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:708ffa5ee77a6d67,full,calculation_error,"A towel, when bleached, lost 20% of its length and 20% of its breadth. What is the percentage decrease in area?","The area of the towel is decreased by 44% because 20% + 20% + (20% x 20%) = 44%
