#### 140",Uses the wrong conversion factor from hours to minutes,2.8 hours * 50 minutes per hour = 140 minutes.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,from,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the time taken to drive from a-ville to b-town be x hours.\nThen the time taken to drive from b-town to a-ville = 5 - x hours.\nDistance = Speed × Time\n110x = 140(5 - x)\n110x = 700 - 140x\n250x = 700\nx = 2.8 hours\nTo convert hours to minutes, multiply by 60: 2.8 hours * 60 minutes per hour = 168 minutes.\n#### 168"", ""original_answer"": 168.0, ""transformed_answer"": 140.0, ""wrong_step"": 8, ""explanation"": ""In step 8, the unit conversion error occurs by wrongly converting 1 hour to 50 minutes instead of 60 minutes, thus leading to an incorrect transformation from \""2.8 hours * 60 minutes per hour = 168 minutes\"" in the original_solution to \""2.8 hours * 50 minutes per hour = 140 minutes\"" in the transformed_solution. This is the only error introduced into the solution process, and it directly affects the final answer without changing any of the previous or unrelated steps."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
