eic,eic:740e85c9f1284fae,full,confusing_formula_error,"The area of a forest is three times the area of the square-shaped street. If the street has a length of 100 meters on one side and the number of trees per square meter in the forest is 4, calculate the total number of trees in the forest.","Since the perimeter of a square is all sides added, the perimeter of the square-shaped street is 100+100+100+100 = 400 meters.
