The area of the newly formed rectangle is 32+32=64 cm^2
So, the length of the new rectangle is 8 and its width is 8 (the area being taken as the side length in error)
The perimeter of the new rectangle is 2*(8+8)=32 cm
#### 32",Confuses perimeter calculation with area calculation,The area of the square is 8+8+8+8=32 cm^2,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,with,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The area of the square is 8*8=64 cm^2\nThe area of the original rectangle is 8*4=32 cm^2\nThe area of the newly formed rectangle is 64+32=96 cm^2\nSo, the length of the new rectangle is 8 and its width is 12 (8+4)\nThe perimeter of the new rectangle is 2*(8+12)=40 cm\n#### 40"", ""original_answer"": 40.0, ""transformed_answer"": 32.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""In step 1, the original_solution used the correct formula for the area of a square (side length squared), but the transformed_solution mistakenly uses the formula for the perimeter of a square (adding up all side lengths), which is 8+8+8+8=32 cm^2. This change affects the subsequent step 3, changing from 64+32=96 cm^2 to 32+32=64 cm^2. In the last step, the length of the newly formed rectangle remains at 8 cm, but the width is incorrectly taken as 8 cm from the erroneous area calculation (treating the area from step 3 as the side length), and thus the perimeter calculation changes from 2*(8+12)=40 cm to 2*(8+8)=32 cm."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:773bdf2864cb8c19,full,missing_step,fresh grapes contain 85 % water by weight and raisins obtained by drying fresh grapes contain 25 % water by weight . how many kgs of fresh grapes are needed to get 20 kgs of raisins ?," Let x be the weight of fresh grapes needed to get 20 kgs of raisins
