#### 25",Adds an unjustified quantity to the correct equation,4x + 6 + 8 = 102 because there was a mistake in the original sum calculation.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the first number.\nThe sum of the four consecutive numbers is x + (x+1) + (x+2) + (x+3) = 4x + 6.\n4x + 6 = 102.\n4x = 96.\nx = 24.\nThe greatest number is x + 3 = 24 + 3 = 27.\n#### 27"", ""original_answer"": 27.0, ""transformed_answer"": 25.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <because there was a mistake in the original sum calculation>, resulting in step 3 changing from 4x + 6 = 102 in the original_solution to 4x + 6 + 8 = 102 in the transformed_solution. This incorrect addition of 8 erroneously increases the sum, which alters the solution cascade and leads to a different greatest number, 25 instead of 27. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:77f1c657b1f19990,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"8 business executives and 7 chairmen meet at a conference. If each business executive shakes the hand of every other business executive and every chairman once, and each chairman shakes the hand of each of the business executives but not the other chairmen, how many handshakes would take place?","The business executives will have 8C2 = 28 handshakes
