eic,eic:7b60e0805691038d,full,referencing_context_value_error,"Mr. Callen bought 10 paintings at $40 each and 8 wooden toys at $20 each from the crafts store to resell at a profit. However, when he sold the items, the selling price of a painting was 10% less and the selling price of a hat 15% less. Calculate the total loss Mr. Callen made from the sale of the items.","If he sold a painting at a 10% loss, then he made a 10/100*$30 = $3 loss on each painting.
