#### 54",Calculates a percentage loss using the wrong reference value,10/100*$30 = $3 loss on each painting,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,loss,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If he sold a painting at a 10% loss, then he made a 10/100*$40 = $4 loss on each painting.\nsince he bought 10 paintings, the total loss he made from selling the paintings is 10*$4 = $40\nHe also made a loss of 15/100*20 = $3 loss from selling each wooden toy.\nSince he bought 8 wooden toys, the total loss he made was 3*8 = $24\nIn total, Mr. Callen made a loss of $40+$24 = $64 from the sales of the items.\n#### 64"", ""original_answer"": 64.0, ""transformed_answer"": 54.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references $40 in the question as $30 wrongly, and calculates 10/100*$30 = $3 loss on each painting instead of 10/100*$40 = $4. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 10*$3 = $30 instead of 10*$4 = $40 in step 2. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the steps that reference the correct cost of the wooden toy will still reference $20 in the question correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
