x=53.333333333333336
Tom has been teaching for 53.333333333333336 years
#### 53.333333333333336",Adds the wrong amount when isolating a variable in an equation,80=(3/2)x,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the number of years Tom has been teaching\nDevin has been teaching for (1/2)x-5 years\n70=x+((1/2)x-5)\n70=(3/2)x-5\n75=(3/2)x\nx=50\nTom has been teaching for 50 years\n#### 50"", ""original_answer"": 50, ""transformed_answer"": 53.333333333333336, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Step 5 mistakenly references 75 as 80 from step 4 and changes 75=(3/2)x to 80=(3/2)x. It should be noted that step 4 in the transformed_solution <70=(3/2)x-5> should be the same as the step 4 in the original_solution <70=(3/2)x-5> and calculates its result 75 correctly. The changed reference affects only the subsequent steps that directly involve the value from the erroneous step but still uses correct arithmetic. Therefore, step 6 is affected by step 5 and changes from 75=(3/2)x to 80=(3/2)x, leading to an incorrect value for x. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all other steps is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:822dc387dca47b98,full,calculation_error,find 62976 ÷ ? = 123,"123 x ? = 62976
