#### 72",Uses an unsupported value when reversing the fractional relationship,"In 2005, 24/2*3=36 kids came to the cookout.",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""In 2005, 20/2*3=30 kids came to the cookout.\nIn 2004, 30*2=60 kids came to the cookout.\n#### 60"", ""original_answer"": 60.0, ""transformed_answer"": 72.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 20 in the question as 24 wrongly, and calculates 24/2*3=36 instead of 20/2*3=30. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 36*2=72 instead of 30*2=60 in step 2. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 2 still references the result from step 1 correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:84e7abd5afe1d531,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"worker a takes 8 hours to do a job. worker b takes 6 hours to do the same job. how long it take both a & b, working together but independently, to do the same job?","Worker A can complete 1/8 of the job in 1 hour.
