#### 2",Uses subtraction instead of addition when finding a quantity one unit older,Corey is 10 - 1 = 9 years old,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,older,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""James is 10 and 1 year younger than Corey, so Corey is 10 + 1 = 11 years old\nAmy is 2 years younger than Corey so is 11 - 2 = 9 years old\nAmy is also 5 years older than Jackson, so Jackson is 9 - 5 = 4 years old\n#### 4"", ""original_answer"": 4.0, ""transformed_answer"": 2.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""This example changes the addition in step 1 to subtraction, turning '10 + 1 = 11' into '10 - 1 = 9'. This error affects subsequent related steps 2 and 3. In step 2, the equation is now '9 - 2 = 7' resulting from the changed age of Corey, and in step 3, the equation becomes '7 - 5 = 2' due to Amy being 5 years older than Jackson, which has now been calculated based on the incorrect age of Amy. It should be noted that other than the erroneous operator change in step 1, the calculations in all other steps correctly follow through from the error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
