#### 850",Makes an arithmetic error when isolating the variable,850 = 20x - 19x = x,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,4,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the total number of students be x\nNumber of A's = (1/5)x\nNumber of B's = (1/4)x\nNumber of C's = (1/2)x\nNumber of D's = 40\n(1/5)x + (1/4)x + (1/2)x + 40 = x\nMultiplying by 20 to clear fractions gives 4x + 5x + 10x + 800 = 20x\n19x + 800 = 20x\n800 = 20x - 19x = x\n#### 800"", ""original_answer"": 800.0, ""transformed_answer"": 850.0, ""wrong_step"": 8, ""explanation"": ""Step 8 mistakenly references 800 as 850 from step 7 and changes 800 = 20x - 19x to 850 = 20x - 19x. It should be noted that step 7 in the transformed_solution <19x + 800 = 20x> should be the same as the step 7 in the original_solution <19x + 800 = 20x> and calculates its result 800 correctly. This is the only step where there should be an intentional error. The subsequent step 8 is affected by step 7 and changes the result from 800 to 850. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all other steps is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:8a39da41afbe58f0,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"of 70 players on a football team, 31 are throwers. the rest of the team is divided so one third are left-handed and the rest are right-handed. assuming that all throwers are right-handed, how many right-handed players are there total?","There are 70-31 = 39 non-throwers.
