#### 56",Uses an incorrect value from the previous calculation,There are 25 + 31 = 56 right-handed players in total.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""There are 70-31 = 39 non-throwers.\nThere are 39/3 = 13 left-handed players.\nThere are 39 - 13 = 26 right-handed non-throwers.\nThere are 26 + 31 = 57 right-handed players in total.\n#### 57"", ""original_answer"": 57.0, ""transformed_answer"": 56.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 mistakenly references 26 as 25 from step 3 and changes 26 + 31 = 57 to 25 + 31 = 56. It should be noted that step 3 in the transformed_solution <There are 39 - 13 = 26 right-handed non-throwers.> should be the same as the step 3 in the original_solution <There are 39 - 13 = 26 right-handed non-throwers.> and calculates its result 26 correctly. The final result of 57 is changed to 56 due to the error on step 4 affecting only the referencing of 26 as 25. All other steps maintain the correct relationship to their previous steps as per the original_solution, so the calculation of all steps is still correct, except for the intentional referencing error introduced in step 4."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:8a775d213393c30e,full,confusing_formula_error,"the ratio between the length and the breadth of a rectangular park is 3 : 2 . if a man cycling along the boundary of the park at the speed of 12 km / hr completes one round in 9 minutes , then the area of the park ( in sq . m ) is :","Let the length of the park be 3x and the breadth be 2x
