#### 2.4",Uses an incorrect number of minutes in one hour,50 minutes are in 1 hour,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""There are 80 cherries in a pound and she needs 3 pounds to make a pie so she needs 80*3 = 240 cherries\nIt takes her 10 minutes to pit a unit of 20 cherries. She has 240/20 = 12 units of cherries to pit\nIt takes 10 minutes to pit a unit of cherries and she has 12 units so it will take her 10*12 = 120 minutes\n60 minutes are in 1 hour and it takes her 120 minutes so that’s 120/60 = 2 hours\n#### 2"", ""original_answer"": 2.0, ""transformed_answer"": 2.4, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 4 contains an incorrect unit conversion, erroneously stating that 50 minutes are in an hour instead of the correct 60 minutes. This error alters the computation from 120/60 = 2 hours in the original solution to 120/50 = 2.4 hours in the transformed solution. This error affects only the related unit conversion in the final step, while previous calculations remain unaffected."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
