#### 16.7142857143",Miscounts the number of days worked at one hourly rate,Total hours worked in a week = (8 * 2) + (6 * 2) = 16 + 12 = 28 hours,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Total hours worked in a week = (8 * 3) + (6 * 2) = 24 + 12 = 36 hours\nShe earns $468 per week\nEarning per hour = 468 / 36\n#### 13"", ""original_answer"": 13.0, ""transformed_answer"": 16.7142857143, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 erroneously counts Monday, Wednesday, and Friday as 2 days each instead of 3, reducing the total worked hours from (8 * 3) to (8 * 2). This counting error affects only the calculation related to the total hours worked (step 1) and subsequently changes the earning per hour computation (step 3) from 468 / 36 = 13 to 468 / 28 = 16.7142857143. It should be noted that the counting error should only be at one place, and the other calculation processes after the count alteration stay correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
