eic,eic:8d7299620173c83b,full,operator_error,"A manufacturer produces a certain men's athletic shoe in integer sizes from 8 to 17. For this particular shoe, each unit increase in size corresponds to a 1/5-inch increase in the length of the shoe. If the largest size of this shoe is 20% longer than the smallest size, how long, in inches, is the shoe in size 15?","The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17+8 = 25
The increase in length is 25 x (1/5) = 25/5 inches
The length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x
