So, 1.2x = x + 25/5
0.2x = 25/5
x = (25/5) / 0.2 = 25
The length of size 8 is 25 inches, and size 15 is 25 + 7/5 = 26.4 inches
#### 26.4",Adds endpoint values instead of subtracting to find their difference,The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17+8 = 25,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17-8 = 9\nThe increase in length is 9 x (1/5) = 9/5 inches\nThe length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x\nThe length of size 17 is x + 9/5\nSo, 1.2x = x + 9/5\n0.2x = 9/5\nx = (9/5) / 0.2 = 9\nThe length of size 8 is 9 inches, and size 15 is 9 + 7/5 = 10.4 inches\n#### 10.4"", ""original_answer"": 10.4, ""transformed_answer"": 26.4, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""This example changes the subtraction operator to addition in the first step, modifying the difference in size from 17-8 = 9 to 17+8 = 25. Consequently, the computed length increase changes from 9/5 inches to 25/5 inches. The incorrect larger size for step 1 leads to the incorrect calculation for the length of size 17, and this carries forward to the final step, which calculates the length of size 15. The process retains the correction of all operations and the correct application of percentages but is predicated on the wrong initial value caused by the step 1 error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:8d8270e705575b97,full,counting_error,Berry is curious about what his average temperature is during the week. On Sunday his temperature is 99.1. On Monday his temperature is 98.2. On Tuesday his temperature is 98.7. On Wednesday his temperature is 99.3. On Thursday his temperature is 99.8. On Friday his temperature is 99. On Saturday his temperature is 98.9. What is his average temperature that week?,"The total temperature for the week is 693 because 99.1 plus 98.2 plus 98.7 plus 99.3 plus 99.8 plus 99 plus 98.9 equals 693.
