#### 3.3",Uses an incorrect speed value when calculating travel time,Time to travel that far is 330km / 100km/hour = 3.3 hours.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,travel,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Total distance travelled is 220km + 110km = 330 km.\nTime to travel that far is 330km / 110km/hour = 3 hours.\n#### 3"", ""original_answer"": 3.0, ""transformed_answer"": 3.3, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 mistakenly references 110km/hour as 100km/hour from step 1 and changes 330km / 110km/hour = 3 hours to 330km / 100km/hour = 3.3 hours. It should be noted that step 1 in the transformed_solution <Total distance travelled is 220km + 110km = 330 km.> should be the same as the step 1 in the original_solution <Total distance travelled is 220km + 110km = 330 km.> and calculates its result 330 km correctly. The change in speed from 110 km/hour to 100 km/hour in step 2 leads to an erroneous calculation of time as 3.3 hours instead of 3 hours. The subsequent step showing the calculated time will reflect this incorrect speed, showing 3.3 hours instead of the correct 3 hours. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the initial distance calculation step is still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:8e681c319f844591,full,calculation_error,"Jaco wants to buy Christmas gifts for his 8 friends that are worth $9 each. Also, he wants to buy gifts for his mother and father that are of the same amount. He has a $100 budget to buy all gifts. How much is Jaco's budget for each of his mother and father's gift?","Jaco will spend a total of $9 x 8 = $72 for his 8 friends' gifts.
