eic,eic:963520f41b9a3cf4,full,confusing_formula_error,"Find the area of trapezium whose parallel sides are 20 cm and 15 cm long, and the distance between them is 14 cm?","The formula for the perimeter of a trapezium is (sum of all sides)
So the perimeter of the trapezium is (20+15+14+14)=63 cm
#### 63",Uses the perimeter formula instead of the area formula,The formula for the perimeter of a trapezium is (sum of all sides),ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,12,"{""original_solution"": ""The formula for the area of a trapezium is (1/2)*(sum of parallel sides)*height\nSo the area of the trapezium is (1/2)*(20+15)*14= (1/2)*35*14= 245 square cm\n#### 245"", ""original_answer"": 245.0, ""transformed_answer"": 63.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 confuses the area and the perimeter of a trapezium. The question requires that the area of the trapezium to be solved be equal to (1/2)*(sum of parallel sides)*height, not the sum of all sides, which is equivalent to the perimeter of the trapezium, resulting in (1/2)*(20+15)*14= (1/2)*35*14= 245 square cm in the original_solution being changed to (20+15+14+14)=63 cm in the transformed_solution. This significantly affects the calculation leading to step 2 being omitted as it is related to area, not perimeter, and the final transformed_answer which should be different from the original_answer. Note that the language description of step 1 < The formula for the area of a trapezium is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. It should be also noted that you need to only consider one step of confusing formula error, and leave the sentences explaining steps correct in the context of the new, incorrect formula."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:9638ad8ee2db75ea,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"Wink, Inc. follows a certain procedure that requires two tasks to be finished independently in order for a job to be done. On any given day, there is a 2/3 probability that task 1 will be completed on time, and a 3/5 probability that task 2 will be completed on time. On a certain day, what is the probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not?","The probability that task 1 will be completed on time is 2/3.
The probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 2/5
The probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not is 2/3 * 3/5 = 6/15
#### 6/15",Multiplies by the original probability instead of the computed complement,"The probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not is 2/3 * 3/5 = 6/15",ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,probability,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The probability that task 1 will be completed on time is 2/3.\nThe probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 2/5\nThe probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not is 2/3 * 2/5 = 4/15\n#### 4/15"", ""original_answer"": 0.26666666666666666, ""transformed_answer"": 0.4, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 mistakenly references 2/5 as 3/5 from step 2 and changes the multiplication from 2/3 * 2/5 to 2/3 * 3/5. It should be noted that step 2 in the transformed_solution <The probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 2/5> should be the same as the step 2 in the original_solution <The probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 2/5> and calculates its result 2/5 correctly. Step 3 is the only step with an error because it incorrectly references the probability for task 2 being not completed instead of the correct value. All previous steps remain unmodified, and the calculations in the subsequent steps are performed correctly based on the erroneous value provided in the modified step."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:9638d3cc87696b7e,full,referencing_context_value_error,"if a - b = 3 and a^2 + b^2 = 29, then find the value of ab","a - b = 3
