ab = 9 (Dividing 18 by 2)
#### 9",Changes the given value before applying the identity,a^2 + b^2 = 27,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""a - b = 3\na^2 + b^2 = 29\na^2 - 2ab + b^2 = 9 (squaring a - b)\n2ab = 20 (Subtracting 9 from 29)\nab = 10 (Dividing 20 by 2)\n#### 10"", ""original_answer"": 10.0, ""transformed_answer"": 9.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 references 29 in the question as 27 wrongly, and calculates a^2 + b^2 = 27 instead of a^2 + b^2 = 29. Its subsequent related steps, step 4 and step 5, will be affected. Step 4 changes from 2ab = 20 (Subtracting 9 from 29) to 2ab = 18 (Subtracting 9 from 27), and step 5 changes from ab = 10 (Dividing 20 by 2) to ab = 9 (Dividing 18 by 2). Please note that you should only consider one error, so the squaring of a - b to get a^2 - 2ab + b^2 = 9 is still calculated correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:964cc0e625fbd5bb,full,adding_irrelevant_information,The sum of three consecutive even numbers is 246. What are the numbers?,"Let the three consecutive even numbers be x, x+2, and x+4, and they found an additional even number x+6 lying on the ground which they also took.
