#### Error",Includes an irrelevant extra quantity in the sum,The sum of the four numbers including the one found is x + (x+2) + (x+4) + (x+6) = 4x + 12.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the three consecutive even numbers be x, x+2, and x+4.\nThe sum of the three numbers is x + (x+2) + (x+4) = 3x + 6.\nAccording to the problem, 3x + 6 = 246.\n3x = 240.\nx = 80.\nThe three consecutive even numbers are 80, 82, and 84.\n#### 80, 82, 84"", ""original_answer"": [80, 82, 84], ""transformed_answer"": ""Error"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement by including a non-existent additional number <and they found an additional even number x+6 lying on the ground which they also took>, resulting in step 1 changing from calculating the sum of three even numbers x + (x+2) + (x+4) in the original_solution to calculating the sum of four numbers including the supposed number found x + (x+2) + (x+4) + (x+6) in the transformed_solution. This change caused the derived equation to become 4x + 12 = 246, which led to an incorrect calculation of the value of x, and thus the incorrect listing of the numbers as this violates the original problem constraints. This error makes the new answer not viable."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:96a16a341bbe0856,full,adding_irrelevant_information,Jim decides to open up a bike shop.  The most common repair he does is fixing bike tires.  He charges $20 for this and it cost him $5 in parts.  In one month Jim does 300 of these repairs.  He also does 2 more complex repairs for $300 each and cost $50 in parts.  He also sells $2000 profit worth of things from his retail shop.  If rent and other fixed expense for the shop is $4000 a month how much profit did the shop make?,"From each tire repair, he made 20-5=$15 profit
So repairs made him a profit of 15*300=$4500
The two complex repairs each made him 300-50=$250 profit
So those added 250*2=$500
Because Jim had to pay a $300 fine for a parking violation related to his shop, his total profit from everything was 4500+500+2000-300=$6700
So he made a profit of 6700-4000=$2700
#### 2700",Adds an unsupported expense to the profit calculation,Because Jim had to pay a $300 fine for a parking violation related to his shop,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,expense,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""From each tire repair, he made 20-5=$15 profit\nSo repairs made him a profit of 15*300=$4500\nThe two complex repairs each made him 300-50=$250 profit\nSo those added 250*2=$500\nSo his total profit from everything was 4500+500+2000=$7000\nSo he made a profit of 7000-4000=$3000\n#### 3000"", ""original_answer"": 3000.0, ""transformed_answer"": 2700.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because Jim had to pay a $300 fine for a parking violation related to his shop>, resulting in step 4 changing from 4500+500+2000=$7000 in the original_solution to 4500+500+2000-300=$6700 in the transformed_solution. This change also affected step 5, where the new profit calculation is 6700-4000=$2700 instead of the original $3000. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:96d5667385f857f5,full,unit_conversion_error,"The distance from city A to city B is 30 miles. While driving from city A to city B, Bob drives at a constant speed of 40 miles per hour. Alice leaves city A 30 minutes after Bob. What is the minimum constant speed in miles per hour that Alice must exceed in order to arrive in city B before Bob?","The time it takes Bob to get to city B is 30 miles / 40 miles per hour = 0.75 hours.
Alice leaves 30 minutes after Bob, so she has 0.75 hours less time to get to city B than Bob.
To get to city B before Bob, Alice must drive 30 miles in 0.75 - 0.75 = 0 hours.
Therefore, the minimum constant speed in miles per hour that Alice must exceed in order to arrive in city B before Bob is 30 miles / 0 hours = undefined miles per hour.
#### undefined",Fails to convert minutes to hours before subtracting times,"Alice leaves 30 minutes after Bob, so she has 0.75 hours less time to get to city B than Bob.",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,before,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The time it takes Bob to get to city B is 30 miles / 40 miles per hour = 0.75 hours.\nAlice leaves 30 minutes after Bob, so she has 0.5 hours less time to get to city B than Bob.\nTo get to city B before Bob, Alice must drive 30 miles in 0.75 - 0.5 = 0.25 hours.\nTherefore, the minimum constant speed in miles per hour that Alice must exceed in order to arrive in city B before Bob is 30 miles / 0.25 hours = 120 miles per hour.\n#### 120"", ""original_answer"": 120.0, ""transformed_answer"": null, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 makes an incorrect unit conversion error by stating that Alice has 0.75 hours less time instead of 0.5 hours, due to incorrectly converting 30 minutes into 0.75 hours instead of the correct 0.5 hours. This error affects the subsequent steps, specifically steps 3 and 4, where the time Alice has to drive is calculated incorrectly as 0 hours (0.75 - 0.75), leading to an incorrect, undefined speed calculation since one cannot divide by zero."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
