#### 42",Uses an incorrect conversion factor between minutes and hours,30 minutes * (1 hour/50 minutes) = 0.6 hours,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""We must first convert minutes to hours, so 30 minutes * (1 hour/60 minutes) = 0.5 hours\nThe number of miles Greg travels on his trip home is 0.5 hours * 20 mph = 10 miles\nThe total miles Greg travels is 10 + 30 = 40 miles\n#### 40"", ""original_answer"": 40.0, ""transformed_answer"": 42.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 incorrectly converts minutes to hours by stating 1 hour is equal to 50 minutes instead of the correct 60 minutes, which results in 30 minutes being converted to 0.6 hours in the transformed_solution rather than the correct 0.5 hours. The subsequent calculation directly related to this conversion is affected, changing the distance Greg travels from home from 10 miles to 12 miles. The total distance thus changes from 40 miles to 42 miles. This change is the only error introduced to generate the transformed_solution; other calculations are left as in the original_solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:99d834ac338b8fb5,full,adding_irrelevant_information,Tabitha and her friends were excited to go to the Christmas parade because they knew candy would be thrown to the crowd from the floats. Tabitha caught 22 pieces of candy. Stan caught 13 pieces. Julie caught half the amount of candy as Tabitha caught and Carlos caught twice as much candy as Stan. How many pieces in total did the friends catch?,"Julie caught half the amount of Tabitha's 22 pieces so 22/2 = 11 pieces of candy caught by Julie
