#### 9",Substitutes an incorrect value for one of the given speeds,x - s = 7,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the speed of the boat in still water.\nThe speed of the boat along the stream is x + s and against the stream is x - s.\nAccording to the given information, x + s = 11 and x - s = 5.\nAdding the two equations, we get 2x = 16, so x = 8.\n#### 8"", ""original_answer"": 8.0, ""transformed_answer"": 9.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references 5 in the question as 7 wrongly, and calculates x - s = 7 instead of x - s = 5. Its subsequent steps will correctly calculate values based on this erroneous result: adding the two equations results in 2x = 18 instead of the correct 2x = 16, leading to x = 9 instead of the correct x = 8. All the other steps correctly reference their respective numbers, but the transformed_answer changes due to the wrong value used in step 3."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:a028a8b2b6124363,full,operator_error,"if n is an integer, f(n) = f(n - 1) - n and f(4) = 14. What is the value of f(6)?","f(5) = f(4) + 5 = 14 + 5 = 19
