#### 1024",Treats a negative exponent as a positive exponent,The value of ( 4 ) ^ - 5 is 1 * (4^5).,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The value of ( 4 ) ^ - 5 is 1 / (4^5).\nThis means 1 / (4 x 4 x 4 x 4 x 4).\nThis results in 1 / 1024.\n#### 1 / 1024"", ""original_answer"": 0.0009765625, ""transformed_answer"": 1024, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""The original step 1 represents raising 4 to the power of -5, which is correctly calculated as 1 divided by 4 raised to the power of 5. By changing the division in step 1 to multiplication, the inversion of the exponentiation is eliminated, incorrectly implying that (4)^-5 is equal to 1 multiplied by 4 raised to the power of 5 instead of 1 divided. This mistake results in a positive exponent and a final result of 1024 instead of the correct result 1 / 1024. All other steps used correct calculations based on the erroneous interpretation in step 1."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:a06c2baa8888474e,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"if the average (arithmetic mean) of 2a + 16, 3a - 8 is 94, what is the value of a?","The average of 2a + 16 and 3a - 8 is (2a + 16 + 3a - 8) / 2 = 5a + 8 / 2 = (5a + 8) / 2
