#### 30",Uses an incorrect starting value when calculating a later age,"In 10 years, Zion will be 5 + 10 = 15 years old.",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Four times Zion's age is 8 x 4 = 32.\nSo Zion's dad is 32 + 3 = 35 years old.\nIn 10 years, Zion will be 8 + 10 = 18 years old.\nIn 10 years, Zion's dad will be 35 + 10 = 45 years old.\nHence, in 10 years, Zion's dad will be 45 - 18 = 27 years older than Zion.\n#### 27"", ""original_answer"": 27, ""transformed_answer"": 30, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 references 8 in the question as 5 wrongly, and calculates 5 + 10 = 15 instead of 8 + 10 = 18. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 45 - 15 = 30 instead of 45 - 18 = 27 in step 5. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the 35 in step 4 is calculated correctly based on step 2."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
