#### 25.14",Miscounts the number of terms when computing the average,The total number of these numbers is 7,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The numbers between 6 and 38 which are divisible by 4 are: \n8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 28, 32, 36\nThe total of these numbers is 8 + 12 + 16 + 20 + 24 + 28 + 32 + 36 = 176\nThe total number of these numbers is 8\nThe average of these numbers is 176 / 8 = 22\n#### 22"", ""original_answer"": 22.0, ""transformed_answer"": 25.14, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 mistakenly counts the total number of numbers divisible by 4 between 6 and 38 as 7 instead of 8, resulting in the transformed solution calculating the average by dividing 176 by 7 to get 25.14 instead of dividing by 8 to get 22 as in the original solution. This counting error led to a different average being calculated in the transformed solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:a642b6674de7e2cc,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,John takes care of 10 dogs.  Each dog takes .5 hours a day to walk and take care of their business.  How many hours a week does he spend taking care of dogs?,"He spends 10*.5=5 hours per day
