#### 40",Uses an incorrect per-unit value in the mixture equation,20(8) + 5x = (20 + x)(6),ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,mixture,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the number of pounds of $5.00 per pound candy.\n20(10) + 5x = (20 + x)(6)\n200 + 5x = 120 + 6x\n80 = x\n#### 80"", ""original_answer"": 80.0, ""transformed_answer"": 40.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 incorrectly references $10.00 as $8.00, resulting in the calculation 20(8) instead of the correct 20(10). The subsequent steps inherit the faulty resultant value but are computed correctly based on the new incorrect condition. Consequently, in step 2, the equation 160 + 5x = 120 + 6x is formed instead of the correct 200 + 5x = 120 + 6x, leading to an erroneous solution of x = 40 instead of x = 80."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:a6e0fd53811fdd87,full,confusing_formula_error,A cistern 4 m long and 2 m wide contains water up to a depth of 1 m 25 cm. The total area of the wet surface is:,"The wet surface area includes the bottom and all four sides of the cistern.
