#### 360",Uses an incorrect weekly homework amount,"Add to that his 5 hours of small group work, 5 + 10 = 15 hours a week.",ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,homework,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Each week, David will spend 3 hours + 3 hours + 4 hours = 10 hours in class.\nAdd to that his 4 hours of small group work, 4 + 10 = 14 hours a week.\nHe will spend 14 hours x 24 weeks = 336 hours on the course.\n#### 336"", ""original_answer"": 336.0, ""transformed_answer"": 360.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 references 4 in the question as 5 wrongly, and calculates 5 + 10 = 15 hours a week instead of 4 + 10 = 14 hours a week. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 15 hours x 24 weeks = 360 hours on the course instead of 14 hours x 24 weeks = 336 hours. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 3 still references 24 in the question correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:aaba239229c16f08,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"The region east of plain A is 50 square miles less than the region east of plain B. If plain B has 200 square miles, how many square miles do the plains have in total?","The region of plain A has a total of 200 - 50 = 150 square miles.
