The combined time that 20 bunnies coming out of their holes will have taken in 10 hours is 1500*20=30000 times.
#### 30000",Uses an incorrect number of minutes per hour in time conversion,"in an hour, with 50 minutes",ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If a bunny comes out of its hole three times in a minute, in an hour, with 60 minutes, the bunny will come out of the hole 60*3=180 times.\nIn 10 hours, a bunny will come out of their hole 180*10=1800 times.\nThe combined time that 20 bunnies coming out of their holes will have taken in 10 hours is 1800*20=36000 times.\n#### 36000"", ""original_answer"": 36000.0, ""transformed_answer"": 30000.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 makes incorrect unit conversion, which assumes that there are 50 minutes in an hour instead of the correct 60 minutes. This results in a cascade of errors through the subsequent steps. The original_solution stating that a bunny will come out of the hole 60*3=180 times is transformed to 50*3=150 times. Consequently, the 10-hour total for one bunny changes from 180*10=1800 in the original_solution to 150*10=1500 in the transformed_solution. The final combined count for 20 bunnies then changes from 1800*20=36000 times to 1500*20=30000 times. It should be noted that only one step of unit conversion error is considered and the rest of calculation steps are kept consistent with the original solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:ad206e710d0f6f33,full,counting_error,"Danivan Drugstore has 4500 bottles of hand sanitizer gel in inventory at the beginning of the week. On Monday 2445 bottles were sold, on Tuesday 900 bottles were sold, and 50 bottles each day for the rest of the week were sold (from Wednesday until Sunday). On Saturday, the supplier delivers an order for 650 bottles. How many bottles of sanitizer gel does the Drugstore have at the end of the week?","The number of bottles sold on Monday and Tuesday is 2445 + 900 = 3345 bottles
Each day of the rest of the week, 50 bottles were sold, that is 4 * 50 = 200 bottles sold.
Now the total of bottles sold in a week is 3345 + 200= 3545 bottles
The drugstore has in stock 4500 – 3545= 955 bottles
Finally, after the supplier delivered on Saturday, the drugstore has 955 + 650= 1605 bottles at the end of the week.
#### 1605",Counts the number of repeated daily sales days incorrectly,that is 4 * 50 = 200 bottles sold.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The number of bottles sold on Monday and Tuesday is 2445 + 900 = 3345 bottles\nEach day of the rest of the week, 50 bottles were sold, that is 5 * 50 = 250 bottles sold.\nNow the total of bottles sold in a week is 3345 + 250= 3595 bottles\nThe drugstore has in stock 4500 – 3595= 905 bottles\nFinally the drugstore has 905 + 650 the supplier brought = 1555 bottles at the end of the week.\n#### 1555"", ""original_answer"": 1555.0, ""transformed_answer"": 1605.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed_solution, the error has been introduced at step 2, where the original counting of the days from Wednesday to Sunday being 5 days has erroneously been counted as 4 days. This affected the calculation of the total number of bottles sold from the rest of the week, and consequently the final stock count at the end of the week. While this counting error has altered the outcome, the structure and calculations of the other steps in the solution have been performed correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:ad5742b1e8cb893c,full,calculation_error,"A manufacturer produces a certain men's athletic shoe in integer sizes from 8 to 17. For this particular shoe, each unit increase in size corresponds to a 1/5-inch increase in the length of the shoe. If the largest size of this shoe is 20% longer than the smallest size, how long, in inches, is the shoe in size 15?","The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17-8 = 9
The increase in length is 9 x (1/5) = 9/5 inches
The length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x
The length of size 17 is x + 9/5
So, 1.2x = x + 9/5
0.2x = 9/5
x = (9/5) / 0.2 = 45
The length of size 8 is 45 inches, and size 15 is 45 + 7/5 = 46.4 inches
#### 46.4",Makes an arithmetic error when dividing by a decimal,x = (9/5) / 0.2 = 45,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""The difference in size between the largest and smallest is 17-8 = 9\nThe increase in length is 9 x (1/5) = 9/5 inches\nThe length of size 8 is x, the length of size 17 is (1 + 20%) x = 1.2x\nThe length of size 17 is x + 9/5\nSo, 1.2x = x + 9/5\n0.2x = 9/5\nx = (9/5) / 0.2 = 9\nThe length of size 8 is 9 inches, and size 15 is 9 + 7/5 = 10.4 inches\n#### 10.4"", ""original_answer"": 10.4, ""transformed_answer"": 46.4, ""wrong_step"": 6, ""explanation"": ""The error is introduced at step 6 where the division (9/5) / 0.2 is incorrectly calculated as 45 instead of 9. All previous operations and logic are correct and unrelated to the error. The wrong result of step 6 leads to a miscalculation in the subsequent step 7, where the length of size 8 is incorrectly stated as 45 inches, and then the length of size 15 will also be wrong, calculated as 45 + 7/5 = 46.4 inches instead of 9 + 7/5 = 10.4 inches."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:adc37671296b664d,full,calculation_error,"Maddox and Theo both bought 3 Polaroid Cameras, each sold at $20 per camera from Amazon, and decided to sell them on eBay. Maddox sold his cameras at $28 each, while Theo sold his cameras at $23 each. How much more profit did Maddox get from the sale of his cameras than Theo?","The total cost of buying 3 cameras from Amazon for both Maddox and Theo was 3*$20=$60
Maddox sold his cameras at $28 each, for a total of $28*3=$84
Maddox made a profit of $84-$60=$24 from the sale of his cameras.
Theo sold his cameras on eBay for $23*3=$59
Theo made a profit of $59-$60=-$1
Maddox made $24-(-$1)=$25 more profit than Theo from the sale of his cameras.
#### 25",Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying a unit price by a quantity,Theo sold his cameras on eBay for $23*3=$59,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total cost of buying 3 cameras from Amazon for both Maddox and Theo was 3*$20=$60\nMaddox sold his cameras at $28 each, for a total of $28*3=$84\nMaddox made a profit of $84-$60=$24 from the sale of his cameras.\nTheo sold his cameras on eBay for $23*3=$69\nTheo made a profit of $69-$60=$9\nMaddox made $24-$9=$15 more profit than Theo from the sale of his cameras.\n#### 15"", ""original_answer"": 15.0, ""transformed_answer"": 25.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""The miscalculation occurs at step 4, where the total sales for Theo’s cameras are incorrectly calculated as $23*3=$59 instead of $23*3=$69. This error affects Theo’s profit calculation in step 5, changing the correct profit from $9 to -$1, and further affects the comparison of Maddox’s profit to Theo’s profit in step 6, resulting in an incorrect higher profit for Maddox of $25 instead of $15."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:add08d13942414cd,full,counting_error,"Steve decides to read a new book. He reads 100 pages Monday, Wed, and Friday. The book is 2100 pages long. How many weeks does it take to read them all?","He reads 100*2=200 pages a week
So it would take 2100/200=10.5 weeks to read the book
#### 10.5",Miscounts the number of reading days per week,He reads 100*2=200 pages a week,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""He reads 100*3=300 pages a week\nSo it would take 2100/300=7 weeks to read the book\n#### 7"", ""original_answer"": 7.0, ""transformed_answer"": 10.5, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 erroneously counts Monday, Wednesday, and Friday as 2 days instead of 3 days, resulting in 100*3=300 becoming 100*2=200. This affects step 2, changing from 2100/300=7 to 2100/200=10.5. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of counting error, and the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:ae185ccc831153d8,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"Mr. Sam shared a certain amount of money between his two sons, Ken and Tony. If Ken got $1750, and Tony got twice as much as Ken, how much was the money shared?","Tony got twice $1750 which is 2*$1750 = $3500
