#### -160",Divides by a fraction instead of multiplying to find a part of a whole,There are 160 / 1/2 = 320 girls in the class.,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""There are 160 x 1/2 = 80 girls in the class.\nThere are 160 - 80 = 80 boys in the class.\n#### 80"", ""original_answer"": 80.0, ""transformed_answer"": -160.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the multiplication operator in step 1 has been changed to division, thus incorrectly calculating the number of girls as 160 / 1/2 = 320 instead of 160 x 1/2 = 80. This results in an impossible count of boys, calculated in step 2 as 160 - 320 = -160, which is not a feasible number of students. The original count was 80 boys, so the transformation caused by the operator error in step 1 led to a nonsensical answer. Every step's calculation is correct except for the incorrect application of the operator in step 1."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:ae74f8f7b301d128,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,Trevor buys several bouquets of carnations. The first included 9 carnations; the second included 14 carnations; the third included 13 carnations. What is the average number of carnations in the bouquets?,"The sum is 9+14+13=36.
