#### 89.44",Uses an incorrect dimension when calculating the rectangle's area,The area of the rectangle is 20 * 5 = 100 square cm.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The area of the rectangle is 25 * 5 = 125 square cm.\nThe area of the square is 125 * 5 = 625 square cm.\nThe side length of the square is √625 = 25 cm.\nThe perimeter of the square is 4 * 25 = 100 cm.\n#### 100"", ""original_answer"": 100.0, ""transformed_answer"": 89.44, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 25 in the question as 20 wrongly, and calculates 20 * 5 = 100 square cm instead of 25 * 5 = 125 square cm. Its subsequent related steps will be affected by the erroneous result of this step but will still be calculated correctly, with step 2 changing to 100 * 5 = 500 square cm, step 3 changing to √500 = 22.36 (rounded to 2 decimal places), and step 4 changing to 4 * 22.36 = 89.44 cm. Please note that you should only consider one error, so the subsequent related steps are still calculated correctly considering the previous incorrect result."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:aff30f9065abb1a3,full,missing_step,A small theater company sells tickets to a show. They have a 400 seat theater and fill to 80% capacity. Each ticket cost $30. They repeated the same performance 2 other days. How much did they make?,"So each day they made 400 * 30 = $12,000
