x = 150.
#### 150",Uses the wrong water percentage when calculating dry mass,The weight of water in x kgs of fresh grapes is 0.90x.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,water,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the weight of fresh grapes needed to get 20 kgs of raisins.\nThe weight of water in x kgs of fresh grapes is 0.85x.\nThe weight of dry grapes in x kgs of fresh grapes is x - 0.85x = 0.15x.\nThe weight of water in 20 kgs of raisins is 0.25 * 20 = 5 kgs.\nThe weight of dry grapes in 20 kgs of raisins is 20 - 5 = 15 kgs.\n0.15x = 15.\nx = 15 / 0.15.\nx = 100.\n#### 100"", ""original_answer"": 100.0, ""transformed_answer"": 150.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 references 85% in the question as 90% wrongly, and calculates the weight of dry grapes in fresh grapes as x - 0.90x = 0.10x instead of x - 0.85x = 0.15x. Its subsequent related step will be affected, changing the equation from 0.15x = 15 to 0.10x = 15 in step 6, and the solution from x = 100 to x = 150 in step 7. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 4 is still referencing the correct percentage for raisins and calculates it correctly as 0.25 * 20 = 5 kgs."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:b1adfff10dd2757e,full,unit_conversion_error,Micah can type 20 words per minute and Isaiah can type 40 words per minute. How many more words can Isaiah type than Micah in an hour?,"There are 50 minutes in an hour.
