#### 44",Introduces an unsupported extra quantity into the calculation,he needs to spend 2 extra hours helping Greg,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,5,"{""original_solution"": ""If Jacob has 18 hours left to finish his homework, Greg has 18-6 = 12 hours left to finish his homework.\nThe total number of hours Jacob and Greg have left to finish their homework is 12+18 = 30 hours.\nPatrick has 4 hours less than twice Greg has left to finish his homework, meaning Patrick has 4 hours less than 12*2 = 24 hours left to finish his homework.\nPatrick has 24-4 = 20 hours left to finish his homework.\nAltogether, the three have 30+20 = 50 hours left to finish their homework.\n#### 50"", ""original_answer"": 50.0, ""transformed_answer"": 44.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <and he needs to spend 2 extra hours helping Greg>, resulting in step 1 changing from 18-6 = 12 hours left to finish his homework in the original_solution to 18 - 6 - 2 = 10 hours left to finish his homework in the transformed_solution. Its subsequent related steps (2, 3, and 4) are affected, changing the final total from 50 hours to 44 hours. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:b8c2b8dd08fde18d,full,referencing_context_value_error,"The pizza delivery person has 12 pizzas to deliver. If two of the stops are for orders of two pizzas and the rest are for single pizzas, how many minutes per stop does the delivery person need to average to deliver all of the pizzas in 40 minutes?","If two pizzas will be delivered at two of the stops, the total number of stops will be 12-4=8 stops.
