#### 4.07",Uses an incorrect combined speed when calculating travel time,The time it takes to meet is 855 / 210 = 4.07 hours.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the speed of the second car be x km/h.\nThe speed of the first car is 120 km/h, which is 28% faster than the second car, so 120 = x + 0.28x.\n120 = 1.28x\nx = 120 / 1.28 = 93.75 km/h.\nIn 1 hour, the cars cover 120 + 93.75 = 213.75 km.\nThe time it takes to meet is 855 / 213.75 = 4 hours.\n#### 4"", ""original_answer"": 4.0, ""transformed_answer"": 4.07, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the result of step 5 has been changed from 213.75 to an erroneous value of 210 km/h. Therefore, the cars would supposedly cover 210 km in 1 hour instead of 213.75 km. All the previous steps remain unchanged, and the subsequent step 6 uses the incorrect value from step 5 for further calculation: 855 / 210 = 4.07 hours instead of the correct 855 / 213.75 = 4 hours. Only one calculation result was incorrectly modified, and the rest of the solution is adapted based on this error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:b90274627e61f5d3,full,calculation_error,Alissa used discarded paper to make notepads for her friends. She would fold 5 pieces of letter-size paper 3 times then cut along the edges to form smaller note papers. She would then stack these smaller note papers and staple them together. How long would 1 notepad last if someone wrote 10 notes per day?,"Alissa folding it 3 times makes 2 × 2 × 2 = 8 pieces of note-size paper per letter-size paper.
