#### 336",Adds the discount to the original cost instead of subtracting it,Her $280.00 towels have a $56.00 discount making them 280+56 = $336.00,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""She needs 2 sets of guest towels that are $40.00 each so that’s 2*40 = $80.00\nShe needs 4 sets of master bath towels that are $50.00 each so that’s 4*50 = $200.00\nTogether, the towels will cost 80+200 = $280.00\nThe store is offering 20% off of her $280.00 towels so that’s 280*.20 = $56.00 discount\nHer $280.00 towels have a $56.00 discount making them 280-56 =$224.00\n#### 224"", ""original_answer"": 224.0, ""transformed_answer"": 336.0, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""This example converts the subtraction in step 5 into addition, changing 280-56 to 280+56 by changing - to +. As a result, the calculation in step 5 is still correct given the altered operator, but the outcome is different, leading to a changed transformed_answer. The wrong step (step 5) alters the outcome of the calculation such that Bailey will be spending more than the discounted price, which is incorrect in the context of the problem. However, all prior steps and calculations remain correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:bbacd762174cde06,full,calculation_error,"A train crosses a platform of 250 m in 20 sec, the same train crosses another platform of length 640 m in 40 sec. Then find the length of the train?","Speed = Distance/Time
