eic,eic:bd1b1104ed072f31,full,confusing_formula_error,The cost of painting the whole surface area of a cube at the rate of 13 paise per sq. cm is Rs. 343.98. Then the volume of the cube is,"Let the side of the cube be x
The volume of the cube is x^3
The cost of painting the whole surface area is x^3 * 13 paise = 13x^3 paise
So, 13x^3 paise = 343.98 rs
1 paise = 1/100 rs
Therefore, 13x^3 * (1/100) = 343.98
13x^3 = 34398
x^3 = 2646
x = 14
The surface area of the cube is 6x^2 = 6*14^2 = 1176 sq. cm
#### 1176",Uses the volume formula instead of the surface-area formula in the cost equation,The cost of painting the whole surface area is x^3 * 13 paise = 13x^3 paise,ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the side of the cube be x\nThe surface area of the cube is 6x^2\nThe cost of painting the whole surface area is 6x^2 * 13 paise = 78x^2 paise\nSo, 78x^2 paise = 343.98 rs\n1 paise = 1/100 rs\nTherefore, 78x^2 * (1/100) = 343.98\n78x^2 = 34398\nx^2 = 441\nx = 21\nThe volume of the cube is x^3 = 21^3 = 9261 cubic units\n#### 9261"", ""original_answer"": 9261.0, ""transformed_answer"": 1176.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 confuses the surface area and volume of a cube. The question requires that the cost calculation be based on the surface area (6x^2), not the volume (x^3) of the cube. The original step 3 is transformed from calculating the cost based on the surface area to incorrectly calculating it based on the volume, resulting in 6x^2 * 13 paise = 78x^2 paise in the original_solution being changed to x^3 * 13 paise = 13x^3 paise in the transformed_solution. This modification also affects the subsequent steps, causing a chain of incorrect calculations leading to a transformed answer (1176 sq. cm as the calculated \""surface area\""). Note that the natural language descriptions in the steps of the transformed_solution were kept the same as in the original_solution, and only the formula was changed to create the error. The resulting answer should not be the volume but is mistakenly presented as such, which emphasizes the incorrect application of volume formula where surface area formula was required."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:bd27f50cf46b30f6,full,referencing_context_value_error,"If a rectangle has a width of 42 inches and an area of 1638, how many rectangles of the same size would reach a length of 390 inches?","The rectangle has a length of 1638 in/ 40in = 40.95 in.
