Total tax as a percent of the total amount spent = (0.048x / x) * 100
Total tax as a percent of the total amount spent = 4.8%
#### 4.8%",Uses an incorrect percentage for one category,Amount spent on clothing = 0.6x,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the total amount that Rose spent, excluding taxes.\nAmount spent on clothing = 0.5x\nAmount spent on food = 0.2x\nAmount spent on other items = 0.3x\nTax paid on clothing = 0.04 * 0.5x = 0.02x\nTax paid on other items = 0.08 * 0.3x = 0.024x\nTotal amount spent on taxes = 0.02x + 0.024x = 0.044x\nTotal tax as a percent of the total amount spent = (0.044x / x) * 100\nTotal tax as a percent of the total amount spent = 4.4%\n#### 4.4%"", ""original_answer"": 4.4, ""transformed_answer"": 4.8, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 50 percent in the question as 60 percent wrongly, calculating 0.6x for the amount spent on clothing instead of the correct 0.5x. This error affects the computation of the tax paid on clothing in step 4, leading to a miscalculation of the tax amount as 0.024x instead of 0.02x. Consequently, the erroneous tax values affect the total tax computation in step 6, changing the total tax from 0.044x to 0.048x, and affecting the final percentage calculation in step 8. Note that the numbers for the other items and their tax rates are referenced correctly, and it's the first erroneous step that causes all subsequent related steps to inherit its erroneous result, though they are computed correctly based on the wrong value provided."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:bdaaf68ac544547d,full,operator_error,In what time will a railway train 30 m long moving at the rate of 36 kmph pass a telegraph post on its way?,"First convert the speed from km/h to m/s: 36 km/h * (1000 m/km) * (1/3600 s/h) = 10 m/s
The time it takes to pass the telegraph post is the length of the train divided by the speed: 30 m * 10 m/s = 300 s
#### 300 seconds",Multiplies length by speed instead of dividing length by speed,30 m * 10 m/s = 300 s,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""First convert the speed from km/h to m/s: 36 km/h * (1000 m/km) / (3600 s/h) = 10 m/s\nThe time it takes to pass the telegraph post is the length of the train divided by the speed: 30 m / 10 m/s = 3 s\n#### 3 seconds"", ""original_answer"": 3.0, ""transformed_answer"": 300.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""This transformed solution changes the division operator to a multiplication operator in the second step of the calculation process. Specifically, it incorrectly represents the time it takes for the train to pass the telegraph post by changing 30 m / 10 m/s to 30 m * 10 m/s. This leads to a mathematically incorrect formula and an incorrect result of 300 seconds instead of the correct result of 3 seconds. The conversion from km/h to m/s in the first step remains correct, but the subsequent step of calculating time, which was affected by changing the division operator to multiplication, is erroneous. This is the only step where an error occurs in the transformation, and all other calculations are carried out correctly according to the wrong operator used."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
