eic,eic:bf47c38d94602a0f,full,missing_step,There are 6 trees in Chris's yard.  Ferdinand has half the number of trees that Chris has.  Harry has 5 more than twice the number of trees that Ferdinand has.  How many more trees are in Harry's yard than Ferdinand's yard?,"Harry:5+2(6/2)=5+2*3=5+6=11 trees
11-3=8 trees
