#### 24",Uses an incorrect number of minutes per hour,There are 50 minutes in an hour so she spends 1200/50 = 24 hours grooming her dogs,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,5,"{""original_solution"": ""She has 2 dogs and it takes 20 minutes to groom just 1 dog so it takes her 2*20 = 40 minutes per day to groom 2 dogs\nIn 30 days, she will have spent 30*40 = 1,200 minutes grooming her dogs\nThere are 60 minutes in an hour so she spends 1200/60 = 20 hours grooming her dogs\n#### 20"", ""original_answer"": 20.0, ""transformed_answer"": 24.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 hour wrongly has 50 minutes instead of 60 minutes, resulting in 1200/60 = 20 hours in the original_solution becoming 1200/50 = 24 hours in the transformed_solution. The previous steps 1 and 2, which are not related to unit conversion of minutes to hours, remain correct and unchanged."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c597ec46e43c968f,full,calculation_error,"In a manufacturing plant, it takes 36 machines 4 hours of continuous work to fill 4 standard orders. At this rate, how many hours of continuous work by 72 machines are required to fill 12 standard orders?","It takes 36 machines 4 hours to fill 4 standard orders, so it takes 36 x 4 = 144 machine-hours to fill 4 standard orders.
To fill 12 standard orders, it will take 144 x (12/4) = 144 x 3 = 442 machine-hours.
