#### 6.14",Makes an arithmetic error when scaling a quantity by a ratio,144 x (12/4) = 144 x 3 = 442 machine-hours,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""It takes 36 machines 4 hours to fill 4 standard orders, so it takes 36 x 4 = 144 machine-hours to fill 4 standard orders.\nTo fill 12 standard orders, it will take 144 x (12/4) = 144 x 3 = 432 machine-hours.\n72 machines working together will take 432 / 72 = 6 hours to fill 12 standard orders.\n#### 6"", ""original_answer"": 6.0, ""transformed_answer"": 6.14, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""In this example, there is an intentional miscalculation in step 2 where 144 x 3 was incorrectly calculated as 442 instead of 432. This affected the last step, where it falsely states that 442 machine-hours worked by 72 machines would take 6.14 hours to complete rather than the correct 6 hours. The earlier step calculating the machine-hours needed for 4 standard orders is unaffected, so it remains the same as in the original solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c598258af90c9c89,full,referencing_context_value_error,"If a train, traveling at a speed of 360 kmph, crosses a pole in 5 sec, then the length of the train is?","First, convert the speed from km/h to m/s: 350 km/h * (1000 m/1 km) * (1 h/3600 s) = 97.22 m/s
