Therefore, √ 6 ¤ √ 6 = 0 - 24 = -24
#### -24",Interchanges the squared sum and squared difference,"So ( x - y ) ^ 2 = (2√6) ^ 2 = 24
And ( x + y ) ^ 2 = 0",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x = √6 and y = √6\nThen x + y = √6 + √6 = 2√6\nAnd x - y = √6 - √6 = 0\nSo ( x + y ) ^ 2 = (2√6) ^ 2 = 24\nAnd ( x - y ) ^ 2 = 0\nTherefore, √ 6 ¤ √ 6 = 24 - 0 = 24\n#### 24"", ""original_answer"": 24.0, ""transformed_answer"": -24.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""This example switches the operators of the exponents in steps 4 and 5 by changing ( x + y ) ^ 2 to ( x - y ) ^ 2 and vice versa. The new calculations correctly apply the changes in operators but lead to an incorrect overall result. The transformed_solution results in a value of -24 instead of 24, affecting the outcome of the expression where √ 6 ¤ √ 6 results in -24 - 0 = -24. The calculation within each step is performed correctly, but due to the switched operators, the outcome differs from the original solution."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
