(3) # 3 = (3) ^ 2 / 3 = 9 / 3 = 3
#### 3",Uses multiplication instead of division in the defined operation,(-1 # 3) = (-1 ^ 2 * 3) = 3,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,defined,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""(-1 # 3) = (-1 ^ 2 / 3) = 1 / 3\n(1 / 3) # 3 = (1 / 3) ^ 2 / 3 = 1 / 9\n#### 1 / 9"", ""original_answer"": ""1 / 9"", ""transformed_answer"": ""3"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""The transformation changes the division operator to multiplication in the first use of the # operator, specifically changing (-1 ^ 2 / 3) to (-1 ^ 2 * 3), resulting in a value of 3 instead of 1 / 3. The subsequent step properly inherits the outcome of this transformed operation and calculates the square of 3 divided by 3 correctly as 3, which is reflected in the transformed answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c6660b5e490c9ea0,full,operator_error,Suppose 8 monkeys take 8 minutes to eat 8 bananas. How many minutes would it take 3 monkeys to eat 3 bananas?,"It takes 8 minutes for 8 monkeys to eat 8 bananas because they eat 1 banana per monkey per minute.
