#### 165",Adds an unmentioned quantity to the calculation,Because Naomi also needs to wash a delicate blouse which takes the same amount of time as the clothes,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The clothes take 30 minutes to wash and the towels take twice as long, 30 x 2 = 60 minutes to wash the towels.\nThe sheets take 15 minutes less than the towels, 60 - 15 = 45 minutes to wash the sheets.\nIt takes 30 minutes + 60 minutes + 45 minutes = 135 minutes to wash everything.\n#### 135"", ""original_answer"": 135.0, ""transformed_answer"": 165.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because Naomi also needs to wash a delicate blouse which takes the same amount of time as the clothes>, resulting in step 3 changing from 30 minutes + 60 minutes + 45 minutes = 135 minutes in the original_solution to 30 minutes for clothes + 30 minutes for the delicate blouse + 60 minutes for towels + 45 minutes for sheets = 165 minutes in the transformed_solution. The transformed solution now includes an extra laundry item, therefore altering the final calculation. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c67877297a1eb707,full,calculation_error,"Wink, Inc. follows a certain procedure that requires two tasks to be finished independently in order for a job to be done. On any given day, there is a 2/3 probability that task 1 will be completed on time, and a 3/5 probability that task 2 will be completed on time. On a certain day, what is the probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not?","The probability that task 1 will be completed on time is 2/3.
The probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 3/5
The probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not is 2/3 * 3/5 = 6/15
#### 6/15",Calculates the complement of a probability incorrectly,The probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 3/5,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,probability,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The probability that task 1 will be completed on time is 2/3.\nThe probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is 1 - 3/5 = 2/5\nThe probability that task 1 will be completed on time, but task 2 will not is 2/3 * 2/5 = 4/15\n#### 4/15"", ""original_answer"": ""4/15"", ""transformed_answer"": ""6/15"", ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the error occurs at step 2, where the probability that task 2 will not be completed on time is calculated incorrectly as 3/5 instead of 2/5. This error then affects the final calculation of the probability that task 1 will be completed on time but task 2 will not, leading to a transformed probability of 6/15 instead of the original 4/15. The subsequent step related to step 2 inherits the wrong result, modifying the calculation from 2/3 * 2/5 = 4/15 to 2/3 * 3/5 = 6/15. It's important to note that the calculation within step 2 (1 - 3/5) is still correct in terms of process, but the numerical result is incorrect."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c68e5927112365ca,full,counting_error,"On the weekend, Tony will walk to the store. On weekdays, he runs to the store. When he walks, he goes 2 MPH. When he runs he goes 10 MPH. The store is 4 miles away. If he goes on Sunday, Tuesday, and Thursday, what is the average time in minutes that he spends to get to the store?","On Sunday he takes 2 hours to get there because 4 / 2 = 2
This takes him 120 minutes because 2 x 60 = 120
On Tuesday and Thursday, it takes him .4 hours to get to the store because 4 / 10 = .4
On Tuesday and Thursday, it takes him 24 minutes to get to the store because .4 x 60 = 24
In total it takes him 192 minutes to get to the store because 120 + 24 + 48 = 192
On average it takes him 64 minutes because 192 / 3 = 64
#### 64",Double-counts one trip's time when calculating the total,In total it takes him 192 minutes to get to the store because 120 + 24 + 48 = 192,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,when,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""On Sunday he takes 2 hours to get there because 4 / 2 = 2\nThis takes him 120 minutes because 2 x 60 = 120\nOn Tuesday and Thursday, it takes him .4 hours to get to the store because 4 / 10 = .4\nOn Tuesday and Thursday, it takes him 24 minutes to get to the store because .4 x 60 = 24\nIn total it takes him 168 minutes to get to the store because 120 + 24 + 24 = 168\nOn average it takes him 56 minutes because 168 / 3 = 56\n#### 56"", ""original_answer"": 56.0, ""transformed_answer"": 64.0, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Here, the wrong step (5) erroneously counts the time taken on Tuesday and Thursday as 48 minutes in total instead of 24 + 24 = 48 minutes, which should have been unchanged from the original solution. Therefore, instead of adding 120 + 24 + 24 = 168, we erroneously added 120 + 48 = 168. Consequently, the final step calculation also changed from 168 / 3 = 56 to 192 / 3 = 64, although it was performed correctly given the wrong input."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c6bec7567f1d362c,full,counting_error,"Gary's gas station serves an average of 12 cars per hour on Saturdays, 10 cars per hour on Sundays, and 9 cars per hour on all other days of the week. If the station is open from 6 a.m. to 10 p.m. every day, how many cars does Gary's station serve over the course of a typical week?","On Saturdays, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours. So, the total number of cars served on Saturdays is 16 * 12 = 192 cars
On Sundays, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours. So, the total number of cars served on Sundays is 16 * 10 = 160 cars
On the other days, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours each. So, the total number of cars served on other days is 16 * 9 * 4 = 576 cars
So, the total number of cars served in a week is 192 + 160 + 576 = 928 cars
#### 928",Counts one fewer day than required when aggregating weekly totals,16 * 9 * 4 = 576 cars,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""On Saturdays, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours. So, the total number of cars served on Saturdays is 16 * 12 = 192 cars\nOn Sundays, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours. So, the total number of cars served on Sundays is 16 * 10 = 160 cars\nOn the other days, the station is open for (10-6) + (22-10) = 16 hours each. So, the total number of cars served on other days is 16 * 9 * 5 = 720 cars\nSo, the total number of cars served in a week is 192 + 160 + 720 = 1072 cars\n#### 1072"", ""original_answer"": 1072, ""transformed_answer"": 928, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""In this transformed_solution, the mistakenly counted number of other days of the week has been changed from 5 to 4, which affects the total number served on those days, changing from 16 * 9 * 5 = 720 cars to 16 * 9 * 4 = 576 cars. The final step was also affected, changing the sum from 192 + 160 + 720 = 1072 cars to 192 + 160 + 576 = 928 cars. The transformed_answer differs from the original_answer due to the counting error, and previous steps have not been altered."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c6f0c968d4641bcd,full,unit_conversion_error,"Abel leaves for a vacation destination 1000 miles away driving 50 miles per hour. An hour later Alice leaves from the same point for the same destination, traveling 40 miles per hour. How much earlier does Abel reach the destination in minutes??","If Abel needs to travel 1000 miles going 50 miles per hour, this means it will take him 1000/50=20 hours to get there.
If Alice needs to travel 1000 miles going 40 miles per hour, this means it will take her 1000/40=25 hours to get there.
Since there are 50 minutes in an hour, this means it will take Abel 20*50= 1000 minutes to arrive.
Similarly, this means it will take Alice 25*50= 1250 minutes to arrive.
This means Abel arrives 1250-1000= 250 minutes before Alice if they both leave simultaneously.
However, since Abel had a head start of 1 hour, which is 50 minutes, this means Abel arrives 250 + 50 = 300 minutes ahead of Alice
#### 300",Uses 50 minutes per hour instead of 60 when converting time units,Since there are 50 minutes in an hour,ok,ok,,10,False,False,True,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If Abel needs to travel 1000 miles going 50 miles per hour, this means it will take him 1000/50=20 hours to get there.\nIf Alice needs to travel 1000 miles going 40 miles per hour, this means it will take her 1000/40=25 hours to get there.\nSince there are 60 minutes in an hour, this means it will take Abel 20*60= 1200 minutes to arrive.\nSimilarly, this means it will take Alice 25*60= 1500 minutes to arrive.\nThis means Abel arrives 1500-1200= 300 minutes before Alice if they both leave simultaneously.\nHowever, since Abel had a head start of 1 hour, which is 60 minutes, this means Abel arrives 300 + 60 = 360 minutes ahead of Alice\n#### 360"", ""original_answer"": 360.0, ""transformed_answer"": 300.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 and 4 make incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 hour is wrongly equated to 50 minutes instead of 60 minutes, resulting in 20*60= 1200 minutes and 25*60= 1500 minutes in the original_solution becoming 20*50= 1000 minutes and 25*50= 1250 minutes in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent related steps 5 and 6, which changes from 1500-1200= 300 minutes to 1250-1000= 250 minutes and from 300 + 60 = 360 minutes to 250 + 50 = 300 minutes. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of unit conversion error, so the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c70cebfcc0ff1277,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,A factory produces 90 refrigerators per hour. It also produces 70 more coolers than refrigerators per hour. How many products did the factory produce for 5 days if it works 9 hours a day?,"The factory produces 90 + 70 = 160 coolers per hour.
The factory works 5 * 9 = 45 hours in 5 days.
The factory produces ( 90 + 150) * 45 = 10800 products for 5 days.
#### 10800",Uses an incorrect previously calculated quantity in a later calculation,The factory produces ( 90 + 150) * 45 = 10800 products for 5 days.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The factory produces 90 + 70 = 160 coolers per hour.\nThe factory works 5 * 9 = 45 hours in 5 days.\nThe factory produces ( 90 + 160) * 45 = 11250 products for 5 days.\n#### 11250"", ""original_answer"": 11250.0, ""transformed_answer"": 10800.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 mistakenly references 160 as 150 from step 1 and changes (90 + 160) * 45 = 11250 to (90 + 150) * 45 = 10800. It should be noted that step 1 in the transformed_solution <The factory produces 90 + 70 = 160 coolers per hour.> should be the same as the step 1 in the original_solution <The factory produces 90 + 70 = 160 coolers per hour.> and calculates its result 160 correctly. Step 3 is the only error, maintaining the correct calculation of the number of hours worked in step 2 as 45. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all other steps is still correct, and the steps that come after the wrong step take into account the erroneous value generated by the wrong step."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c70f5375da188bca,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"Boris has 24 books and he donates a fourth of his books to the library. Cameron has 30 books and he donates a third of his books to the library. After donating their books, how many books in total do Boris and Cameron have together?","Boris donates 24 / 4 = 6 books
Then Boris has a total of 24 - 6 = 18 books
Because Boris found 2 more books at home, he then has a total of 18 + 2 = 20 books
Cameron donates 30 / 3 = 10 books
Then Cameron has a total of 30 - 10 = 20 books
Altogether, Boris and Cameron have 20 + 20 = 40 books
#### 40",Adds an unstated quantity to the calculation,"Because Boris found 2 more books at home, he then has a total of 18 + 2 = 20 books",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""Boris donates 24 / 4 = 6 books\nThen Boris has a total of 24 - 6 = 18 books\nCameron donates 30 / 3 = 10 books\nThen Cameron has a total of 30 - 10 = 20 books\nAltogether, Boris and Cameron have 18 + 20 = 38 books\n#### 38"", ""original_answer"": 38.0, ""transformed_answer"": 40.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Step 2 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Because Boris found 2 more books at home>, resulting in step 2 changing from 24 - 6 = 18 books in the original_solution to 18 + 2 = 20 books in the transformed_solution. This error subsequently affects the final tally of books, changing from 18 + 20 = 38 books to 20 + 20 = 40 books. It should be noted that you only need to consider one error of adding additional information in one step, and the other calculation processes should be correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c736334ab946cfc4,full,counting_error,A library has an average of 150 visitors on Sundays and 120 on other days. The average number of visitors per day in a month of 30 days beginning with a Sunday is?,"Total visitors on Sundays = 150 * 4 = 600 visitors
Total visitors on other days = 120 * 26 = 3120 visitors
Total visitors in a month = 600 + 3120 = 3720 visitors
The average number of visitors per day in a month of 30 days is 3720 / 30 = 124 visitors
#### 124",Miscounts the number of days in each category,Total visitors on Sundays = 150 * 4 = 600 visitors,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Total visitors on Sundays = 150 * 5 = 750 visitors\nTotal visitors on other days = 120 * 25 = 3000 visitors\nTotal visitors in a month = 750 + 3000 = 3750 visitors\nThe average number of visitors per day in a month of 30 days is 3750 / 30 = 125 visitors\n#### 125"", ""original_answer"": 125, ""transformed_answer"": 124, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 mistakenly counts Sundays as 4 days instead of 5 days, leading to the change from 150 * 5 = 750 visitors to 150 * 4 = 600 visitors. As a result of this change, total visitors on other days have been recalculated from 120 * 25 = 3000 visitors to 120 * 26 = 3120 visitors to account for the extra non-Sunday day. This affects the subsequent steps, changing the total visitors in a month from 3750 to 3720 and the average number of visitors per day from 125 to 124. The previous steps and unrelated calculations remain accurate, in alignment with the constraints given."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c7557d01eb336677,full,operator_error,"In a company of 148 employees, 92 are females. A total of 78 employees have advanced degrees and the rest have a college degree only. If 31 employees are males with a college degree only, how many employees are females with advanced degrees?","There are 148 - 92 = 56 male employees.
There are 56 + 31 = 87 male employees with advanced degrees.
There are 78 - 87 = -9 female employees with advanced degrees.
#### -9",Adds a subgroup to its total instead of subtracting it,There are 56 + 31 = 87 male employees with advanced degrees.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""There are 148 - 92 = 56 male employees.\nThere are 56 - 31 = 25 male employees with advanced degrees.\nThere are 78 - 25 = 53 female employees with advanced degrees.\n#### 53"", ""original_answer"": 53.0, ""transformed_answer"": -9.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""The example changes the subtraction in step 2 to an addition, thus we change 56 - 31 = 25 to 56 + 31 = 87. This is the first step we modify, which then affects the logical flow of the problem since there cannot be a negative number of female employees with advanced degrees. Steps 1 and 3's calculations are correct based on the modified step 2, but the final answer is logically invalid due to the operator change creating an erroneous situation."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c78edc031cc2efb9,full,confusing_formula_error,"If the area of a triangle with base 6 cm is equal to the area of a square with side 6 cm, then the altitude of the triangle is","The area of the square is 6+6+6+6=24 square cm
The area of the triangle is (1/2)*6*h, where h is the altitude. So (1/2)*6*h=24
(1/2)*6*h=24
3h=24
h=8 cm
#### 8",Confuses a square’s perimeter with its area,The area of the square is 6+6+6+6=24 square cm,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,with,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The area of the square is 6*6=36 square cm\nThe area of the triangle is (1/2)*6*h, where h is the altitude. So (1/2)*6*h=36\n(1/2)*6*h=36\n3h=36\nh=12 cm\n#### 12"", ""original_answer"": 12.0, ""transformed_answer"": 8.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 confuses the area and perimeter of the square. The question requires that we find the area of the square, which should be equal to side length multiplied by side length, but the perimeter is calculated instead by summing all four sides, resulting in 6*6=36 square cm in the original_solution being changed to 6+6+6+6=24 square cm in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent related steps, changing the area of the triangle equation from (1/2)*6*h=36 to (1/2)*6*h=24 and ultimately changing the solution from h=12 cm to h=8 cm. Note that the language description of step 1 < The area of the square is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. It should be also noted that only one step of confusing formula error is considered, and the other calculation processes are still correct. In this example, only step 1 mistakenly uses the perimeter formula for the area of the square, while the other calculation processes that depend on this area value are adjusted accordingly but still correctly performed."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c7901966a3a68089,full,unit_conversion_error,"a train covers a distance of 12 km in 10 minutes. if it takes 9 seconds to pass a telegraph post, then the length of the train is","First, convert 10 minutes to seconds: 10 minutes * 50 seconds/minute = 500 seconds
Now calculate the speed of the train: 12 km / 500 seconds = 0.024 km/second
Convert 0.024 km/second to meters/second: 0.024 km/second * 1000 meters/km = 24 meters/second
Now use the formula: length = speed * time
Length of the train = 24 meters/second * 9 seconds = 216 meters
#### 216",Uses an incorrect minutes-to-seconds conversion factor,10 minutes * 50 seconds/minute = 500 seconds,ok,ok,,6,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""First, convert 10 minutes to seconds: 10 minutes * 60 seconds/minute = 600 seconds\nNow calculate the speed of the train: 12 km / 600 seconds = 0.02 km/second\nConvert 0.02 km/second to meters/second: 0.02 km/second * 1000 meters/km = 20 meters/second\nNow use the formula: length = speed * time\nLength of the train = 20 meters/second * 9 seconds = 180 meters\n#### 180"", ""original_answer"": 180.0, ""transformed_answer"": 216.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 minute is wrongly being converted to 50 seconds instead of 60 seconds, resulting in 10 minutes * 60 seconds/minute = 600 seconds in the original_solution becoming 10 minutes * 50 seconds/minute = 500 seconds in the transformed_solution. This error affects the subsequent related steps. Step 2 changes from 12 km / 600 seconds = 0.02 km/second to 12 km / 500 seconds = 0.024 km/second. Step 3 changes from 0.02 km/second * 1000 meters/km = 20 meters/second to 0.024 km/second * 1000 meters/km = 24 meters/second. Step 4 remains logically correct in structure, calculating the length as speed times time, with the modified values resulting in 24 meters/second * 9 seconds = 216 meters. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of unit conversion error, so the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c7f378f93f0e8429,full,unit_conversion_error,"Boston had .5 feet of snow on the first day of winter. The next day they got an additional 8 inches. Over the next 2 days, 2 inches of the snow melted. On the fifth day, they received another 2 times the amount of snow they received on the first day. How many feet of snow do they now have?","10 inches is 1 foot and they received a .5 foot of snow on the first day so they received 10*.5 = 5 inches of snow
The first day they had 5 inches and then received another 8 inches for a total of 5+8 = 13 inches
2 inches melted from their 13 inches so that leaves 13-2 = 11 inches of snow
They received 2 times the amount as the first day's 5 inches of snow so that's 2*5 = 10 inches of snow
So they had 11 inches of snow and received another 10 inches of snow for a total of 11+10 = 21 inches
10 inches is 1 foot and they have 21 inches of snow so they have 21/10 = 2.1 feet of snow
#### 2.1",Uses an incorrect conversion factor between inches and feet,10 inches is 1 foot,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,"feet, inches",True,2,"{""original_solution"": ""12 inches is 1 foot and they received a .5 foot of snow on the first day so they received 12*.5 = 6 inches of snow\nThe first day they had 6 inches and then received another 8 inches for a total of 6+8 = 14 inches\n2 inches melted from their 14 inches so that leaves 14-2 = 12 inches of snow\nThey received 2 times the amount as the first day's 6 inches of snow so that's 2*6 = 12 inches of snow\nSo they had 12 inches of snow and received another 12 inches of snow for a total of 12+12 = 24 inches\n12 inches is 1 foot and they have 24 inches of snow so they have 24/12 = 2 feet of snow\n#### 2"", ""original_answer"": 2.0, ""transformed_answer"": 2.1, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 foot is wrongly equal to 10 inches instead of 12 inches, resulting in 12*.5 = 6 inches of snow in the original_solution becoming 10*.5 = 5 inches of snow in the transformed_solution. And it affects the subsequent related steps 2, 3, 4, and 5, which changes the intermediate values from 14 inches to 13 inches, from 12 inches to 11 inches, and from 24 inches to 21 inches, respectively. The final result changes from 2 feet of snow to 2.1 feet of snow in the last step. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of unit conversion error, and the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:c7fed42f99fdc6fa,full,calculation_error,"a train 630 m long, running with a speed of 63 km / hr will pass a tree in ?","First convert the speed from km/hr to m/s: 63 km/hr * (1000 m / 1 km) * (1 hr / 3600 s) = 63000 / 3600 = 175/10 = 15 m/s
