#### 42",Makes an arithmetic error when simplifying the converted speed.,63000 / 3600 = 175/10 = 15 m/s,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""First convert the speed from km/hr to m/s: 63 km/hr * (1000 m / 1 km) * (1 hr / 3600 s) = 63000 / 3600 = 175/10 = 17.5 m/s\nCalculate the time it takes to pass the tree using the formula time = distance / speed: 630 m / 17.5 m/s = 36 s\n#### 36"", ""original_answer"": 36.0, ""transformed_answer"": 42.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""This example mistakenly calculates the conversion from km/hr to m/s as 15 m/s instead of the accurate conversion, which is 17.5 m/s. This error in step 1 affects the step when calculating the time it takes to pass the tree. The original time calculation of 630 m / 17.5 m/s = 36 s is altered to 630 m / 15 m/s = 42 s due to the incorrect conversion rate in step 1."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:c80ff316982fffe8,full,adding_irrelevant_information,Kat decides she wants to start a boxing career. She gets a gym membership and spends 1 hour in the gym 3 times a week doing strength training. She also trained at the boxing gym 4 times a week for 1.5 hours. How many hours a week does she train?,"She strength trains 3*1=3 hours a week
Because Kat also spends an additional 0.5 hours on stretching after each strength training, her total strength training time is 3+(3*0.5)=4.5 hours a week
