#### 93.33",Subtracts an incorrect water amount from the total mass,The weight of dry grapes in 20 kgs of raisins is 20 - 6 = 14 kgs,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,water,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let x be the weight of fresh grapes needed to get 20 kgs of raisins\nThe weight of water in x kgs of fresh grapes is 0.85x\nThe weight of dry grapes in x kgs of fresh grapes is x - 0.85x = 0.15x\nThe weight of water in 20 kgs of raisins is 0.25 x 20 = 5 kgs\nThe weight of dry grapes in 20 kgs of raisins is 20 - 5 = 15 kgs\n0.15x = 15\nx = 15 / 0.15\nx = 100\n#### 100"", ""original_answer"": 100.0, ""transformed_answer"": 93.33, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Step 5 mistakenly references 5 as 6 from step 4 and changes 20 - 5 = 15 kgs to 20 - 6 = 14 kgs. It should be noted that step 4 in the transformed_solution <The weight of water in 20 kgs of raisins is 0.25 x 20 = 5 kgs> should be the same as the step 4 in the original_solution <The weight of water in 20 kgs of raisins is 0.25 x 20 = 5 kgs> and calculates its result 5 correctly. Furthermore, the language description of step 5 has also changed from <The weight of dry grapes in 20 kgs of raisins is 20 - 5 = 15 kgs> to <The weight of dry grapes in 20 kgs of raisins is 20 - 6 = 14 kgs>. Step 5 affects the subsequent step 6 and 7 related to it. Step 6 changes from 0.15x = 15 to 0.15x = 14 and step 7 changes from x = 15 / 0.15 to x = 14 / 0.15. You need to only consider one error of referencing, so the calculation of all steps is still correct, hence transformed solution ends with x = 93.33."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_previous_step_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
