Together is takes him 60+180 = 240 minutes to dry all of the dogs
50 minutes are in 1 hour and he spends 240 minutes on the dogs so he worked for 240/50 = 4.8 hours drying the dogs
#### 4.8",Uses an incorrect number of minutes per hour when converting units,50 minutes are in 1 hour,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""It takes 10 minutes to dry the coat of a short-haired dog and twice as long for a full haired dog so they take 10*2 = 20 minutes to dry\nHe had 6 short hair dogs and they took 10 minutes to dry each so they took 6*10= 60 minutes to dry\nHe had 9 full haired dogs that took 20 minutes to dry each so they took 9*20 = 180 minutes to dry\nTogether is takes him 60+180 = 240 minutes to dry all of the dogs\n60 minutes are in 1 hour and he spends 240 minutes on the dogs so he worked for 240/60 = 4 hours drying the dogs\n#### 4"", ""original_answer"": 4.0, ""transformed_answer"": 4.8, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 5 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 hour is wrongly equal to 50 minutes instead of 60 minutes, resulting in 240/60 = 4 hours in the original_solution becoming 240/50 = 4.8 hours in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent related step which changes the total hours worked from 4 to 4.8. It should be noted that you only need to consider one step of unit conversion error, so the calculation processes of drying the dogs remain correct and are unaffected by this error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:cda8fa258bdfdeeb,full,referencing_previous_step_value_error,"There is a train and car. The ratio between the speed of a train and a car is 16:15 respectively. Also, a bus covered a distance of 480 km in 8 h. The speed of the bus is 3/4 of the speed of the train. How much distance will the car cover in 6 h?","Let the speed of the car be 15x and the speed of the train be 16x.
