#### 326",Uses an incorrect given value when converting the speed,70 km/h * (1000 m/km) * (1 h/3600 s) = 19.44 m/s,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""First, convert the speed from km/h to m/s: 72 km/h * (1000 m/km) * (1 h/3600 s) = 20 m/s\nNext, find the distance covered by the train in 25 sec: 25 s * 20 m/s = 500 m\nThen, subtract the length of the train to get the length of the platform: 500 m - 160 m = 340 m\n#### 340"", ""original_answer"": 340.0, ""transformed_answer"": 326.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references 72 in the question as 70 wrongly, and calculates 70 km/h * (1000 m/km) * (1 h/3600 s) = 19.44 m/s instead of 72 km/h * (1000 m/km) * (1 h/3600 s) = 20 m/s. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating 25 s * 19.44 m/s = 486 m instead of 25 s * 20 m/s = 500 m in step 2. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 3 still references 160 m correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:d7e4f7aa1e38fc91,full,unit_conversion_error,A man crosses a 600 m long street in 5 minutes. What is his speed in km per hour?,"First, let's convert the distance from meters to kilometers. 600 meters = 0.6 kilometers.
