eic,eic:db18709d5a04dadd,full,counting_error,Emily wants to know how much it rained last week. She sees that it rained 2 inches on Monday morning and 1 more inch later that day. It rained twice that much on Tuesday. It did not rain on Wednesday but on Thursday it rained 1 inch. The biggest storm was on Friday when the total was equal to Monday through Thursday combined. What was the daily average rain total for the week?,"The total rain was 2 inches + 1 inches = 3 inches on Monday.
The total rain was 2 * 3 inches = 6 inches on Tuesday.
The total rain was 0 inches + 1 inch = 1 inch across Wednesday and Thursday.
The total rain was 3 inches + 6 inches + 1 inch = 10 inches on Friday.
There were 3 inches + 6 inches + 1 inch + 10 inches = 20 inches total from Monday to Thursday.
20 inches/4 days = 5 inches average daily rain.
#### 5",Uses the wrong number of days when calculating the weekly average,20 inches/4 days = 5 inches average daily rain.,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,when,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total rain was 2 inches + 1 inches = 3 inches on Monday.\nThe total rain was 2 * 3 inches = 6 inches on Tuesday.\nThe total rain was 0 inches + 1 inch = 1 inch across Wednesday and Thursday.\nThe total rain was 3 inches + 6 inches + 1 inch = 10 inches on Friday.\nThere were 3 inches + 6 inches + 1 inch + 10 inches = 20 inches total last week.\n20 inches/5 days = 4 inches average daily rain.\n#### 4"", ""original_answer"": 4, ""transformed_answer"": 5, ""wrong_step"": 5, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 5 incorrectly counts the number of days. In the transformed_solution, the divisor has been mistakenly changed from 5 days to 4 days (Monday to Thursday), excluding Friday. This incorrect counting affects step 6, changing the average daily rain calculation from 20/5=4 inches to 20/4=5 inches, thus leading to a different transformed_answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
