#### 11",Uses an incorrect number of occurrences when multiplying a daily duration,Josh practices soccer 2 hours x 4 days = 8 hours.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Josh practices soccer 2 hours x 3 days = 6 hours.\nHe practices band 1.5 hours x 2 days = 3 hours.\nFrom Monday to Friday, on extracurricular activities, Josh spends 6 + 3 = 9 hours.\n#### 9"", ""original_answer"": 9.0, ""transformed_answer"": 11.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed_solution, step 1 incorrectly counts soccer practice as happening for 4 days (Monday, Wednesday, Friday, and one additional incorrect day) instead of 3 days, resulting in 2 hours x 4 days = 8 hours instead of the correct 2 hours x 3 days = 6 hours. This error affects the final step as well, changing the total number of hours Josh spends from 9 to 11 hours. The counting result in this step is the only error, and the rest of the calculation is correctly performed based on this mistake."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:df60d50fdf974883,full,calculation_error,"A convenience store sold 100 bags of chips in a month. In the first week, 15 bags of chips were sold. In the second week, thrice as many bags of chips were sold. There was an equal number of chips sold in the third and fourth week. How many chips was each sold in the third and fourth week?","In the second week, 15 x 3 = 45 bags of chips were sold.
So there was a total of 45 + 15 = 60 bags of chips sold on the first and second week.
Thus, a total of 100 - 60 = 50 bags of chips were sold on the third and fourth week.
