#### 25",Makes an arithmetic error when subtracting the known total from the overall total,"Thus, a total of 100 - 60 = 50 bags of chips were sold",ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""In the second week, 15 x 3 = 45 bags of chips were sold.\nSo there was a total of 45 + 15 = 60 bags of chips sold on the first and second week.\nThus, a total of 100 - 60 = 40 bags of chips were sold on the third and fourth week.\nTherefore, 40/2 = 20 bags of chips were each sold on the third and fourth week.\n#### 20"", ""original_answer"": 20.0, ""transformed_answer"": 25.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""This example mistakenly calculates 100 - 60 as 50 instead of 100 - 60 as 40 in step 3, which affects the subsequent step 4 related to it. Step 4 then inherits the error from step 3, not only modifying the formula 40/2 to 50/2 but also modifying the language description from <40 bags of chips were sold on the third and fourth week> to <50 bags of chips were sold on the third and fourth week>. The result of the calculation in the subsequent related step 4 changes to 25 bags of chips each on the third and fourth week from the initial 20 bags of chips each, due to the propagated error from the wrong step 3. The previous steps 1 and 2 remain unchanged as they are not affected by this error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
