#### 120",Misreads the given total amount when calculating the unit rate,Ella earned $30 / 3 hours of dog walking = $10 per hour.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Ella earned $33 / 3 hours of dog walking = $11 per hour.\nSo for 12 hours of dog walking, Ella would earn $11 x 12 = $132.\n#### 132"", ""original_answer"": 132.0, ""transformed_answer"": 120.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references $33 in the question as $30 wrongly, and calculates $30 / 3 hours of dog walking = $10 per hour instead of $33 / 3 = $11 per hour. Its subsequent related step will be affected, calculating $10 x 12 = $120 instead of $11 x 12 = $132 in step 2. Please note that you should only consider one error, so step 2 still references 12 in the question correctly."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:e0189c3208cb8ced,full,calculation_error,"An avant-garde sushi house sells jellyfish for a certain amount and eel for nine times that amount. If the combined cost of one order each kind of sushi is $200, how much does the eel cost?","Let j be the cost of the jellyfish and e be the cost of the eel. We know that j + e = $200 and e = 9j.
