#### 32",Divides successive percentage factors instead of multiplying them,100 - ((100 - 20) / (100 - 10) * 100) = 32,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total decrease percentage is 28% because 100 - ((100 - 20) * (100 - 10) / 100) = 28\n#### 28"", ""original_answer"": 28.0, ""transformed_answer"": 32.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the division in step 1 was transformed into a multiplication, so instead of dividing by the percentage after the second decrease, it multiplies, which leads to an incorrect percentage decrease calculation. Specifically, ((100 - 20) * (100 - 10) / 100) was changed to ((100 - 20) / (100 - 10) * 100). The calculation of the result is then carried out correctly, but since it's based on the wrong operator, the final transformed_answer is incorrect while being different from the original_answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:e376ee43ae1b87a9,full,counting_error,"A factory produces 6400 toys per week. If the workers at this factory work 3 days a week and if these workers make the same number of toys everyday, how many toys are produced each day?","The total number of toys produced per week is 6400
