#### 23.2",Adds an extra hour when converting hours and minutes to total hours,"So, x/25 + x/4 = 6 + 48/60",ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the distance between the village and the post-office be x km.\nTime taken to go from village to post-office = x/25 hours\nTime taken to return from post-office to village = x/4 hours\nTotal time is given as 5 hours 48 minutes or 5 + 48/60 hours.\nSo, x/25 + x/4 = 5 + 48/60\nSolving for x gives x = 20 km.\n#### 20"", ""original_answer"": 20.0, ""transformed_answer"": 23.2, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 4 makes an incorrect unit conversion by considering the total time to be 6 + 48/60 hours instead of the correct time, which is 5 + 48/60 hours. This mistake in unit conversion leads to an incorrect total time and thus affects the equation in step 5, leading to the wrong solution for x. The correct calculation steps for the original solution are still maintained for the rest of the problem-solving process."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
