#### 60",Uses an incorrect conversion factor when converting hours to minutes,1.2 hours * 50 minutes/hour = 60 minutes.,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,7,"{""original_solution"": ""First, calculate the combined speed at which they are approaching each other by adding their individual speeds: 460 km/h + 525 km/h = 985 km/h.\nThen, divide the initial distance by the combined speed to find the time it takes for them to meet: 1182 km ÷ 985 km/h = 1.2 hours.\nFinally, convert 1.2 hours to minutes by multiplying by 60: 1.2 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 72 minutes.\n#### 72"", ""original_answer"": 72.0, ""transformed_answer"": 60.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 makes incorrect unit conversion, which means 1 hour is wrongly equated to having 50 minutes instead of 60 minutes, resulting in 1.2 hours * 60 minutes/hour = 72 minutes in the original_solution becoming 1.2 hours * 50 minutes/hour = 60 minutes in the transformed_solution. It affects the final calculation of the time in minutes, without affecting the previous steps of speed calculation and time in hours."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""unit_conversion_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:e7c570d93e119110,full,missing_step,"Sarah is driving to the airport. After driving at 50 miles per hour for one hour, she realizes that if she continues at that same average rate she will be an hour late for her flight. She then travels 100 miles per hour for the rest of the trip, and arrives 30 minutes before her flight departs. How many miles did she drive in all?","She drove 150 miles in the second part of the trip because (1 + 1/2) x 100 = 150
