#### 25",Adds side lengths instead of multiplying them to calculate area,So the area the picture covers is 5.5+7+5.5+7=25 square inches,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The inner area of the paper is 8.5-2*1.5=5.5 inches by 10-2*1.5=7 inches\nSo the area the picture covers is 5.5*7=38.5 square inches\n#### 38.5"", ""original_answer"": 38.5, ""transformed_answer"": 25.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 correctly calculates the dimensions of the area covered by the picture. However, step 2 confuses the area formula with the perimeter formula. Instead of multiplying the length and the width to get the area, the transformed solution incorrectly adds the length and the width, mistakenly treating it as a calculation of the perimeter. This results in 5.5*7=38.5 in the original_solution changing to 5.5+7+5.5+7=25 in the transformed_solution. This affects the answer, changing it from 38.5 square inches to just 25 square inches. The language description of step 2 < So the area the picture covers is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. The other steps in the calculation are unaffected by this error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:eb0acb1f4ea23721,full,counting_error,"Jason sent 220 text messages on Monday, half as many text messages on Tuesday, and 50 text messages each day Wednesday through Friday. How many text messages did he send on average during those five days?","First find how many text messages he sent on Tuesday: 220 messages / 2 = 110 messages
