#### 19.25",Uses an incorrect given speed when calculating travel time,Tony walks 3 miles at 4 miles per hour for 3/4=0.75 hour.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Tony walks 3 miles at 3 miles per hour for 3/3=1 hour.\nTony also runs 10 miles at 5 miles per hour for 10/5=2 hours.\nThus, each day he exercises for 1+2=3 hours.\nOver the course of one week, he exercises for 3*7=21 hours.\n#### 21"", ""original_answer"": 21.0, ""transformed_answer"": 19.25, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Step 1 references the walking speed (3 miles per hour) incorrectly as 4 miles per hour, and calculates the time to walk 3 miles as 3/4=0.75 hour instead of 3/3=1 hour. This error impacts the calculation in step 3, modifying it to 0.75+2=2.75 hours instead of 1+2=3 hours. Step 4 uses the result from the modified step 3 to multiply by 7, which leads to 2.75*7=19.25 hours instead of the correct 3*7=21 hours for the week. The steps that reference the walking speed after step 1 still use the correct speed of 3 miles per hour."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""referencing_context_value_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
