So he has 280+140=420 square feet of rooms
#### 420",Adds dimensions instead of multiplying them to calculate area,So the rooms are 15+20+15+20=70 square feet,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""He increases the length to 13+2=15 feet\nHe increases the width to 18+2=20 feet\nSo the rooms are 15*20=300 square feet\nSo he has 1+3=4 rooms of this size\nSo he has 4*300=1200 square feet of rooms this size\nHe also has one room of size 300*2=600 square feet\nSo he has 1200+600=1800 square feet of rooms\n#### 1800"", ""original_answer"": 1800.0, ""transformed_answer"": 420.0, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 3 confuses the perimeter and area of a rectangle. The question requires that the area of the rectangle to be solved be equal to the length multiplied by width, rather than the length plus length plus width plus width, which is equivalent to the perimeter of the rectangle, resulting in 15*20=300 square feet in the original_solution becoming 15+20+15+20=70 square feet in the transformed_solution. This affects the subsequent related steps, where step 5 changes from 4*300=1200 to 4*70=280, and step 6 changes from 300*2=600 to 70*2=140, and finally, step 7 changes from 1200+600=1800 to 280+140=420. Note that the language description of step 3 < So the rooms are > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. In this example, only step 3 mistakenly uses the formula of rectangular area, while the other calculation processes are based on that error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:f09eedc099687cba,full,counting_error,"A factory produces 4340 toys per week. If the workers at this factory work 2 days a week and if these workers make the same number of toys every day, how many toys are produced each day?","The total number of toys produced per week is 4340
The workers work 1 days a week
