#### 4340",Miscounts the number of days when converting a weekly total to a daily amount,The workers work 1 days a week,ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The total number of toys produced per week is 4340\nThe workers work 2 days a week\nSo, the total number of toys produced each day is 4340 / 2 = 2170\n#### 2170"", ""original_answer"": 2170, ""transformed_answer"": 4340, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""In the transformed_solution, step 2 incorrectly counts the number of workdays as 1 instead of 2. This error changes the division in step 3 from 4340 / 2 = 2170 to 4340 / 1 = 4340. Please note that only this counting error should be considered and the subsequent step is calculated correctly based on the modified counting."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:f0a6674345c940c2,full,operator_error,"John had a son James when he was 19. James is now twice as old as his sister Dora, who will turn 12 in 3 years. How old will John's youngest son, who was born when John was 32, be in 3 years?","Dora is 12+3=15
So James is 15*2=30 years old
That means John is 30+19=49
Johns youngest son is 49-32=17 years old
So he will be 17+3=20 in 3 years
#### 20",Uses a future age as the current age,"Dora is 12+3=15
So James is 15*2=30 years old",ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Dora is 12-3=9\nSo James is 9*2=18 years old\nThat means John is 18+19=37\nJohns youngest son is 37-32=5 years old\nSo he will be 5+3=8 in 3 years\n#### 8"", ""original_answer"": 8.0, ""transformed_answer"": 20.0, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""This example turns the subtraction in step 1 into addition by changing - to +, turning 12-3=9 into 12+3=15. This affects the subsequent related step 2, where now James is 15*2=30 years old instead of 9*2=18. The impact further cascades to step 3 and 4, where John now is calculated to be 30+19=49, and consequently, his youngest son is 49-32=17 years old. Step 5 inherits this result, changing the youngest son's age in 3 years from 5+3=8 to 17+3=20. It should be noted that the only incorrect thing in the solution is the operator in step 1, but the calculations carried out after the change in the operator are correct, leading to a different result from the original answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""operator_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:f0b66e1116dd087d,full,referencing_context_value_error,"A construction company is building 2 apartment buildings with 12 floors each. The apartments are almost ready to sell but all of them need doors to be completed. Each floor has 6 apartments, and each apartment needs 7 doors in total. How many doors does the company need to buy?","The number of floors is 13 floors/building x 2 buildings = 26 floors
