#### 13.75",Miscounts the number of days when calculating the average,An average of 55 people / 4 days = 13.75 people per day attended class,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""A total of 10 + 15 + 10 + 10 + 10 = 55 people attended class across the 5 days\nAn average of 55 people / 5 days = 11 people per day attended class\n#### 11"", ""original_answer"": 11.0, ""transformed_answer"": 13.75, ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""The error in step 1 is the assumption that the 5 days should be counted as 4 days, changing the correct denominator from 5 to 4 in the calculation of the average number of people attending per day. This affects the subsequent related step, causing the average to be miscomputed as 55 people / 4 days = 13.75 instead of 55 people / 5 days = 11. The calculation of the total number of people who attended during the week remains unaffected. The previous steps, which correctly summed the total number of attendees, are not influenced by this counting error."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""counting_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""GSM8K""}",,,,
eic,eic:f2c7a06b62e3a557,full,confusing_formula_error,A goat is tied to one corner of a square plot of side 12 m by a rope 7 m long. Find the area it can graze?,"The goat can graze in a quarter circle with radius 7 m (length of the rope).
The circumference of a circle is 2πr, so the circumference of a quarter circle is (1/4)*2πr.
So, the area the goat can graze is (1/4)*2π*7=11 square meters
#### 11",Uses the circumference formula instead of the area formula.,The circumference of a circle is 2πr,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""original_solution"": ""The goat can graze in a quarter circle with radius 7 m (length of the rope).\nThe area of a circle is πr^2, so the area of a quarter circle is (1/4)πr^2.\nSo, the area the goat can graze is (1/4)*π*7^2=38.5 square meters\n#### 38.5"", ""original_answer"": 38.5, ""transformed_answer"": 11.0, ""wrong_step"": 2, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 2 confuses the area and circumference of a circle. The original step should find the area of the quarter circle with the formula (1/4)πr^2 which relates to the area of a circle (πr^2), but instead, it mistakenly uses the formula (1/4)*2πr that calculates the circumference of a quarter circle, equivalent to the perimeter of the circle. The original_solution calculation is therefore altered from (1/4)*π*7^2 to (1/4)*2π*7 in the transformed_solution. This results in step 3 changing from the calculation of the quarter circle area to an incorrect calculation based on the circumference. Note that the language description of step 2 < The area of a circle is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution and that other steps are consistent with the correct formulas except for the single altered step."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:f2d3342219edf7d3,full,adding_irrelevant_information,"p is 40 % more efficient than q . p can complete a work in 24 days . if p and q work together , how many days will it take to complete the same work ?","If q is 100, p is 140 because 100 + (40% * 100) = 100 + 40 = 140
If p can complete the work in 24 days, q can complete the work in 24 x (140/100) = 33.6 days
Assuming on one of the days there is a required break for maintenance taking half a day, working together without the break, they would complete the work in 1 / (1/24 + 1/33.6) days, but with the break, it will take additional 0.5 day. So the total days are 1 / (0.04166667 + 0.0297619) + 0.5 = 1 / 0.07142857 + 0.5 = 14 + 0.5 = 14.5 days
#### 14.5",Adds an unsupported maintenance break to the calculation,Assuming on one of the days there is a required break for maintenance taking half a day,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""If q is 100, p is 140 because 100 + (40% * 100) = 100 + 40 = 140\nIf p can complete the work in 24 days, q can complete the work in 24 x (140/100) = 33.6 days\nWorking together, they can complete the work in 1 / (1/24 + 1/33.6) = 1 / (0.04166667 + 0.0297619) = 1 / 0.07142857 = 14 days\n#### 14"", ""original_answer"": 14.0, ""transformed_answer"": 14.5, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""Step 3 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Assuming on one of the days there is a required break for maintenance taking half a day>, resulting in step 3 changing from 1 / (1/24 + 1/33.6) = 14 days in the original_solution to 1 / (0.04166667 + 0.0297619) + 0.5 = 14.5 days in the transformed_solution. The additional break time was not provided in the question and directly affects the final calculation of the answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
