#### 23/32",Uses perimeter instead of area to calculate uncovered area,The fraction of the area of the floor that is not covered by the rug is (64-18)/64=46/64=23/32,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""The area of the rectangular rug is 2*7=14 square feet\nLet x be the side length of the square floor.\nThe area of the floor is x^2=64\nSo x=8 feet.\nSince the rug does not extend beyond the area of the floor, the side length of the square floor is the same as the longest side of the rectangular rug.\nThe fraction of the area of the floor that is not covered by the rug is (64-14)/64=50/64=25/32\n#### 25/32"", ""original_answer"": ""25/32"", ""transformed_answer"": ""23/32"", ""wrong_step"": 1, ""explanation"": ""Here, step 1 confuses the perimeter and area of rectangle. The question requires the area of the rectangular rug, which is normally found by multiplying length by width, but in the transformed_solution, the perimeter is calculated instead by summing the sides twice each resulting in 2+2+7+7=18. This affects the subsequent calculation of the fraction of the area that is not covered by the rug, changing from (64-14)/64 to (64-18)/64. Note that the language description of step 1 < The area of the rectangular rug is > in the original_solution remains unchanged in the transformed_solution. In this example, only step 1 mistakenly uses the formula of rectangular perimeter while the other calculation processes are still correct."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""confusing_formula_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:f96c624449ec3d8d,full,referencing_context_value_error,"If two dice are thrown together, the probability of getting an even number on one die and an odd number on the other is -","Total outcomes when two dice are thrown = 6 * 5 = 30
