Percentage of failed candidates = (1362 / 2000) x 100 = 68.1%
#### 68.1",Makes an arithmetic error when calculating a percentage of a quantity,Number of boys passed = 1100 x 32% = 1100 x 0.32 = 350,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""original_solution"": ""Number of boys = 2000 - 900 = 1100\nNumber of girls passed = 900 x 32% = 900 x 0.32 = 288\nNumber of boys passed = 1100 x 32% = 1100 x 0.32 = 352\nTotal number of candidates passed = 288 + 352 = 640\nTotal number of candidates failed = 2000 - 640 = 1360\nPercentage of failed candidates = (1360 / 2000) x 100 = 68%\n#### 68"", ""original_answer"": 68.0, ""transformed_answer"": 68.1, ""wrong_step"": 3, ""explanation"": ""In this example, the calculation 1100 x 0.32 is incorrectly transformed to 350 in step 3 instead of the correct calculation, which is 352. The mistake is made without changing any operands or operators in the formula. Subsequently, related steps 4, 5, and 6 inherit the mistake, and the numbers in the formulas inherit the error from step 3. Step 4 is modified to 288 + 350 = 638, step 5 to 2000 - 638 = 1362, and step 6 to (1362 / 2000) x 100 = 68.1%. This results in a transformed answer of 68.1%, which is different from the original answer."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""calculation_error"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:fdc8b900dce52c53,full,adding_irrelevant_information,the total marks obtained by a student in mathematics and physics is 40 and his score in chemistry is 20 marks more than that in physics . find the average marks scored in mathamatics and chemistry together .,"Let the score in physics be x
