#### 35",Adds an unsupported extra quantity to the calculation,Assuming the student also participated in an extra project which gave him an additional 10 marks in chemistry,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,8,"{""original_solution"": ""Let the score in physics be x\nThe score in mathematics is 40 - x because the total marks obtained by a student in mathematics and physics is 40\nThe score in chemistry is x + 20 because his score in chemistry is 20 marks more than that in physics\nThe average marks scored in mathematics and chemistry together is (40 - x + x + 20) / 2 = (60)/2 = 30\n#### 30"", ""original_answer"": 30.0, ""transformed_answer"": 35.0, ""wrong_step"": 4, ""explanation"": ""Step 4 adds information that is not mentioned in the question statement <Assuming the student also participated in an extra project which gave him an additional 10 marks in chemistry>, resulting in step 4 changing from (40 - x + x + 20) / 2 = (60)/2 = 30 in the original_solution to (40 - x + x + 20 + 10) / 2 = (70)/2 = 35 in the transformed_solution. The transformed solution incorrectly adds 10 marks to the chemistry score even though this additional score is not mentioned in the question. The transformed_answer is different from the original_answer due to this additional information."", ""is_single_error"": true, ""type_dir"": ""adding_irrelevant_information"", ""source_benchmark"": ""MathQA""}",,,,
eic,eic:fdf9129809e67223,full,referencing_context_value_error,"In a college the ratio of the numbers of boys to the girls is 8 : 5. if there are 120 girls, the total number of students in the college is ?","The total ratio of boys to girls is 8+5 = 13
