mathclean,mathclean:2c156872566dc0d2,full,logic error,"A farmer hires small trucks to transport his lemons to the markets. The load on a truck may not exceed 900 kilograms. If the farmer starts with 100 bags of lemons, each weighing 8 kilograms, and plans to add 10 more bags each month, how many additional kilograms can be loaded into the truck at the end of 6 months?","To solve this problem, we need to calculate the total weight of the lemons after 6 months and then determine how much additional weight the truck can carry without exceeding its maximum load of 900 kilograms.

