mathclean,mathclean:33830d6835eb263c,full,computing error,"Mary and Mike are sharing a jar of paint. Mary paints a dragon using 3 square feet of paint. Mike paints a castle using 2 square feet more paint than Mary used on her dragon. They then decide to paint a series of smaller suns, each using 1 square foot less paint than the previous one, starting with a sun that uses 4 square feet of paint. If there was originally enough paint in the jar to cover 13 square feet, how many suns can they paint before running out of paint?","To solve this problem, we need to follow these steps:

