If \( a + b + c + d \) must be a multiple of 3, find the smallest possible value of \( |a| + |b| + |c| + |d| \).","To solve the given problem, we start by examining the matrix equation \(\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 7 & 0 \\ 0 & 7 \end{pmatrix}\).

