mathclean,mathclean:66ad6f33c1b6528d,full,computing error,"School coaches decided to upgrade their sports equipment. Coach A started by buying ten new basketballs for $29 each. Each quarter, Coach A buys two more basketballs at a 10% discount off the original price. Coach B, on the other hand, bought 14 new baseballs for $2.50 each and a baseball bat for $18 at the beginning of the year. In addition, Coach B buys a new baseball bat every three months at a 15% discount off the original price. How much more did Coach A spend than Coach B over the year?","To solve this problem, we will break it down into smaller steps and calculate the total expenses for each coach over the year. Here's the step-by-step breakdown:

