mathclean,mathclean:8351714360a1cde0,full,expression error,"Keaton climbed a 30-foot ladder 20 times while working at a construction site. Reece, also working at the same site, climbed a ladder 5 feet taller than Keaton's ladder 10 times. If both workers then climbed a 25-foot ladder 15 times each, what is the total length of the ladders that both workers climbed, in inches?","To determine the total length of the ladders that both workers climbed, we need to calculate the total length of ladders each worker climbed and then sum these two totals. We will follow these steps:

