To start, let's recall the angle sum and difference formulas for sine and cosine:

\[ \sin (a + b) = \sin a \cos b + \sin b \cos a, \]
\[ \sin (a - b) = \sin a \cos b - \sin b \cos a, \]
\[ \cos (a + b) = \cos a \cos b - \sin a \sin b, \]
\[ \cos (a - b) = \cos a \cos b + \sin a \sin b. \]

We can use these formulas to expand the right-hand side of the given equation:

