mathclean,mathclean:8d36aa633bf73573,full,logic error,"Lucy has been experimenting with baking and wants to ensure she always has enough flour for her recipes. At the start of the month, she had a 1000g bag of flour. She used 350g to make bread on the first week, and then spilled 1/3 of what was left while trying to transfer the flour to a new container. If Lucy wants to have at least 700g of flour in the cupboard by the end of the month, how much more flour does she need to buy, in grams?","To solve this problem step by step, let's break it down into several parts.

