So, \( b = -\left(-\frac{2}{3}\right) = \frac{2}{3} \).

2. The coefficient of \( x \) is \( \frac{1}{r_1r_2} + \frac{1}{r_2r_3} + \frac{1}{r_3r_1} \):
\[ \frac{1}{r_1r_2} + \frac{1}{r_2r_3} + \frac{1}{r_3r_1} = \frac{r_1 + r_2 + r_3}{r_1r_2r_3} = \frac{-1}{-3} = \frac{1}{3} \]
So, \( c = \frac{1}{3} \).

