mathclean,mathclean:f471ec3c79d3d6c6,full,logic error,"James starts the year by writing a 3-page letter to each of his 2 friends once a week. Each month, he decides to write an additional page to each friend, and he also increases the frequency of his letters by one more time per week. How many pages does James write in total over the year?","Let's break down the problem step-by-step. James starts by writing 3 pages to each of his 2 friends every week. This means he writes \(3 \times 2 = 6\) pages per week initially. Since there are 52 weeks in a year, he would normally write \(6 \times 52 = 312\) pages in a year if he wrote 6 pages every week.

