her_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，題目有要求數值需為奇數，因此刪掉不為奇數的選項即可得出答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:458f6961450f63e9,full,Unfinished answer,by approximately what percent is x greater than 1 / 2 if ( 1 / 2 ) ( x ) = 1 ?,\begin{aligned} \frac{1}{2} x & =1 \\ x & =2 \\ 2-\frac{1}{2}=\frac{3}{2} \end{aligned},Stops at the absolute difference instead of calculating the percentage increase,2-\frac{1}{2}=\frac{3}{2},ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""3/2"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 8242, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出x和1/2的差，還需轉換成百分比才正確"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To accurately determine the percentage by which x exceeds 1/2, you must first calculate the difference between x and 1/2. Then, you must convert this difference into a percentage.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 732 % , b ) 560 % , c ) 641 % , d ) 370 % , e ) 300 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""what percent is x greater than 1 / 2 if ( 1 / 2 ) ( x ) = 1 ? = > x = 2 % change = [ ( 2 - 1 / 2 ) / ( 1 / 2 ) ] * 100 = ( 4 - 1 ) * 100 = 300 % approx ans , e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To accurately determine the percentage by which x exceeds 1/2, you must first calculate the difference between x and 1/2. Then, you must convert this difference into a percentage."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出x和1/2的差，還需轉換成百分比才正確""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:45bcd38260d04f2a,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"what profit percent is made by selling an article at a certain price , if by selling at 1 / 3 rd of that price , there would be a loss of 20 % ?","assume the original selling price $X$, and the cost $y$ request: $\frac{x-y}{x}$ let the $x$ be 300 $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{y-\frac{1}{3} \times 300}{\frac{1}{3} \times 300}=20 \% \\ & y-100=20 \\ & y=120 \\ & \frac{x-y}{x}=\frac{300-120}{300}=60 \% \end{aligned} $$",Uses selling price instead of cost price as the loss-percentage denominator,\frac{y-\frac{1}{3} \times 300}{\frac{1}{3} \times 300}=20 \%,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,selling,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""60"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9685, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{y-\\frac{1}{3} \\times 300}{\\frac{1}{3} \\times 300}=20 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤比例的觀念錯誤，計算利潤時應將成本當作基準，而不是售價當作基準"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit percentage is incorrect. When calculating profit, the cost should be used as the benchmark, not the selling price.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 140 % , b ) 29 % , c ) 70 % , d ) 27 % , e ) 28 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""sp 2 = 1 / 3 sp 1 cp = 100 sp 2 = 80 1 / 3 sp 1 = 80 sp 1 = 240 100 - - - 240 = > 140 % answer : a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{y-\\frac{1}{3} \\times 300}{\\frac{1}{3} \\times 300}=20 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit percentage is incorrect. When calculating profit, the cost should be used as the benchmark, not the selling price."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤比例的觀念錯誤，計算利潤時應將成本當作基準，而不是售價當作基準""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:45c8af25f1fea204,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"a car is purchased on hire - purchase . the cash price is $ 22 000 and the terms are a deposit of 10 % of the price , then the balance to be paid off over 60 equal monthly installments . interest is charged at 12 % p . a . what is the monthly installment ?",\begin{aligned} & 22000-2200 \times 10 \%=19800 \\ & 19800 \times 1.1=21780 \\ & 21780 \div 60=363 \end{aligned},Applies an incorrect one-time interest multiplier instead of the annual rate over the full term,19800 \times 1.1=21780,ok,ok,,15,False,False,False,over,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""363"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 14688, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""19800 \\times 1.1=21780"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""利息計算方法錯誤，由於分60期每月一期，因此需要5年才能還完，總利息為12%*5=60%，每月還款金額為19800*(1+60%)/60=528"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The method of calculating interest is incorrect. Since the payment is made in 60 equal monthly installments, it will take 5 years to pay off the loan. The total interest is 12% * 5 = 60%. The monthly payment amount is 19800 * (1 + 60%) / 60 = 528.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 503 , b ) $ 504 , c ) $ 515 , d ) $ 528 , e ) $ 537"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""explanation : cash price = $ 22 000 deposit = 10 % ã — $ 22 000 = $ 2200 loan amount = $ 22000 â ˆ ’ $ 2200 number of payments = 60 = $ 19800 i = p * r * t / 100 i = 11880 total amount = 19800 + 11880 = $ 31680 regular payment = total amount / number of payments = 528 answer : d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""19800 \\times 1.1=21780"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The method of calculating interest is incorrect. Since the payment is made in 60 equal monthly installments, it will take 5 years to pay off the loan. The total interest is 12% * 5 = 60%. The monthly payment amount is 19800 * (1 + 60%) / 60 = 528."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""利息計算方法錯誤，由於分60期每月一期，因此需要5年才能還完，總利息為12%*5=60%，每月還款金額為19800*(1+60%)/60=528""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:45f70af7f0a1adb2,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"rates for having a manuscript typed at a certain typing service are $ 6 per page for the first time a page is typed and $ 4 per page each time a page is revised . if a certain manuscript has 100 pages , of which 40 were revised only once , 10 were revised twice , and the rest required no revisions , what was the total cost of having the manuscript typed ?",\begin{aligned} & 10 \times 4 \times 2+40 \times 4+(100-40-10) \times 6 \\ & =80+160+300 \\ & =540 \text { (dollars) } \end{aligned},Omits first-time typing charges for revised pages,10 \times 4 \times 2+40 \times 4+(100-40-10) \times 6,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,"pages, revised, typing",True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""540"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36022, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\times 4 \\times 2+40 \\times 4+(100-40-10) \\times 6"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算價格的方式錯誤，不是只有沒修改的文件要以6美元價格計算，而是所有100份文件都要，因此將扣掉的6*50加回即可得出正確答案840"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the price is incorrect. It is not only the unmodified documents that need to be calculated at $6 per page, but all 100 documents. Therefore, the deducted $6*50 should be added back to get the correct answer of $840.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 850 , b ) $ 840 , c ) $ 860 , d ) $ 870 , e ) $ 880"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""50 pages typed 1 x 40 pages typed 2 x ( original + one revision ) 10 pages typed 3 x ( original + two revisions ) 50 ( 6 ) + 40 ( 6 + 4 ) + 10 ( 6 + 4 + 4 ) = 300 + 400 + 140 = 840 answer - b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\times 4 \\times 2+40 \\times 4+(100-40-10) \\times 6"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the price is incorrect. It is not only the unmodified documents that need to be calculated at $6 per page, but all 100 documents. Therefore, the deducted $6*50 should be added back to get the correct answer of $840."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算價格的方式錯誤，不是只有沒修改的文件要以6美元價格計算，而是所有100份文件都要，因此將扣掉的6*50加回即可得出正確答案840""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:46207ffc4d8b13e9,full,Unfinished answer,"on a partly cloudy day , milton decides to walk back from work . when it is sunny , he walks at a speed of s miles / hr ( s is an integer ) and when it gets cloudy , he increases his speed to ( s + 1 ) miles / hr . if his average speed for the entire distance is 2.8 miles / hr , what fraction of the total distance did he cover while the sun was shining on him ?",\begin{aligned} &\begin{aligned} & S=2 \\ & S+1=3 \end{aligned}\\ &A: \frac{1}{5} \end{aligned},Calculates the distance fraction incorrectly from the average speed,A: \frac{1}{5},ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,from,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""1/5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 37175, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出陽光照射在他身上的時長為總時間的1/5，但還需計算出距離所佔的比例，計算方法為(1/5*2)/(1/5*2+4/5*3)=2/14=1/7"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Correctly calculate that the duration of sunshine is 1/5 of the total time, but you still need to calculate the proportion of distance covered. The calculation method is (1/5*2)/(1/5*2+4/5*3)=2/14=1/7""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 / 5 , b ) 1 / 6 , c ) 1 / 4 , d ) 1 / 7 , e ) 1 / 3"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""if s is an integer and we know that the average speed is 2.8 , s must be = 2 . that meanss + 1 = 3 . this implies that the ratio of time for s = 2 is 1 / 4 of the total time . the formula for distance / rate is d = rt . . . so the distance travelled when s = 2 is 2 t . the distance travelled for s + 1 = 3 is 3 * 4 t or 12 t . therefore , total distance covered while the sun was shining over him is 2 / 14 = 1 / 7 . answer : d"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Correctly calculate that the duration of sunshine is 1/5 of the total time, but you still need to calculate the proportion of distance covered. The calculation method is (1/5*2)/(1/5*2+4/5*3)=2/14=1/7"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出陽光照射在他身上的時長為總時間的1/5，但還需計算出距離所佔的比例，計算方法為(1/5*2)/(1/5*2+4/5*3)=2/14=1/7""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4637b9926c6afec0,full,Comprehension error,sandy bought 65 books for $ 1180 from one shop and 55 books for $ 860 from another shop . what is the average price that sandy paid per book ?,\begin{aligned} & 1180 \times 65=7670 \\ & 860 \times 55=4730 \\ & (7670+4730) \div(65+55) = 103.33 \end{aligned},Multiplies total amounts by quantities before averaging,1180 \times 65=7670,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""103.33"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36759, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""1180 \\times 65=7670 \\\\ & 860 \\times 55=4730"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，1180和860為花費的總金額，而不是每本書的售價，因此正確列式為(1180+860)/(65+55)=17"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The problem is misunderstood. 1180 and 860 are the total amounts spent, not the price of each book. Therefore, the correct equation should be (1180+860)/(65+55)=17""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 13 , b ) $ 15 , c ) $ 17 , d ) $ 19 , e ) $ 21"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""average price per book = ( 1180 + 860 ) / ( 65 + 55 ) = 2040 / 120 = $ 17 the answer is c .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""1180 \\times 65=7670 \\\\ & 860 \\times 55=4730"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The problem is misunderstood. 1180 and 860 are the total amounts spent, not the price of each book. Therefore, the correct equation should be (1180+860)/(65+55)=17"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，1180和860為花費的總金額，而不是每本書的售價，因此正確列式為(1180+860)/(65+55)=17""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4672194b77a339af,full,Comprehension error,"in town p , 60 percent of the population are employed , and 42 percent of the population are employed males . what percent of the employed people in town p are females ?",1 \times 0.6 \times(1-0.42)=0.348=34.8 \%,Confuses a percentage of the whole with a percentage within a subgroup,1 \times 0.6 \times(1-0.42)=0.348=34.8 \\%,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""34.8"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 794, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""1 \\times 0.6 \\times(1-0.42)=0.348=34.8 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題意並不是有42%有工作的人是男性，而是總人口的42%是男性"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is not asking what percentage of employed people are male, but rather what percentage of the total population is male.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 20 % , b ) 25 % , c ) 30 % , d ) 35 % , e ) 40 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""the percent of the population who are employed females is 60 - 42 = 18 % the percent of employed people who are female is 18 % / 60 % = 30 % . the answer is c .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""1 \\times 0.6 \\times(1-0.42)=0.348=34.8 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is not asking what percentage of employed people are male, but rather what percentage of the total population is male."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題意並不是有42%有工作的人是男性，而是總人口的42%是男性""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:46db4ab2debe4e54,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"a chemist mixes one liter of pure water with x liters of a 50 % salt solution , and the resulting mixture is a 15 % salt solution . what is the value of x ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{50}{100+x}=15%=\frac{15}{100}=\frac{3}{100} \\ & 300+3 X=1000 \\ & 3 x=700 \\ & x=\frac{700}{3} \end{aligned},Uses a fixed numerator instead of scaling the amount by variable volume,\frac{50}{100+x},ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""700/3"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35933, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{50}{100+x}=15%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""列式錯誤，在計算混和溶液濃度時，分母為溶液總公升數，分子為鹽的數量，因此正確列式為 0.5x / (1+x) =15%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. When calculating the concentration of the mixed solution, the denominator should be the total volume of the solution in liters, and the numerator should be the amount of salt in grams. Therefore, the correct equation should be:\n\n0.5x / (1+x) = 15%""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 / 4 , b ) 1 / 3 , c ) 1 / 2 , d ) 1 , e ) 3 / 7"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""concentration of salt in pure solution = 0 concentration of salt in salt solution = 50 % concentration of salt in the mixed solution = 15 % the pure solution and the salt solution is mixed in the ratio of - - > ( 50 - 15 ) / ( 15 - 0 ) = 7 / 3 1 / x = 7 / 3 x = 3 / 7 answer : e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{50}{100+x}=15%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. When calculating the concentration of the mixed solution, the denominator should be the total volume of the solution in liters, and the numerator should be the amount of salt in grams. Therefore, the correct equation should be:\n\n0.5x / (1+x) = 15%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""列式錯誤，在計算混和溶液濃度時，分母為溶液總公升數，分子為鹽的數量，因此正確列式為 0.5x / (1+x) =15%""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:46ebda46d97b8bc1,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"a straight line in the xy - plane has a slope of 2 and a y - intercept of 2 . on this line , what is the x - coordinate of the point whose y - coordinate is 550 ?","slope $=2, \quad y$-intercept $=2$ then $X$-intercept $=\frac{2}{2}=1$ $$ y:X=2: 1=550:275 $$",Treats coordinates as directly proportional despite a nonzero intercept,y:X=2: 1=550:275,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,intercept,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""275"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36009, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""slope $=2, \\quad y$-intercept $=2$ then $X$-intercept $=\\frac{2}{2}=1$"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""對於截距的觀念錯誤，依照題目給的資訊可以得出的線段為y = 2 x + 2，帶入y=550後即可計算出答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student has a misconception about the concept of the y-intercept. According to the information given in the question, the equation of the line is y = 2x + 2. By substituting y = 550 into this equation, we can calculate the x-coordinate of the point.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 249 , b ) 498 , c ) 676 , d ) 823 , e ) 274"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""slope of 2 and a y - intercept of 2 y - coordinate is 550 y = 2 x + 2 548 = 2 x x = 274 answer : e . 274\"""", ""error_equation"": ""slope $=2, \\quad y$-intercept $=2$ then $X$-intercept $=\\frac{2}{2}=1$"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student has a misconception about the concept of the y-intercept. According to the information given in the question, the equation of the line is y = 2x + 2. By substituting y = 550 into this equation, we can calculate the x-coordinate of the point."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""對於截距的觀念錯誤，依照題目給的資訊可以得出的線段為y = 2 x + 2，帶入y=550後即可計算出答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:47103143a117213e,full,Unfinished answer,"in a dairy farm , 46 cows eat 46 bags of husk in 46 days . in how many days one cow will eat one bag of husk ?",\begin{gathered} 46 \times 46=46 x \quad x=46 \\ A:\frac{1}{46} \end{gathered},Reports the reciprocal of the calculated time instead of the time itself,x=46 \quad A:\frac{1}{46},ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""1/46"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 15596, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算出奶牛每天的消耗量後，還需計算出一頭牛多少天能吃掉一袋穀殼，因此答案為1/(1/46)=46"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To calculate the number of days it takes for one cow to eat one bag of husk, first calculate the daily consumption of the cows. Then, divide 1 by the daily consumption to find the number of days it takes for one cow to eat one bag of husk. Therefore, the answer is 1/(1/46) = 46.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 , b ) 46 , c ) 20 , d ) 26 , e ) 30"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""explanation : one bag of husk = 46 cows per day ⇒ 46 × 1 × 46 = 1 × 46 × x for one cow = 46 days answer : b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To calculate the number of days it takes for one cow to eat one bag of husk, first calculate the daily consumption of the cows. Then, divide 1 by the daily consumption to find the number of days it takes for one cow to eat one bag of husk. Therefore, the answer is 1/(1/46) = 46."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算出奶牛每天的消耗量後，還需計算出一頭牛多少天能吃掉一袋穀殼，因此答案為1/(1/46)=46""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:471fa67ddc91983e,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"ram , who is half as efficient as krish , will take 18 days to complete a task if he worked alone . if ram and krish worked together , how long will they take to complete the task ?",\begin{aligned} & 18 r \geq\left(r+\frac{3}{2} r\right) \\ = & 18 r \geq \frac{5}{2} r \\ = & 18 \times \frac{2}{5}=\frac{36}{5}=7.2 \mathrm{days} \end{aligned},Misinterprets a half-efficiency relationship as a three-halves rate ratio,18 r \geq\left(r+\frac{3}{2} r\right),ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""7.2"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 37064, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""18 r \\geq\\left(r+\\frac{3}{2} r\\right)"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目列式錯誤，ram的工作效率為kris的一半，因此若假設r,a的工作效率為r，kris的工作效率為2r而不是3/2r，正確過程為18r/(r+2r)=6"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation in the problem is incorrect. Ram's efficiency is half of Krish's, so if we assume Ram's efficiency as r, Krish's efficiency should be 2r, not 3/2r. The correct equation should be: 18r/(r+2r) = 6""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 16 days , b ) 12 days , c ) 8 days , d ) 6 days , e ) 18 days"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""number of days taken by ram to complete task = 18 since ram is half as efficient as krish , amount of work done by krish in 1 day = amount of work done by ram in 2 days if total work done by ram in 18 days is 18 w amount of work done by ram in 1 day = w amount of work done by krish in 1 day = 2 w total amount of work done by krish and ram in a day = 3 w total amount of time needed by krish and ram to complete task = 18 w / 3 w = 6 days answer d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""18 r \\geq\\left(r+\\frac{3}{2} r\\right)"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation in the problem is incorrect. Ram's efficiency is half of Krish's, so if we assume Ram's efficiency as r, Krish's efficiency should be 2r, not 3/2r. The correct equation should be: 18r/(r+2r) = 6"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目列式錯誤，ram的工作效率為kris的一半，因此若假設r,a的工作效率為r，kris的工作效率為2r而不是3/2r，正確過程為18r/(r+2r)=6""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:472a2d412771739a,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"tom traveled the entire 60 miles trip . if he did the first 15 miles of at a constant rate 24 miles per hour and the remaining trip of at a constant rate 45 miles per hour , what is the his average speed , in miles per hour ?",24 \times \frac{15}{60}+45 \times \frac{60-15}{60}=39.75,Averages speeds using distance weights instead of total distance divided by total time,24 \times \frac{15}{60}+45 \times \frac{60-15}{60}=39.75,ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""39.75"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34552, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""24 \\times \\frac{15}{60}+45 \\times \\frac{60-15}{60}=39.75"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算平均速度的觀念錯誤，同學的式子需在tom在1/4的時間以每小時 24 英里的速度行走，在3/4的時間以每小時 45 英里行走才成立，但題目並不符合此情境，應先計算出兩種速度各別行走的時間來計算，而不是以兩速度移動的距離計算"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the average speed is incorrect. The student's equation assumes that Tom traveled the first 1/4 of the distance at a speed of 24 mph and the remaining 3/4 of the distance at a speed of 45 mph. However, this is not the case in the problem. The average speed should be calculated based on the time taken to travel at each speed, not the distance covered at each speed.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 35.62 mph , b ) 25.45 mph , c ) 34.52 mph , d ) 36.92 mph , e ) 36.29 mph"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""avg speed = total distance / total time = ( d 1 + d 2 ) / ( t 1 + t 2 ) = ( 15 + 45 ) / ( ( 15 / 24 ) + ( 45 / 45 ) ) = 60 * 2 / 3 = 36.92 mph d"", ""error_equation"": ""24 \\times \\frac{15}{60}+45 \\times \\frac{60-15}{60}=39.75"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the average speed is incorrect. The student's equation assumes that Tom traveled the first 1/4 of the distance at a speed of 24 mph and the remaining 3/4 of the distance at a speed of 45 mph. However, this is not the case in the problem. The average speed should be calculated based on the time taken to travel at each speed, not the distance covered at each speed."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算平均速度的觀念錯誤，同學的式子需在tom在1/4的時間以每小時 24 英里的速度行走，在3/4的時間以每小時 45 英里行走才成立，但題目並不符合此情境，應先計算出兩種速度各別行走的時間來計算，而不是以兩速度移動的距離計算""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:472a37b82edc8a14,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"if grapes are 92 % water and raisins are 20 % water , then how many kilograms did a quantity of raisins , which currently weighs 5 kilograms , weigh when all the raisins were grapes ? ( assume that the only difference between their raisin - weight and their grape - weight is water that evaporated during their transformation . )",\begin{aligned} & 5 \div 20 \% \\ & =5 \div 0.2 \\ & =25 \\ & 25 \times 92 \% \\ & =25 \times 0.92 \\ & =23 \end{aligned},Uses water percentages instead of complementary conserved-material percentages,5 \div 20 \% =5 \div 0.2 =25,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,water,False,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""23"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 4777, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""5 \\div 20 \\% \\\\ & =5 \\div 0.2 \\\\ & =25"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""轉換時去掉水分的葡萄質量是一樣的，差別只有水分含量，因此需先計算出五公斤的葡萄乾中有多少是去除水分的重量，再來推算葡萄的總重量。"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""When converting, the mass of the grapes without water remains the same, and the only difference is the water content. Therefore, we need to first calculate the weight of the dehydrated grapes in the five kilograms of raisins, and then calculate the total weight of the grapes.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 50 , b ) 54 , c ) 55 , d ) 56 , e ) 60"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""let x be the original weight . the weight of the grape pulp was 0.08 x . since the grape pulp is 80 % of the raisins , 0.08 x = 0.8 ( 5 ) . then x = 50 kg . the answer is a .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""5 \\div 20 \\% \\\\ & =5 \\div 0.2 \\\\ & =25"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""When converting, the mass of the grapes without water remains the same, and the only difference is the water content. Therefore, we need to first calculate the weight of the dehydrated grapes in the five kilograms of raisins, and then calculate the total weight of the grapes."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""轉換時去掉水分的葡萄質量是一樣的，差別只有水分含量，因此需先計算出五公斤的葡萄乾中有多少是去除水分的重量，再來推算葡萄的總重量。""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:478d25aee539a056,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"the greatest common divisor of ( b - 2 ) ! , ( b + 1 ) ! , and ( b + 4 ) ! is 5040 . what is the value of b ?",\begin{gathered} (b+4) !=5040 \\ 7 !=5040 \\ b=7-4=3 \end{gathered},Assumes the greatest common divisor equals one of the factorials,(b+4) !=5040,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"common, divisor, greatest",True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""3"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 1894, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{gathered} (b+4) !=5040 \\\\ 7 !=5040 \\\\ b=7-4=3 \\end{gathered}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""沒有理解最大公因數的涵義，最大公因數是三個數的因數中最大相同的值，可以先將5040質因數分解後再來觀察哪個數可以符合條件"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student does not understand the meaning of the greatest common divisor. The greatest common divisor is the largest common factor of three numbers. First, factorize 5040 into prime factors and then observe which number meets the condition.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 8 , b ) 10 , c ) 12 , d ) 9 , e ) 6"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""gcd of ( b - 2 ) ! , ( b + 1 ) ! , and ( b + 4 ) ! is 5040 . find x . best way to find n is substitute each of the answer and find out the correct one . only option d gave the correct answer . option d : 9 and find gcd or 7 ! , 10 ! and 13 ! . 7 ! itself is 5040 and 7 ! which is contained in the other two factorials . this satisfies the condition , hence answer is 9 . answer is d ."", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{gathered} (b+4) !=5040 \\\\ 7 !=5040 \\\\ b=7-4=3 \\end{gathered}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student does not understand the meaning of the greatest common divisor. The greatest common divisor is the largest common factor of three numbers. First, factorize 5040 into prime factors and then observe which number meets the condition."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""沒有理解最大公因數的涵義，最大公因數是三個數的因數中最大相同的值，可以先將5040質因數分解後再來觀察哪個數可以符合條件""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:47d94eca6d83c64e,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"sandy buys an old scooter for $ 800 and spends $ 200 on its repairs . if sandy sells the scooter for $ 1400 , what is the gain percent ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{1400-(800+200)}{1400} \\ & =\frac{400}{1400} \\ & =28.6 \% \end{aligned},Uses selling price instead of cost price as the gain percentage denominator,\frac{1400-(800+200)}{1400},ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,gain,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""28.6"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 11178, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1400-(800+200)}{1400}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算收益時觀念錯誤，計算收益的比例時，應該是以收益除以成本來計算，而不是收益除已售出價格計算"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit is incorrect. When calculating the profit percentage, it should be calculated by dividing the profit by the cost, not by dividing the profit by the selling price.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 20 % , b ) 30 % , c ) 40 % , d ) 50 % , e ) 60 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""selling price / total cost = 1400 / 1000 = 1.4 the gain percent is 40 % . the answer is c .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} & \\frac{1400-(800+200)}{1400}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit is incorrect. When calculating the profit percentage, it should be calculated by dividing the profit by the cost, not by dividing the profit by the selling price."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算收益時觀念錯誤，計算收益的比例時，應該是以收益除以成本來計算，而不是收益除已售出價格計算""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:47f6b9790584e965,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,what is the probability for a family with 3 children to have a girl and two boys ( assuming the probability of having a boy or a girl is equal ) ?,\frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{8},Counts only one birth order instead of all valid arrangements,\frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{2} \times \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{8},ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""1/8"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34403, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{8}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目詢問機率，因此不需要排列，因此同學還需要將算出的值乘以三才正確(女男男，男女男，男男女)"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks for the probability, so there is no need to arrange the order. Therefore, the student also needs to multiply the calculated value by three to get the correct answer (girl-boy-boy, boy-girl-boy, boy-boy-girl).""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 / 8 , b ) 1 / 4 , c ) 1 / 2 , d ) 3 / 8 , e ) 5 / 8"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""one possible case is : girl - boy - boy the probability of this is 1 / 2 * 1 / 2 * 1 / 2 = 1 / 8 there are 3 c 2 = 3 such cases so we should multiply by 3 . p ( one girl and two boys ) = 3 / 8 the answer is d ."", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{8}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks for the probability, so there is no need to arrange the order. Therefore, the student also needs to multiply the calculated value by three to get the correct answer (girl-boy-boy, boy-girl-boy, boy-boy-girl)."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目詢問機率，因此不需要排列，因此同學還需要將算出的值乘以三才正確(女男男，男女男，男男女)""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:484727842cec3f23,full,Unfinished answer,"the cost of one photocopy is $ 0.02 . however , a 25 % discount is offered on orders of more than 100 photocopies . if arthur and david have to make 80 copies each , how much will each of them save if they submit a single order of 160 copies ?",160 \times 0.02-160 \times 0.02 \times(1-0.25)=0.8,Does not divide the total savings equally between the two people,160 \times 0.02-160 \times 0.02 \times(1-0.25)=0.8,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""0.8"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34356, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目是問每人可節省多少錢，因此還需將總節省金額除以人數來得出正確答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks how much each person can save, so you also need to divide the total savings by the number of people to get the correct answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 0.32 , b ) $ 0.40 , c ) $ 0.45 , d ) $ 0.48 , e ) $ 0.54"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""if arthur and david submit separate orders , each would be smaller than 100 photocopies , so no discount . each would pay ( 80 ) * ( $ 0.02 ) = $ 1.60 , or together , a cost of $ 3.20 - - - that ' s the combined no discount cost . if they submit things together as one big order , they get a discount off of that $ 3.20 price - - - - 25 % or 1 / 4 of that is $ 0.80 , the discount on the combined sale . they each effective save half that amount , or $ 0.40 . answer = ( b ) .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks how much each person can save, so you also need to divide the total savings by the number of people to get the correct answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目是問每人可節省多少錢，因此還需將總節省金額除以人數來得出正確答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:48590ffab905f58d,full,Lack of necessary mathematical concepts,"p and q are the only two applicants qualified for a short - term research project that pays 300 dollars in total . candidate p has more experience and , if hired , would be paid 50 percent more per hour than candidate q would be paid . candidate q , if hired , would require 10 hours more than candidate p to do the job . candidate p ’ s hourly wage is how many dollars greater than candidate q ’ s hourly wage ?",Assume $q$ would be paid $x$ per hour $$ \begin{aligned} & (10 x+10 x \times 15) \times t+10 x \times 10=300 \\ & 25 x \times t+100 x=300 \\ & (100+25 t) x=300 \end{aligned} $$,Combines mutually exclusive payment scenarios into one total-pay equation,(10 x+10 x \times 15) \times t+10 x \times 10=300,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": NaN, ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": ""不知道怎麼求出來"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": ""Not knowing how to solve for it"", ""mathedu_id"": 14561, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Lack of necessary mathematical concepts"", ""error_equation"": ""(10 x+10 x \\times 15) \\times t+10 x \\times 10=300"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於雙方的總薪資皆為300，因此可以假設q的時薪為x，p的薪資為1.5x，q花費時間t來完成工作，建立方程式x * t = 1.5 x * ( t - 10 )且x*t=300，可以得出t=30，因此q ' s hourly wage is 300 / 30 = $ 10 p ' s hourly wage is 300 / ( t - 10 ) = $ 15 which is $ 5 per hour more"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since the total pay for both candidates is $300, we can assume that candidate Q's hourly wage is $x, and candidate P's hourly wage is $1.5x. Let's say candidate Q takes t hours to complete the job. We can set up the equation:\n\nx * t = 1.5x * (t - 10)\n\nWe also know that x * t = 300.\n\nSolving for t, we get t = 30.\n\nTherefore, candidate Q's hourly wage is $300 / 30 = $10.\n\nCandidate P's hourly wage is $300 / (t - 10) = $15, which is $5 per hour more.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 5 , b ) $ 10 , c ) $ 15 , d ) $ 20 , e ) $ 25"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""let q ' s hourly wage be x , then p ' s hourly wage is 1.5 x let t be the number of hours that q needs , then p needs t - 10 hours to do the job . since they both are paid an equal total amount of $ 300 : x * t = 1.5 x * ( t - 10 ) t = 30 hours and q ' s hourly wage is 300 / 30 = $ 10 p ' s hourly wage is 300 / ( t - 10 ) = $ 15 which is $ 5 per hour more . the answer is a .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""(10 x+10 x \\times 15) \\times t+10 x \\times 10=300"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since the total pay for both candidates is $300, we can assume that candidate Q's hourly wage is $x, and candidate P's hourly wage is $1.5x. Let's say candidate Q takes t hours to complete the job. We can set up the equation:\n\nx * t = 1.5x * (t - 10)\n\nWe also know that x * t = 300.\n\nSolving for t, we get t = 30.\n\nTherefore, candidate Q's hourly wage is $300 / 30 = $10.\n\nCandidate P's hourly wage is $300 / (t - 10) = $15, which is $5 per hour more."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於雙方的總薪資皆為300，因此可以假設q的時薪為x，p的薪資為1.5x，q花費時間t來完成工作，建立方程式x * t = 1.5 x * ( t - 10 )且x*t=300，可以得出t=30，因此q ' s hourly wage is 300 / 30 = $ 10 p ' s hourly wage is 300 / ( t - 10 ) = $ 15 which is $ 5 per hour more""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4875c35686ba0eec,full,Unfinished answer,"tough and tricky questions : statistics . set x consists of prime numbers { 3 , 11 , 7 , a , 17 , 19 } . if integer y represents the product of all elements in set x and if 11 y is an even number , what is the range of set x ?","$$ \begin{aligned} & y=3 \times 11 \times 7 \times a \times 17 \times 19 \\ & 11 y=2 \alpha \\ & 11y=3 \times 11^2 \times 7 \times a \times 17 \times 19=2 \alpha\right. \end{aligned} $$ $\therefore$ a must be a multiple of 2 , should be a prime number $\Rightarrow a=2$ range $=2$ to 19",Confuses the range with the interval from minimum to maximum,range $=2$ to 19,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,range,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""2 to 19"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9816, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出範圍，還需將19-2=17來得出範圍的大小"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To correctly calculate the range, you also need to subtract 19 - 2 = 17 to find the size of the range.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 14 , b ) 16 , c ) 17 , d ) 20 , e ) 26"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""since 11 y = even therefore y has to beevensince 11 is a odd integer ( even * odd = even ) similarly , y is the product of all integers in set x but all integers in set x are odd except the unknown a and since x contains only prime numbers , a has to equal to 2 . . . ( 2 is the only even prime number and the product of all prime numbers in set x has to be even , even * odd = even ) since you know value of a you can calculate the range = largest integer in the set minus smallest integer in the set = 19 - 2 = 17 answer is c"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To correctly calculate the range, you also need to subtract 19 - 2 = 17 to find the size of the range."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出範圍，還需將19-2=17來得出範圍的大小""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:48ba12d5b994dd49,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,a car takes 6 hours to cover a distance of 540 km . how much should the speed in kmph be maintained to cover the same direction in 3 / 2 th of the previous time ?,\begin{aligned} & 540 \div 6=90 \\ & 90 \times \frac{3}{2}=135 \end{aligned},Multiplies speed by the time factor instead of using inverse proportionality,90 \times \frac{3}{2}=135,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""135"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 1122, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""90 \\times \\frac{3}{2}=135"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於會花費原速度度的3/2倍時間，因為距離=時間*速度，因此速度應為原來的2/3倍，也就是90*2/3=60"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since it will take 3/2 times the original speed, and distance = time * speed, the speed should be 2/3 of the original speed, which is 90 * 2/3 = 60.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 35 kmph , b ) 48 kmph , c ) 52 kmph , d ) 54 kmph , e ) 60 kmph"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""time = 6 distance = 540 3 / 2 of 6 hours = 6 * 3 / 2 = 9 hours required speed = 540 / 9 = 60 kmph e )\"""", ""error_equation"": ""90 \\times \\frac{3}{2}=135"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since it will take 3/2 times the original speed, and distance = time * speed, the speed should be 2/3 of the original speed, which is 90 * 2/3 = 60."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於會花費原速度度的3/2倍時間，因為距離=時間*速度，因此速度應為原來的2/3倍，也就是90*2/3=60""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:48ccfc1cc935f2e9,full,Arithmetical error,"45 litres of diesel is required to travel 600 km using a 800 cc engine . if the volume of diesel required to cover a distance varies directly as the capacity of the engine , then how many litres of diesel is required to travel 800 km using 1200 cc engine ?",$800 \mathrm{cc}$ engine need $45 \div 6=7.5$ liters for  $100 \mathrm{~km}$ $1200 \mathrm{CC}$ engine need $7.5 \times \frac{1200}{800}=11.25$ liters for $100 \mathrm{~km}$ $11.25 \times 8=89$ liters,Makes an arithmetic error when multiplying the final quantities,$11.25 \times 8=89$ liters,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""89"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 14586, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""11.25 \\times 8=89"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，11.25*8應為90而不是89"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. 11.25 * 8 should be 90, not 89.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 80 litres , b ) 90 litres , c ) 120 litres , d ) 170 litres , e ) none of these"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""explanatory answer to cover a distance of 800 kms using a 800 cc engine , the amount of diesel required = 800 / 600 * 45 = 60 litres . however , the vehicle uses a 1200 cc engine and the question states that the amount of diesel required varies directly as the engine capacity . i . e . , for instance , if the capacity of engine doubles , the diesel requirement will double too . therefore , with a 1200 cc engine , quantity of diesel required = 1200 / 800 * 60 = 90 litres . answer b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""11.25 \\times 8=89"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. 11.25 * 8 should be 90, not 89."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，11.25*8應為90而不是89""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4967457c93e46200,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,john makes $ 40 a week from his job . he earns a raise and now makes $ 60 a week . what is the % increase ?,\frac{60-40}{60}=33.33 \%,Uses the new amount instead of the original amount as the percentage baseline,\frac{60-40}{60}=33.33 \%,ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""33.33"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 10930, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{60-40}{60}=33.33 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算增長的觀念錯誤，計算增長比例時應將原先的薪水當作基準，而不是加薪後的薪水當作基準"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the increase is incorrect. When calculating the percentage increase, the original salary should be used as the base, not the salary after the raise.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 16 % , b ) 16.66 % , c ) 18 % , d ) 21 % , e ) 50 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""increase = ( 20 / 40 ) * 100 = 50 % . e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{60-40}{60}=33.33 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the increase is incorrect. When calculating the percentage increase, the original salary should be used as the base, not the salary after the raise."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算增長的觀念錯誤，計算增長比例時應將原先的薪水當作基準，而不是加薪後的薪水當作基準""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:496f540d7666b951,full,Comprehension error,"a student needs 60 % of the marks on a test to pass the test . if the student gets 80 marks and fails the test by 100 marks , find the maximum marks set for the test .",100 \div 60 \% \fallingdotseq 166.67,Uses the shortfall alone instead of adding it to the obtained amount,100 \div 60 \% \fallingdotseq 166.67,ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""166.67"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6927, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""100 \\div 60 \\% \\fallingdotseq 166.67"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，學生是拿到80分，和及格分相差100分，而不是及格分為100分"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is misunderstood. The student got 80 marks and failed the test by 100 marks, not that the passing mark is 100 marks.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 250 , b ) 300 , c ) 350 , d ) 400 , e ) 450"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""60 % = 180 marks 1 % = 3 marks 100 % = 300 marks the answer is b .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""100 \\div 60 \\% \\fallingdotseq 166.67"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is misunderstood. The student got 80 marks and failed the test by 100 marks, not that the passing mark is 100 marks."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，學生是拿到80分，和及格分相差100分，而不是及格分為100分""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:49f6595c2591043a,full,Comprehension error,a trader sells 40 metres of cloth for rs . 8200 at a profit of rs . 30 per metre of cloth . how much profit will the trder earn on 40 metres of cloth ?,8200 \times(40-30)=82000,Confuses total selling amount with per-unit profit when calculating total profit,8200 \times(40-30)=82000,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""82000"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 932, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""8200 \\times(40-30)=82000"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有理解各個數字的涵義，40是貿易商出售的米數，30是每米的利潤，因此要計算出出售40米有多少利潤，將40*30=1200即可得出答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not understand the meaning of each number. 40 is the number of meters the trader sold, and 30 is the profit per meter. Therefore, to calculate the profit on 40 meters, multiply 40 * 30 = 1200 to get the answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) rs . 950 , b ) rs . 1500 , c ) rs . 1000 , d ) rs . 1200 , e ) none of these"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""explanation : sp of 1 metre cloth = 8200 / 40 = rs . 205 . cp of 1 metre cloth = rs . 205 – 30 = rs . 175 cp on 40 metres = 175 x 40 = rs . 7000 profit earned on 40 metres cloth = rs . 8200 – rs . 7000 = rs . 1200 . answer : option d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""8200 \\times(40-30)=82000"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not understand the meaning of each number. 40 is the number of meters the trader sold, and 30 is the profit per meter. Therefore, to calculate the profit on 40 meters, multiply 40 * 30 = 1200 to get the answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有理解各個數字的涵義，40是貿易商出售的米數，30是每米的利潤，因此要計算出出售40米有多少利潤，將40*30=1200即可得出答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4a2b8ffba78c9176,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"8 men can dig a pit in 20 days . if a man works half as much again a s a boy , then 4 men and 9 boys can dig a similar pit in :",\frac{8 \times 20}{4+\frac{9}{2}}=\frac{320}{17},Misinterprets “half as much again” as a one-half relative work rate,4+\frac{9}{2},ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"again, half, much",True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""320/17"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34465, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{8 \\times 20}{4+\\frac{9}{2}}=\\frac{320}{17}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目是說八個男人可以在20天挖一個坑，不是八個男孩，因此以同學的假設，正確列式應為(8*(1/2)*20)/(4+(9/2))"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question states that 8 men can dig a pit in 20 days, not 8 boys. Therefore, based on your assumption, the correct equation should be (8*(1/2)*20)/(4+(9/2)).""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 10 days , b ) 12 days , c ) 15 days , d ) 16 days , e ) 20 days"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""explanation : 1 work done = 8 × 20 1 man = 3 / 2 boys 1 boy = 2 / 3 men then , 9 boys = 9 × 2 / 3 men = 6 men then , 4 men + 9 boys = 10 men then , 8 × 20 = 10 × ? days ? days = 8 × 20 / 10 = 16 days . answer : option d"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{8 \\times 20}{4+\\frac{9}{2}}=\\frac{320}{17}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question states that 8 men can dig a pit in 20 days, not 8 boys. Therefore, based on your assumption, the correct equation should be (8*(1/2)*20)/(4+(9/2))."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目是說八個男人可以在20天挖一個坑，不是八個男孩，因此以同學的假設，正確列式應為(8*(1/2)*20)/(4+(9/2))""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4a70a408fa69aea7,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"a camera lens filter kit containing 5 filters sells for $ 87.50 . if the filters are purchased individually , 2 of them are priced at $ 16.45 each , 2 at $ 14.05 each , 1 at $ 19.50 . the amount saved by purchasing the kit is what percent of the total price of the 5 filters purchased individually ?",\begin{aligned} & 2 \times 16.45+2 \times 14.05+19.5=32.9+28.1+19.5=80.5 \\ & \frac{80.5-87.5}{80.5}=\frac{-7}{80.5} \fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \% \end{aligned},Rounds the percentage to an inaccurate whole-percent value,\frac{-7}{80.5}\fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \%,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""-8"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9056, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{80.5-87.5}{80.5}=\\frac{-7}{80.5} \\fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於五個套件一起買，價格會比單買便宜，因此省的錢是正數，同學在後續計算節省金額時應拿單買得較高價格扣掉一起買的折扣價格才能得出正確答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since buying the five filters as a kit is cheaper than buying them individually, the amount saved should be a positive number. When calculating the amount saved, students should subtract the discounted price of the kit from the higher price of buying the filters individually to get the correct answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 7 % , b ) 8 % , c ) 9 % , d ) 10 % , e ) 11 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""cost of kit = $ 87.50 if filters are purchased individually - $ 16.45 * 2 + $ 14.05 * 2 + $ 19.50 = $ 80.50 amount saved = $ 87.50 - $ 80.50 = $ 7 required % age = ( $ 7 / $ 87.50 ) * 100 = 8 % so , the correct answer is b .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{80.5-87.5}{80.5}=\\frac{-7}{80.5} \\fallingdotseq-0.08=-8 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Since buying the five filters as a kit is cheaper than buying them individually, the amount saved should be a positive number. When calculating the amount saved, students should subtract the discounted price of the kit from the higher price of buying the filters individually to get the correct answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""由於五個套件一起買，價格會比單買便宜，因此省的錢是正數，同學在後續計算節省金額時應拿單買得較高價格扣掉一起買的折扣價格才能得出正確答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4ac5bf1d112598d9,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in a 200 m race , if a gives b a start of 25 metres , then a wins the race by 10 seconds . alternatively , if a gives b a start of 45 metres the race ends in a dead heat . how long does a take to run 200 m ?",$$ 45-25=20 $$ speed of a is $20 \div 10=2 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$ $$ 200 \div 2=100 \mathrm{sec} $$,Confuses one participant’s speed with the other’s,speed of a is $20 \div 10=2 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""100"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 14161, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""speed of a is $20 \\div 10"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算出的速度2m/s並不是a的速度而是b的速度，得知b的速度後，b will take 22.5 seconds to run this 45 metres as b runs 20 metres in 10 seconds or at the speed of 2 m / s . hence , a will take 22.5 seconds lesser than b or 100 - 22.5 = 77.5 seconds to complete the race ."", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculated speed of 2m/s is not the speed of A but the speed of B. Knowing the speed of B, B will take 22.5 seconds to run this 45 meters as B runs 20 meters in 10 seconds or at the speed of 2 m / s. Hence, A will take 22.5 seconds lesser than B or 100 - 22.5 = 77.5 seconds to complete the race.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 100 seconds , b ) 112.5 seconds , c ) 77.5 seconds , d ) 87.5 seconds , e ) none"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""explanatory answer a gives b a start of 25 metres and still wins the race by 10 seconds . alternatively , if a gives b a start of 45 metres , then the race ends in a dead heat . therefore , the additional 20 metres start given to b compensates for the 10 seconds . i . e . , b runs 20 metres in 10 seconds . hence , b will take 100 seconds to run 200 metres . we know that a gives b a start of 45 metres . b will take 22.5 seconds to run this 45 metres as b runs 20 metres in 10 seconds or at the speed of 2 m / s . hence , a will take 22.5 seconds lesser than b or 100 - 22.5 = 77.5 seconds to complete the race . answer c"", ""error_equation"": ""speed of a is $20 \\div 10"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculated speed of 2m/s is not the speed of A but the speed of B. Knowing the speed of B, B will take 22.5 seconds to run this 45 meters as B runs 20 meters in 10 seconds or at the speed of 2 m / s. Hence, A will take 22.5 seconds lesser than B or 100 - 22.5 = 77.5 seconds to complete the race."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算出的速度2m/s並不是a的速度而是b的速度，得知b的速度後，b will take 22.5 seconds to run this 45 metres as b runs 20 metres in 10 seconds or at the speed of 2 m / s . hence , a will take 22.5 seconds lesser than b or 100 - 22.5 = 77.5 seconds to complete the race .""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4aec24c4e25c0aff,full,Careless error,"mary sold boxes of butter cookies . ann sold 5 times as much as she did . 18 boxes of cookies were sold that day , how many boxes did mary sell ?",Assume mary sold $x$ boxes of butter cookies. $$ \begin{aligned} & x+5 x=18 \\ \Rightarrow & 6 x=18 \\ \Rightarrow & x=18 \div 6 \\ \Rightarrow & x=3 \# \end{aligned} $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies.,Reports an answer inconsistent with the calculated value,\Rightarrow & x=3 \# \end{aligned} $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies.,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""6"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35234, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Careless error"", ""error_equation"": ""& x=3 $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學有正確計算出mary販賣的盒數(x=3)，但最後寫答案時卻寫錯寫成6"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student correctly calculated the number of boxes Mary sold (x = 3), but made a mistake when writing the final answer, writing 6 instead.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 3 , b ) 5 , c ) 6 , d ) 10 , e ) 18"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""# of boxes of cookies mary sold = x ann sold 5 times more = 5 x x + 5 x = 18 6 x = 18 x = 18 / 6 = 3 answer : a"", ""error_equation"": ""& x=3 $$ A. mary sold 6 boxes of butter cookies."", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student correctly calculated the number of boxes Mary sold (x = 3), but made a mistake when writing the final answer, writing 6 instead."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學有正確計算出mary販賣的盒數(x=3)，但最後寫答案時卻寫錯寫成6""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4b6c4ab0e56b5296,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"if x dollars is invested at 10 percent for one year and y dollars is invested at 8 percent for one year , the annual income from the 10 percent investment will exceed the annual income from the 8 percent investment by $ 56 . if $ 2,000 is the total amount invested , how much is invested at 8 percent ?",\begin{aligned} & 10 \% x-8 \% y=56 \\ & 2000 \times 8 \%=160 \end{aligned},Confuses the total amount invested with the amount invested at one rate,2000 \times 8 \%=160,ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,invested,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""160"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 10888, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""2000 \\times 8 \\%=160"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式假設錯誤，由於2000為總投資金額，因此x+y=2000，將x轉換為2000-y帶入10%x-8%y=56運算及可得出y=800"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrectly set up. Since the total amount invested is $2,000, x + y = 2000. Substitute x for 2000 - y in the equation 10%x - 8%y = 56 and solve for y to get y = 800.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 280 , b ) $ 800 , c ) $ 892 , d ) $ 1,108 , e ) $ 1,200"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""( a ) $ 280 ( b ) $ 800 ( c ) $ 892 ( d ) $ 1,108 ( e ) $ 1,200 y = 2000 - x . 1 x - . 08 ( 2000 - x ) = 56 . - 160 + . 18 x = 56 x = 1200 and y = 800 answer : b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""2000 \\times 8 \\%=160"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrectly set up. Since the total amount invested is $2,000, x + y = 2000. Substitute x for 2000 - y in the equation 10%x - 8%y = 56 and solve for y to get y = 800."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式假設錯誤，由於2000為總投資金額，因此x+y=2000，將x轉換為2000-y帶入10%x-8%y=56運算及可得出y=800""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4c16fca2d01c6a17,full,Lack of necessary mathematical concepts,"if 3 ^ x * 4 ^ y = 531,441 and x – y = 12 , then x = ?",$$ \begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} 3 x \cdot 4 y=531441 \ldots (1) \\ x-y=12 \ldots(2) \end{array}\right. \\ & \text { (2) } \Rightarrow y=x-12 \ldots(3) \end{aligned} $$ substitute $(x-12)$ for $y$ in (1) $$ \begin{aligned} \Rightarrow 3 x \cdot 4(x-12) & =531441 \\ x(x-12) & =\frac{531441}{3 \times 4} \end{aligned} $$,Treats exponentiation as multiplication by the exponent,3 x \cdot 4 y=531441,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,3,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""none"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": ""無法解方程式"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": ""Unable to solve the equation"", ""mathedu_id"": 8062, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Lack of necessary mathematical concepts"", ""error_equation"": ""3 x \\cdot 4 y=531441 \\ldots"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""對^使用錯誤的方式計算，^為幾次方的意思而不是相乘"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The use of ^ in the problem is incorrect. ^ represents exponentiation, not multiplication.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 10 , b ) 11 , c ) 12 , d ) 13 , e ) 14"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""since 531,441 is an odd number , it is not a multiple of 4 . this means that y must equal zero . since x - y = 12 and y = 0 , then x = 12 . the answer is c .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""3 x \\cdot 4 y=531441 \\ldots"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The use of ^ in the problem is incorrect. ^ represents exponentiation, not multiplication."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""對^使用錯誤的方式計算，^為幾次方的意思而不是相乘""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4c3ab6c2ac473f7c,full,Unfinished answer,"following an increase in prices , the price of a candy box was 10 pounds and the price of a can of soda was 12 pounds . if the price of a candy box was raised by 25 % , and the price of a can of soda was raised by 50 % . what was the price of a box of candy plus a can of soda before prices were raised ?",assume the price of candy box and soda was $x$ and $y$. $$ \begin{array}{rlrl} 1.25 x & =10 & 1.5 y & =12 \\ x & =8 \text { (pounds) } & y & =8 \text { (pounds) } \# \end{array} $$,Does not add the recovered prices to find their combined total,x =8 (pounds)    y =8 (pounds),ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,prices,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""8 , 8"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 8194, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出兩者的價錢，但還需算出他們的總和"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To accurately calculate the total cost of a box of candy and a can of soda before the price increase, you need to first calculate the new price of each item after the increase and then add those prices together.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 11 . , b ) 12 . , c ) 16 . , d ) 14 . , e ) 14.5"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""price of candy before price increase = 10 / 1.25 = 8 price of soda before price increase = 12 / 1.5 = 8 total price = 8 + 8 = 16 c is the answer\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To accurately calculate the total cost of a box of candy and a can of soda before the price increase, you need to first calculate the new price of each item after the increase and then add those prices together."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出兩者的價錢，但還需算出他們的總和""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4c46598616a78766,full,Careless error,a 750 m long train crosses a platform in 39 sec while it crosses a signal pole in 18 sec . what is the length of the platform ?,The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \mathrm{~m}$ So the speed is $750 \div 15=50 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$ 39 secund can pass $50 \times 39=1950 \mathrm{~m}$ $1950-750=1200 \mathrm{~m}$,Uses the wrong time interval to calculate speed,The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \mathrm{~m}$,ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""1200"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36404, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Careless error"", ""error_equation"": ""The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \\mathrm{~m}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""粗心看錯題目數字導致錯誤，火車是花費18秒通過信號桿，而不是花費15秒，因此火車正確速度為750/18=125 / 3"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Careless mistake in reading the problem numbers led to the error. The train took 18 seconds to pass the signal pole, not 15 seconds. Therefore, the correct speed of the train is 750/18 = 125/3""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 300 , b ) 875 , c ) 360 , d ) 770 , e ) 380"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""speed = 750 / 18 = 125 / 3 m / sec . let the length of the platform be x meters . then , ( x + 750 ) / 39 = 125 / 3 = > x = 1625 m . l = 1625 - 750 = 875 answer : option b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""The train needs 15 second to pass $750 \\mathrm{~m}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Careless mistake in reading the problem numbers led to the error. The train took 18 seconds to pass the signal pole, not 15 seconds. Therefore, the correct speed of the train is 750/18 = 125/3"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""粗心看錯題目數字導致錯誤，火車是花費18秒通過信號桿，而不是花費15秒，因此火車正確速度為750/18=125 / 3""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4c56dd10462926ff,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"two bullet trains of equal lengths take 10 seconds and 30 seconds respectively to cross a telegraph post . if the length of each bullet train be 120 metres , in what time ( in seconds ) will they cross each other travelling in opposite direction ?",$\left.\begin{array}{l}120 \div 10=12 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} \\ 120 \div 30=4 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}\end{array}\right\}$ speed of two train $12+4=16 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} \Rightarrow$ total speed when they travel in opposite direction $120 \div 16=\frac{15}{2}=7.5$ seconds,Uses one length instead of the combined lengths as crossing distance,total speed when they travel in opposite direction $120 \div 16=\frac{15}{2}=7.5$ seconds,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,lengths,True,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""7.5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35183, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""total speed when they travel in opposite direction $120 \\div 16=\\frac{15}{2}=7.5$ seconds"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""要使兩輛列車交叉，須通過的距離為兩輛列長的長度和，而不是一輛列車的長度"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""In order for the two trains to pass each other, the distance they need to cover is the sum of their lengths, not just the length of one train.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 13 sec . , b ) 14 sec . , c ) 12 sec . , d ) 15 sec . , e ) 19 sec ."", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""speed of the first bullet train = 120 / 10 m / sec = 12 m / sec . speed of the second bullet train = 120 / 30 m / sec = 4 m / sec . relative speed = ( 12 + 4 ) = 16 m / sec . required time = ( 120 + 120 ) / 16 sec = 15 sec . d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""total speed when they travel in opposite direction $120 \\div 16=\\frac{15}{2}=7.5$ seconds"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""In order for the two trains to pass each other, the distance they need to cover is the sum of their lengths, not just the length of one train."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""要使兩輛列車交叉，須通過的距離為兩輛列長的長度和，而不是一輛列車的長度""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4c80c3d197edbae2,full,Comprehension error,what is the sum of all 3 digit integers formed using the digits 34 and 5 ( repetition is allowed ),3 \times 3 \times 3=27,Computes the number of integers instead of their sum,3 \times 3 \times 3=27,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,integers,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""27"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34457, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""3 \\times 3 \\times 3=27"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題意是要詢問3 4和5組成的所有 3 位整數的總和，而不是總共有幾種不同的組成"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks for the sum of all 3-digit integers formed using the digits 3, 4, and 5 (repetition allowed), not the number of different combinations.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 11982 , b ) 11984 , c ) 11985 , d ) 11988 , e ) 11986"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""n = 3 * 3 * 3 = 27 = ( 555 + 333 ) / 2 = 444 sum = number of integers x average value n * = 27 * 444 = 11988 answer = d"", ""error_equation"": ""3 \\times 3 \\times 3=27"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question asks for the sum of all 3-digit integers formed using the digits 3, 4, and 5 (repetition allowed), not the number of different combinations."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題意是要詢問3 4和5組成的所有 3 位整數的總和，而不是總共有幾種不同的組成""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4d0517c9f7b417b3,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,the h . c . f . of two numbers is 20 and the other two factors of their l . c . m . are 21 and 23 . the larger of the two numbers is,\begin{aligned} & 20 \times(23-21) \\ = & 20 \times 2 \\ = & 40 \end{aligned},Subtracts factors instead of multiplying them to determine the larger number,20 \times(23-21),ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,"factors, larger",True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""40"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 13029, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""20 \\times(23-21)"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""解題觀念錯誤，23和21為兩數最小公倍數的因數，而20為兩數的最大公因數，因此我們可以推測兩數分別為21*20和23*20，因此較大的數為23*20=460"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of the question is incorrect. 23 and 21 are factors of the least common multiple of the two numbers, while 20 is the greatest common factor of the two numbers. Therefore, we can infer that the two numbers are 21*20 and 23*20, respectively. Thus, the larger number is 23*20 = 460.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 276 , b ) 299 , c ) 312 , d ) 460 , e ) none"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""other"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""solution clearly , the numbers are ( 20 x 21 ) and ( 20 x 23 ) . larger number = ( 20 x 23 ) = 460 . answer d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""20 \\times(23-21)"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of the question is incorrect. 23 and 21 are factors of the least common multiple of the two numbers, while 20 is the greatest common factor of the two numbers. Therefore, we can infer that the two numbers are 21*20 and 23*20, respectively. Thus, the larger number is 23*20 = 460."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""解題觀念錯誤，23和21為兩數最小公倍數的因數，而20為兩數的最大公因數，因此我們可以推測兩數分別為21*20和23*20，因此較大的數為23*20=460""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4d7b9bca03d7b6e3,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in the standard formulation of a flavored drink the ratio by volume of flavoring to corn syrup to water is 1 : 12 : 30 . in the ` ` sport ' ' formulation , the ratio of flavoring to corn syrup is 3 times as great as in the standard formulation , and the ratio of flavoring to water is half that of the standard formulation . if a large bottle of the ` ` sport ' ' formulation contains 3 ounces of corn syrup , how many ounces of water does it contain ?",\begin{aligned} & 3:12: 45 \\ & 45 \times \frac{1}{4}=11.25 \end{aligned},Combines pairwise ratio changes into an incorrect three-part ratio,3:12: 45,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""11.25"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 15793, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""3:12:45"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""調味料和水的比例錯誤，調味劑與水的比例是標準配方的一半，因此應由原來的1:30變為1:60而不是1:15，正確的整體比例為3:12:180，因此水的體積為3*180/12=45"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The ratio of flavoring to water is incorrect. The flavoring to water ratio is half that of the standard formulation, so it should be 1:60 instead of 1:15. The correct overall ratio is 3:12:180, so the volume of water is 3*180/12 = 45.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 45 , b ) 50 , c ) 55 , d ) 60 , e ) 63"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""other"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""f : c : w 1 : 12 : 30 sport version : f : c 3 : 12 f : w 1 : 60 or 3 : 180 so c : f : w = 12 : 3 : 180 c / w = 12 / 180 = 3 ounces / x ounces x = 3 * 180 / 12 = 45 ounces of water answer : a"", ""error_equation"": ""3:12:45"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The ratio of flavoring to water is incorrect. The flavoring to water ratio is half that of the standard formulation, so it should be 1:60 instead of 1:15. The correct overall ratio is 3:12:180, so the volume of water is 3*180/12 = 45."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""調味料和水的比例錯誤，調味劑與水的比例是標準配方的一半，因此應由原來的1:30變為1:60而不是1:15，正確的整體比例為3:12:180，因此水的體積為3*180/12=45""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4da37291430d4443,full,Algebraic error,"if w is 40 percent less than x , x is 40 percent less than y , and z is 46 percent less than y , then z is greater than w by what percent of w ?",\begin{aligned} & w=0.6 x \\ & x=0.6 y \\ & z=0.54 y \\ & w=\frac{0.6}{0.54} \times 0.6 z \\ & 15 w=z \\ & \frac{z-w}{w}=14=1400 \% \end{aligned},Miscomputes a proportional relationship when rearranging and evaluating decimal factors,w=\frac{0.6}{0.54} \times 0.6 z \newline & 15 w=z,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""1400"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 2736, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Algebraic error"", ""error_equation"": ""w=\\frac{0.6}{0.54} \\times 0.6 z \\\\ & 15 w=z"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式解錯，這邊的計算結果應為w=2/3z"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The correct calculation should be w = 2/3z.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 4 % , b ) 18 % , c ) 36 % , d ) 40 % , e ) 50 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""given w = 0.6 x , x = 0.6 y , z = 0.54 y , substituting , w = 2 / 3 z - - - - > z = 1.5 w and thus z is 50 % greater than w . e is the correct answer ."", ""error_equation"": ""w=\\frac{0.6}{0.54} \\times 0.6 z \\\\ & 15 w=z"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The correct calculation should be w = 2/3z."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式解錯，這邊的計算結果應為w=2/3z""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4e94bedf4ef681c2,full,Algebraic error,"if w is 40 percent less than q , q is 40 percent less than y , and z is 46 percent less than y , then z is greater than w by what percent of w ?",\begin{aligned} & w=0.6q \\ & q=0.6 y \\ & z=0.54 y \\ & w=\frac{0.6}{0.54} \times 0.6 z \\ & 15 w=z \\ & \frac{z-w}{w}=14=1400 \% \end{aligned},Drops the decimal point in a multiplicative relationship,& 15 w=z,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""1400"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 520, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Algebraic error"", ""error_equation"": ""w=\\frac{0.6}{0.54} \\times 0.6 z \\\\ & 15 w=z"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式解錯，這邊的計算結果應為w=2/3z"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The correct calculation should be w = 2/3z.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 4 % , b ) 18 % , c ) 36 % , d ) 40 % , e ) 50 %"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""given w = 0.6 q , q = 0.6 y , z = 0.54 y , substituting , w = 2 / 3 z - - - - > z = 1.5 w and thus z is 50 % greater than w . e is the correct answer ."", ""error_equation"": ""w=\\frac{0.6}{0.54} \\times 0.6 z \\\\ & 15 w=z"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The correct calculation should be w = 2/3z."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式解錯，這邊的計算結果應為w=2/3z""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4eb75691f0e82034,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"tickets to a certain concert sell for $ 20 each . the first 10 people to show up at the ticket booth received a 40 % discount , and the next 20 received a 15 % discount . if 50 people bought tickets to the concert , what was the total revenue from ticket sales ?",\begin{aligned} & 10 \times 0.4 \times 20+20 \times 0.15 \times 20+(50-10-20) \times 20 \\ = & 80+60+400 \\ = & 540 \text { (dollars) } \end{aligned},Adds discount amounts instead of subtracting them from full prices,10 \times 0.4 \times 20+20 \times 0.15 \times 20+(50-10-20) \times 20,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"discount, from",True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""540"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 10106, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\times 0.4 \\times 20+20 \\times 0.15 \\times 20+(50-10-20) \\times 20"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算discount方式錯誤，在計算discopunt時，x%discount為物品價格乘上(1-x%)，舉例來說10%discount為物品價格乘上90%，因此正確列式為 10*(1-40%)*20+20*(1-15%)*20+20*20"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the discount is incorrect. When calculating the discount, x% discount is the price of the item multiplied by (1-x%). For example, a 10% discount is the price of the item multiplied by 90%. Therefore, the correct formula is: 10*(1-40%)*20+20*(1-15%)*20+20*20""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 600 , b ) $ 740 , c ) $ 860 , d ) $ 980 , e ) $ 1,140"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""price of 1 ticket = 20 $ revenue generated from sales of first 10 tickets = 10 * ( 60 / 100 * 20 ) = 10 * 12 = 120 revenue generated from sales of next 20 tickets = 20 * ( 85 / 100 * 20 ) = 20 * 17 = 340 revenue generated from sales of last 20 tickets = 20 * 20 = 400 revenue generated from sales of 50 tickets = 120 + 340 + 400 = 860 $ answer c\"""", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\times 0.4 \\times 20+20 \\times 0.15 \\times 20+(50-10-20) \\times 20"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the discount is incorrect. When calculating the discount, x% discount is the price of the item multiplied by (1-x%). For example, a 10% discount is the price of the item multiplied by 90%. Therefore, the correct formula is: 10*(1-40%)*20+20*(1-15%)*20+20*20"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算discount方式錯誤，在計算discopunt時，x%discount為物品價格乘上(1-x%)，舉例來說10%discount為物品價格乘上90%，因此正確列式為 10*(1-40%)*20+20*(1-15%)*20+20*20""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4ef12c802ef30af0,full,Comprehension error,"in the game of dubblefud , red chips , blue chips and green chips are each worth 2 , 4 and 5 points respectively . in a certain selection of chips , the product of the point values of the chips is 16000 . if the number of blue chips in this selection doubles the number of green chips , how many red chips are in the selection ?",Assume we have $x$ green chips y red chips $$ \begin{aligned} & 5^x \times 4^{2 x} \times 2^y=16000 \\ & 16000=2^7 \times 5^3 \\ & x=3 \\ & 7-6=1 \\ & y=1 \end{aligned} $$,Mishandles the exponent when rewriting a power of 4 as a power of 2,7-6=1,ok,ok,,10,False,False,True,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""1"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36545, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""5^x \\times 4^{2 x} \\times 2^y=16000"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤導致假設錯誤，題目敘述為藍色籌碼數量是綠色籌碼數量的兩倍，因此正確的假設為5^x*4^2y*2^y = 16000"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The problem understanding is incorrect, leading to incorrect assumptions. The problem statement says that the number of blue chips is double the number of green chips, so the correct assumption should be: 5^x * 4^2y * 2^y = 16000""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 , b ) 2 , c ) 3 , d ) 4 , e ) 5"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""this is equivalent to : - 2 x * 4 y * 5 z = 16000 y / 2 = z ( given ) 2 x * 4 y * 5 y / 2 = 16000 2 x * y ^ 2 = 16000 / 10 2 x * y ^ 2 = 1600 now from options given we will figure out which number will divide 800 and gives us a perfect square : - which gives us x = 2 as 2 * 2 * y ^ 2 = 1600 y ^ 2 = 400 y = 20 number of red chips = 2 hence b"", ""error_equation"": ""5^x \\times 4^{2 x} \\times 2^y=16000"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The problem understanding is incorrect, leading to incorrect assumptions. The problem statement says that the number of blue chips is double the number of green chips, so the correct assumption should be: 5^x * 4^2y * 2^y = 16000"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤導致假設錯誤，題目敘述為藍色籌碼數量是綠色籌碼數量的兩倍，因此正確的假設為5^x*4^2y*2^y = 16000""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f1d8598ca9f9a18,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"if x + ( 1 / x ) = 5 , what is the value q of x ^ 2 + ( 1 / x ) ^ 2 ?",\begin{aligned} & \because x+\frac{1}{x}=5 \\ & \therefore 2 x+\frac{2}{x}=2\left(x+\frac{1}{x}\right)=2 \times 5=10 \end{aligned},Multiplies the sum by two instead of squaring its terms,2 x+\frac{2}{x}=2\left(x+\frac{1}{x}\right)=2 \times 5=10,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""10"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6420, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} 25^{\\wedge} 5 \\times 5^{\\wedge}(-1) & =(125)^{\\wedge} x \\\\ -5 & = x \\end{aligned}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""a^b的運算方式為a的b次方，並不是a*b的意思，舉例來說，x^2=x*x"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The operation of a^b means a to the power of b, not a multiplied by b. For example, x^2 = x * x.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) q = 21 , b ) q = 22 , c ) q = 23 , d ) 24 , e ) 27"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""squaring on both sides , x ^ 2 + ( 1 / x ) ^ 2 + 2 ( x ) ( 1 / x ) = 5 ^ 2 x ^ 2 + ( 1 / x ) ^ 2 = 23 answer : c"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} 25^{\\wedge} 5 \\times 5^{\\wedge}(-1) & =(125)^{\\wedge} x \\\\ -5 & = x \\end{aligned}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The operation of a^b means a to the power of b, not a multiplied by b. For example, x^2 = x * x."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""a^b的運算方式為a的b次方，並不是a*b的意思，舉例來說，x^2=x*x""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f25005c331176f1,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,the sale price sarees listed for rs . 500 after successive discount is 10 % and 5 % is ?,500 \times 10 \% \times 5 \%=500 \times 0.1 \times 0.05=2.5 \text { (rs.) },Multiplies discount percentages instead of applying successive discounts to the price,500 \times 10 \% \times 5\%=500 \times 0.1 \times 0.05=2.5,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,"discount, successive",False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""2.5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35438, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""500 \\times 10 \\% \\times 5 \\%=500 \\times 0.1 \\times 0.05=2.5 \\text { (rs.) }"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算discount方式錯誤，在計算discopunt時，x%discount為物品價格乘上(1-x%)，舉例來說10%discount為物品價格乘上90%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the discount is incorrect. When calculating the discount, x% discount is the price of the item multiplied by (1-x%). For example, a 10% discount is the price of the item multiplied by 90%.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 427.5 , b ) 277 , c ) 342 , d ) 882 , e ) 212"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""500 * ( 90 / 100 ) * ( 95 / 100 ) = 427.5 answer : a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""500 \\times 10 \\% \\times 5 \\%=500 \\times 0.1 \\times 0.05=2.5 \\text { (rs.) }"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the discount is incorrect. When calculating the discount, x% discount is the price of the item multiplied by (1-x%). For example, a 10% discount is the price of the item multiplied by 90%."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算discount方式錯誤，在計算discopunt時，x%discount為物品價格乘上(1-x%)，舉例來說10%discount為物品價格乘上90%""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f4ca9a3fc11c72a,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"alice , benjamin , and carol each try independently to win a carnival game . if their individual probabilities for success are 1 / 5 , 3 / 8 , and 2 / 7 , respectively , what is the probability that exactly two of the 3 players will win but one will lose ?",\begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times\left(1-\frac{2}{7}\right) \\ & =\frac{1}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{5}{7}=\frac{3}{56} \\ & \frac{1}{5} \times\left(1-\frac{3}{8}\right) \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{2}{56} \\ & \left(1-\frac{1}{5}\right) \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{4}{5} \times \frac{3}{8} \times \frac{2}{7} \\ & =\frac{3}{35} \end{aligned} \begin{aligned} & \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{2}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{35} \\ & =\frac{1}{58}+\frac{2}{168}+\frac{3}{105} \\ & =\frac{15+10+24}{840} \\ & =\frac{49}{840} \\ & =\frac{7}{120} \end{aligned},Averages mutually exclusive case probabilities instead of adding them,\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{2}{56}+\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{3}{35},ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,probabilities,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""7/120"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 11936, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{56}+\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{56}+\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{35}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""機率的觀念錯誤，同學在計算各個情形的機率時是拿全局的機率計算的，因此直接將三種情形的機率相加即可，不需要再除以3"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of probability is incorrect. When calculating the probability of each scenario, the student used the overall probability. Therefore, the probabilities of the three scenarios can be directly added together without dividing by 3.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 3 / 140 , b ) 1 / 28 , c ) 3 / 56 , d ) 3 / 35 , e ) 7 / 40"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""p = p ( a wins , b wins , c loses ) + p ( a wins , b loses , c wins ) + p ( a loses , b wins , c wins ) = 1 / 5 * 3 / 8 * 5 / 7 + 1 / 5 * 5 / 8 * 2 / 7 + 4 / 5 * 3 / 8 * 2 / 7 = 7 / 40 . answer : e ."", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{56}+\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{2}{56}+\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{3}{35}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of probability is incorrect. When calculating the probability of each scenario, the student used the overall probability. Therefore, the probabilities of the three scenarios can be directly added together without dividing by 3."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""機率的觀念錯誤，同學在計算各個情形的機率時是拿全局的機率計算的，因此直接將三種情形的機率相加即可，不需要再除以3""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f525b0f6e8f3093,full,Unfinished answer,15 people went to a hotel for combine dinner party 10 of them spent rs . 50 each on their dinner and rest spent 4 more than the average expenditure of all the 15 . what was the total money spent by them .,\begin{aligned} & \frac{50 \times 10+(x+4) \times 5}{15}=x \\ & 15 x=500+5 x+20 \\ & 10 x=520 \\ & x=52 \end{aligned},Finds the average but does not calculate the requested total,& x=52,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""52"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 18154, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確算出平均花費，但還需成以總人數15來計算出總花費，答案為52*15=780"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Calculate the average expenditure correctly, but also multiply it by the total number of people (15) to get the total expenditure. The answer should be 52 * 15 = 780.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1628.4 , b ) 1534 , c ) 780 , d ) 1496 , e ) none of these"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""solution : let average expenditure of 15 people be x . then , 15 x = 10 * 50 + 5 * ( x + 4 ) ; or , 15 x = 10 * 50 + 5 x + 20 ; or , x = 52 ; so , total money spent = 52 * 15 = rs . 780 . answer : option c\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Calculate the average expenditure correctly, but also multiply it by the total number of people (15) to get the total expenditure. The answer should be 52 * 15 = 780."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確算出平均花費，但還需成以總人數15來計算出總花費，答案為52*15=780""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f6ca9daba2114c4,full,Arithmetical error,"in traveling from a dormitory to a certain city , a student went 1 / 4 of the way by foot , 1 / 2 of the way by bus , and the remaining 10 kilometers by car . what is the distance , in kilometers , from the dormitory to the city ?",10 \div\left(1-\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{4}\right)=30,Computes the final division incorrectly,10 \div\left(1-\frac{1}{2}-\frac{1}{4}\right)=30,ok,ok,,5,False,False,False,,True,4,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""30"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 1860, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\div\\left(1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=30"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確運算結果為40"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The correct answer should be 40.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 10 , b ) 45 , c ) 30 , d ) 20 , e ) 40"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""whole trip = distance by foot + distance by bus + distance by car x = 1 / 4 x + 1 / 2 x + 10 x - 1 / 4 x - 1 / 2 x = 10 x = 40 km option : e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""10 \\div\\left(1-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right)=30"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The correct answer should be 40."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確運算結果為40""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4f940c1f0d861638,full,Algebraic error,"the length of the bridge , which a train 160 meters long and travelling at 45 km / hr can cross in 30 seconds , is :",train speed: $45 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr}=45000 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{hr}=12.5 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec}$ assume bridge length is $x$. $$ \begin{aligned} (160+x) \div 12.5 & =30 \\ x & =3750-160 \\ x & =3590(\mathrm{~m}) \end{aligned} $$,Miscomputes the product of speed and time by a factor of ten,x =3750-160,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""3590"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6936, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Algebraic error"", ""error_equation"": ""(160+x) \\div 12.5 & =30 \\\\ x & =3750-160"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式運算錯誤，正確應為x=375-160，同學375算乘3750導致錯誤"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. It should be x = 375 - 160. The student multiplied 375 by 3750, which is incorrect.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 230 , b ) 244 , c ) 245 , d ) 215 , e ) 236"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""speed = ( 45 * 5 / 18 ) m / sec = ( 25 / 2 ) m / sec . time = 30 sec . let the length of bridge be x meters . then , ( 160 + x ) / 30 = 25 / 2 = = > 2 ( 160 + x ) = 750 = = > x = 215 m . answer : option d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""(160+x) \\div 12.5 & =30 \\\\ x & =3750-160"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. It should be x = 375 - 160. The student multiplied 375 by 3750, which is incorrect."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式運算錯誤，正確應為x=375-160，同學375算乘3750導致錯誤""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:4fa6e264b58be8ff,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"let s be the set of all positive integers that , when divided by 8 , have a remainder of 5 . what is the 75 th number in this set ?",8 \times 75+5=605,Fails to subtract one when finding the nth term of a sequence,8 \times 75+5=605,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,when,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""605"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 16132, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""8 \\times 75+5=605"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""要計算第75個數時，中間的差為(75-1)*8而不是75*8，因此正確為8*74+5=597"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To calculate the 75th number, the difference between the numbers is (75-1)*8, not 75*8. Therefore, the correct answer is 8*74+5=597.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 597 , b ) 608 , c ) 613 , d ) 616 , e ) 621"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""the set s = { 5 , 13 , 21 , 29 , . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . . } 1 st number = 8 * 0 + 5 = 5 2 nd number = 8 * 1 + 5 = 13 3 rd number = 8 * 2 + 5 = 21 75 th number = 8 * ( 75 - 1 ) + 5 = 597 answer = a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""8 \\times 75+5=605"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To calculate the 75th number, the difference between the numbers is (75-1)*8, not 75*8. Therefore, the correct answer is 8*74+5=597."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""要計算第75個數時，中間的差為(75-1)*8而不是75*8，因此正確為8*74+5=597""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:50bf865b955254e7,full,Arithmetical error,( 0.0066 ) ( 3.6 ) / ( 0.04 ) ( 0.1 ) ( 0.006 ) =,\frac{0.0066 \times 3.6}{0.04 \times 0.1 \times 0.006}=11,Makes an arithmetic error when evaluating the decimal quotient,\frac{0.0066 \times 3.6}{0.04 \times 0.1 \times 0.006}=11,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""11"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35286, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{0.0066 \\times 3.6}{0.04 \\times 0.1 \\times 0.006}=11"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確計算結果為990"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The correct answer is 990.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 990 , b ) 99.0 , c ) 9.9 , d ) 0.99 , e ) 0.099"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""( 0.0066 ) ( 3.6 ) / ( 0.04 ) ( 0.1 ) ( 0.006 ) = 0.0060 * 360 / 4 * ( 0.1 ) ( 0.006 ) = 0.066 * 90 / 1 * 0.006 = 66 * 90 / 6 = 11 * 90 = 990 answer : a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{0.0066 \\times 3.6}{0.04 \\times 0.1 \\times 0.006}=11"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The correct answer is 990."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確計算結果為990""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:512ace580d9c9230,full,Comprehension error,the simple interest and the true discount on a certain sum for a given time and at a given rate are rs . 90 and rs . 80 respectively . the sum is :,"assume the sum x,rate = i \\\begin{aligned} & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x \times\left(1+i \right)=90 \\ \frac{x}{(1+i)}=80 \end{array}\right. \\ & \left\{\begin{array}{l} x=\frac{90}{1+i} \\ x=80 \times\left(1+i \right) \end{array}\right. \\ & \frac{90}{1+i }=80\left(1+i \right) \end{aligned}\begin{aligned} & \left(1+i \right)^2=\frac{9}{8} \\ & 1+i=\frac{3}{\sqrt{8}} \\ & x=80 \times \frac{3}{\sqrt{8}} \\ & =80 \times \frac{3 \sqrt{2}}{2 \sqrt{2} \times \sqrt{2}} \\ & =60 \sqrt{2} \end{aligned}",Treats interest and discount amounts as total accumulated or present values,x \times\left(1+i \right)=90 \quad \frac{x}{(1+i)}=80,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,discount,False,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""60 \\sqrt{2}"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36160, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""x \\times\\left(1+i \\right)=90"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，90為利息的值而不是本金加利息的總和，正確假設應為x*i=90"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is incorrectly interpreted. 90 is the value of interest, not the sum of principal and interest. The correct assumption should be x*i=90""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1360 , b ) 1450 , c ) 720 , d ) 1800 , e ) none"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""sol . sum = s . i . * t . d . / ( s . i ) - ( t . d . ) = 90 * 80 / ( 90 - 80 ) = rs . 720 . answer c\"""", ""error_equation"": ""x \\times\\left(1+i \\right)=90"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The question is incorrectly interpreted. 90 is the value of interest, not the sum of principal and interest. The correct assumption should be x*i=90"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""題目理解錯誤，90為利息的值而不是本金加利息的總和，正確假設應為x*i=90""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:51a4277b4149cb52,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in 10 years , a will be twice as old as b was 10 years ago . if a is now 8 years older than b the present age of b is","$$ \begin{aligned} & a=b+8 \\ & (a+10) \times 2=(b-10) \\ & 2 a+20=b-10 \\ & 2(b+8)+20=b-10 \\ & b=-46 \end{aligned} $$  No solution, $b$ can't be -46 years old",Reverses the doubling relationship between the two quantities,(a+10) \times 2=(b-10),ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""none"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9945, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""(a+10) \\times 2=(b-10)"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式假設錯誤，題目敘述為10年後，a的年齡將是10年前b的兩倍，因此正確列式應為a+10 = 2*(b-10)，解出方程式後即可得出答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrectly set up. The problem states that in 10 years, a will be twice as old as b was 10 years ago. Therefore, the correct equation should be a+10 = 2*(b-10). Solving this equation will give you the answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 37 , b ) 38 , c ) 39 , d ) 40 , e ) 41"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""let present age of a be a and b be b a + 10 = 2 * ( b - 10 ) = > 2 b - a = 30 . . . . . . ( i ) a = b + 8 = > 2 b - b - 8 = 30 b = 38 so the present age of b is 38 years answer : b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""(a+10) \\times 2=(b-10)"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrectly set up. The problem states that in 10 years, a will be twice as old as b was 10 years ago. Therefore, the correct equation should be a+10 = 2*(b-10). Solving this equation will give you the answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式假設錯誤，題目敘述為10年後，a的年齡將是10年前b的兩倍，因此正確列式應為a+10 = 2*(b-10)，解出方程式後即可得出答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:51caddbe0ce317db,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"x , y , and z are different prime numbers . the product x ^ 2 * y * z is divisible by how many different positive numbers ?","$$ \begin{aligned} & 1,x , x^2 , x y , x^2 y , x z ,x^2 z , y z, y , z , x^2 y z \end{aligned} $$  A:11",Omits a divisor formed by multiplying all distinct prime factors,"1,x , x^2 , x y , x^2 y , x z ,x^2 z , y z, y , z , x^2 y z",ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,prime,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""11"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 16016, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""A:11"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學少考慮了xyz也為x ^ 2 * y * z的因數導致錯誤，正確因數數量為11+1=12"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Students forgot to consider that xyz is also a factor of x^2 * y * z, which led to an incorrect answer. The correct number of factors is 11 + 1 = 12.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 4 , b ) 6 , c ) 8 , d ) 9 , e ) 12"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""the exponents of x ^ 2 * y * z are 2 , 1 , and 1 . the number of factors is ( 2 + 1 ) ( 1 + 1 ) ( 1 + 1 ) = 12 the answer is e ."", ""error_equation"": ""A:11"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Students forgot to consider that xyz is also a factor of x^2 * y * z, which led to an incorrect answer. The correct number of factors is 11 + 1 = 12."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學少考慮了xyz也為x ^ 2 * y * z的因數導致錯誤，正確因數數量為11+1=12""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:51d78174aae75593,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"suresh started a business , investing rs . 18000 . after 3 months and 4 months respectively , rohan and sudhir joined him with capitals of 12000 and 9000 . at the end of the year the total profit was rs . 3960 . what is the difference between rohan ’ s and sudhir ’ s share in the profit ?",$18000+12000+9000=39000 \Rightarrow$ total capital $12-3=9 \Rightarrow$ the time rohan have joined until the end of the year. $12-4=8 \Rightarrow$ the time sudhir have joined until the end of the year. the rohan's share in the profit $$ \Rightarrow 3960 \times \frac{12000}{39000} \times \frac{9}{12}=396 \times \frac{1000}{3900} \times 9=66 \times \frac{9000}{650} = 913.85 $$ the sudhir's share in the profit $$ \begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow 3960 \times \frac{9000}{39000} \times \frac{8}{12}=1300 \times \frac{18000}{39000}=1320 \times \frac{6}{13} = 609.23 \\ & 913.85-609.23=304.62 \end{aligned} $$,Uses total capital instead of total capital–time contributions as the sharing denominator,3960 \times \frac{12000}{39000} \times \frac{9}{12},ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""304.62"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 5022, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""the rohan's share in the profit $$ \\Rightarrow 3960 \\times \\frac{12000}{39000} \\times \\frac{9}{12}=396 \\times \\frac{1000}{3900} \\times 9=66 \\times \\frac{9000}{650} = 913.85 $$ the sudhir's share in the profit $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 3960 \\times \\frac{9000}{39000} \\times \\frac{8}{12}=1300 \\times \\frac{18000}{39000}=1320 \\times \\frac{6}{13} = 609.23 \\\\ & 913.85-609.23=304.62 \\end{aligned} $$"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤的方式錯誤，應該先計算出每個人投資金額成上時間的比例，再以總金額來做計算"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The method of calculating the profit is incorrect. First, you should calculate the ratio of each person's investment amount to the time, and then calculate it with the total amount.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) s . 345 , b ) s . 350 , c ) s . 352 , d ) s . 360 , e ) s . 368"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""suresh : rohan : sudhir ratio of their investments = 18000 × 12 : 12000 × 9 : 9000 × 8 = 6 : 3 : 2 the difference between rohan ’ s and sudhir ’ s share = 1 share : . i . e . = rs . 3960 × 1 / 11 = rs . 360 . d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""the rohan's share in the profit $$ \\Rightarrow 3960 \\times \\frac{12000}{39000} \\times \\frac{9}{12}=396 \\times \\frac{1000}{3900} \\times 9=66 \\times \\frac{9000}{650} = 913.85 $$ the sudhir's share in the profit $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 3960 \\times \\frac{9000}{39000} \\times \\frac{8}{12}=1300 \\times \\frac{18000}{39000}=1320 \\times \\frac{6}{13} = 609.23 \\\\ & 913.85-609.23=304.62 \\end{aligned} $$"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The method of calculating the profit is incorrect. First, you should calculate the ratio of each person's investment amount to the time, and then calculate it with the total amount."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤的方式錯誤，應該先計算出每個人投資金額成上時間的比例，再以總金額來做計算""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:51f3851a0d4d797f,full,Arithmetical error,at what rate percent on simple interest will rs . 750 amount to rs . 825 in 5 years ?,\begin{aligned} & \frac{825-750}{5}=25 \\ & \frac{25}{750}=\frac{1}{30}=3.333 \% \end{aligned},Makes an arithmetic error when dividing the total interest by time,\frac{825-750}{5}=25,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""3.333"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34639, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{825-750}{5}=25"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確運算結果為15"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Incorrect calculation. The correct answer is 15%.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 2 , b ) 3 , c ) 4 , d ) 5 , e ) 6"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""75 = ( 750 * 5 * r ) / 100 r = 2 % . answer : a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{825-750}{5}=25"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Incorrect calculation. The correct answer is 15%."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，正確運算結果為15""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:52d3bd3d07a1db8c,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in the xy - plane , a triangle has vertices ( 0,0 ) , ( 4,0 ) and ( 4,10 ) . if a point ( a , b ) is selected at random from the triangular region , what is the probability that a - b > 0 ?",$4 \times 10 \div 2=20$ $$ (1+2+3) \div 20=\frac{3}{10}=0.3=30 \% $$,Calculates favorable area by summing values instead of finding the region’s area.,(1+2+3) \div 20=\frac{3}{10}=0.3=30 \%,ok,ok,,12,False,False,False,region,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""30"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 959, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""(1+2+3) \\div 20=\\frac{3}{10}=0.3=30 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算a-b>0時三角形面積的方式錯誤，a-b>0代表三角形在x=y線下的面積，也就是 ( 1 / 2 ) ( 4 ) ( 4 ) = 8"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The teacher's suggestion is that the calculation of the area when a-b>0 is incorrect. a-b>0 represents the area of the triangle below the line x=y, which is (1/2) * (4) * (4) = 8.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 / 5 , b ) 1 / 3 , c ) 1 / 2 , d ) 2 / 3 , e ) 2 / 5"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""geometry"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""the area of the right triangle is ( 1 / 2 ) * 4 * 10 = 20 . only the points ( a , b ) below the line y = x satisfy a - b > 0 . the part of the triangle which is below the line y = x has an area of ( 1 / 2 ) ( 4 ) ( 4 ) = 8 . p ( a - b > 0 ) = 8 / 20 = 2 / 5 the answer is e ."", ""error_equation"": ""(1+2+3) \\div 20=\\frac{3}{10}=0.3=30 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The teacher's suggestion is that the calculation of the area when a-b>0 is incorrect. a-b>0 represents the area of the triangle below the line x=y, which is (1/2) * (4) * (4) = 8."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算a-b>0時三角形面積的方式錯誤，a-b>0代表三角形在x=y線下的面積，也就是 ( 1 / 2 ) ( 4 ) ( 4 ) = 8""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:52d9896852f60d98,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,a ball dropped from h height and moves 80 % of height each time . total distance covered is,h,Fails to sum the repeated distances in the geometric sequence,h,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 6, ""student_answer"": ""h"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 17329, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""h"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""這題考的是等比數列，等比數列和的公式為Sn=(a1(1-r^n))/(1-r)，Sn為總和，a1為首項，r為公比，因此正確計算方法為first time distance is h second time 80 h / 100 = 4 h / 5 similarly third time 80 % of 4 h / 5 = h ( 4 ^ 2 ) / ( 5 ^ 2 ) and so on . . . this will lead to infinite terms of geometric progression i . e h + 2 * 4 h / 5 + 2 * 16 h / 25 . . . . . . . . . . . . sum = h + 2 * 4 h / ( 5 ( 1 - 4 / 5 ) ) = 9 h answer : d"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""This question tests geometric progression. The formula for the sum of a geometric progression is Sn=(a1(1-r^n))/(1-r), where Sn is the sum, a1 is the first term, and r is the common ratio. Therefore, the correct calculation method is: first time distance is h second time 80 h / 100 = 4 h / 5 similarly third time 80 % of 4 h / 5 = h ( 4 ^ 2 ) / ( 5 ^ 2 ) and so on . . . this will lead to infinite terms of geometric progression i . e h + 2 * 4 h / 5 + 2 * 16 h / 25 . . . . . . . . . . . . sum = h + 2 * 4 h / ( 5 ( 1 - 4 / 5 ) ) = 9 h answer : d""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 4 h , b ) 5 h , c ) 7 h , d ) 9 h , e ) 8 h"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""first time distance is h second time 80 h / 100 = 4 h / 5 similarly third time 80 % of 4 h / 5 = h ( 4 ^ 2 ) / ( 5 ^ 2 ) and so on . . . this will lead to infinite terms of geometric progression i . e h + 2 * 4 h / 5 + 2 * 16 h / 25 . . . . . . . . . . . . sum = h + 2 * 4 h / ( 5 ( 1 - 4 / 5 ) ) = 9 h answer : d"", ""error_equation"": ""h"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""This question tests geometric progression. The formula for the sum of a geometric progression is Sn=(a1(1-r^n))/(1-r), where Sn is the sum, a1 is the first term, and r is the common ratio. Therefore, the correct calculation method is: first time distance is h second time 80 h / 100 = 4 h / 5 similarly third time 80 % of 4 h / 5 = h ( 4 ^ 2 ) / ( 5 ^ 2 ) and so on . . . this will lead to infinite terms of geometric progression i . e h + 2 * 4 h / 5 + 2 * 16 h / 25 . . . . . . . . . . . . sum = h + 2 * 4 h / ( 5 ( 1 - 4 / 5 ) ) = 9 h answer : d"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""這題考的是等比數列，等比數列和的公式為Sn=(a1(1-r^n))/(1-r)，Sn為總和，a1為首項，r為公比，因此正確計算方法為first time distance is h second time 80 h / 100 = 4 h / 5 similarly third time 80 % of 4 h / 5 = h ( 4 ^ 2 ) / ( 5 ^ 2 ) and so on . . . this will lead to infinite terms of geometric progression i . e h + 2 * 4 h / 5 + 2 * 16 h / 25 . . . . . . . . . . . . sum = h + 2 * 4 h / ( 5 ( 1 - 4 / 5 ) ) = 9 h answer : d""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:534da0713265c56e,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"frank the fencemaker needs to fence in a rectangular yard . he fences in the entire yard , except for one full side of the yard , which equals 40 feet . the yard has an area of 320 square feet . how many feet offence does frank use ?",\begin{aligned} & 320 \div 40=8 \\ & (40+8) \times 2=96 \end{aligned},Calculates the full perimeter instead of excluding the unfenced side,(40+8) \times 2=96,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"full, side",True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""96"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 2440, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""(40+8) \\times 2=96"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出庭院的寬，但在計算柵欄長度時出錯，有一邊長度40的邊不用設置，應此需要設置三邊柵欄，正確長度應為8+8+40=56"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student correctly calculated the width of the yard, but made an error in calculating the length of the fence. Since one side of the yard is already 40 feet long and does not require fencing, Frank only needs to fence the other three sides. The correct length of the fence should be 8 + 8 + 40 = 56 feet.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 14 , b ) 47 , c ) 54 , d ) 56 , e ) 240"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""geometry"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""area = length x breadth 320 = 40 x breadth so , breadth = 8 units fencing required is - breadth + breadth + length 8 + 8 + 40 = > 56 feet answer must be ( d ) 56\"""", ""error_equation"": ""(40+8) \\times 2=96"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student correctly calculated the width of the yard, but made an error in calculating the length of the fence. Since one side of the yard is already 40 feet long and does not require fencing, Frank only needs to fence the other three sides. The correct length of the fence should be 8 + 8 + 40 = 56 feet."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出庭院的寬，但在計算柵欄長度時出錯，有一邊長度40的邊不用設置，應此需要設置三邊柵欄，正確長度應為8+8+40=56""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:538a10c647626eec,full,Measurement error,"the price of commodity x increases by 40 paise every year , while the price of commodity y increases by 15 paise every year . if in 2001 , the price of commodity x was rs . 4.20 and that of y was rs . 6.30 , in which year commodity x will cost 40 paise more than the commodity y ?",Assume after $x$ years $$ \begin{aligned} & 4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40 \\ & 25 x=42.1 \\ & x=1.684 \end{aligned} $$,Mixes rupees and paise without converting units,4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,paise,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""1.684"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36570, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Measurement error"", ""error_equation"": ""4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""單位不一致時直接運算導致錯誤，可以先將盧比轉換為派薩，轉換的比值為1盧比=100派薩，因此正確方程式為420+40x=630+15x+40"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""When the units are different, direct calculation will lead to errors. You can convert rupees to paise first. The conversion ratio is 1 rupee = 100 paise. Therefore, the correct equation is 420 + 40x = 630 + 15x + 40.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 2010 , b ) 2001 , c ) 2012 , d ) 2011 , e ) 2009"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""suppose commodity x will cost 40 paise more than y after z years . then , ( 4.20 + 0.40 z ) - ( 6.30 + 0.15 z ) = 0.40 0.25 z = 0.40 + 2.10 z = 2.50 / 0.25 = 250 / 25 = 10 . therefore , x will cost 40 paise more than y 10 years after 2001 i . e . , 2011 . answer is d .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""4.2+40 x=6.3+15 x+40"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""When the units are different, direct calculation will lead to errors. You can convert rupees to paise first. The conversion ratio is 1 rupee = 100 paise. Therefore, the correct equation is 420 + 40x = 630 + 15x + 40."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""單位不一致時直接運算導致錯誤，可以先將盧比轉換為派薩，轉換的比值為1盧比=100派薩，因此正確方程式為420+40x=630+15x+40""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:53b71796de6fb11c,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"there are certain number of hats and gloves in a box . they are of 41 red , 23 green , 11 orange . power gone but a woman can differentiate between hats and gloves . how many draws are required to obtain a pair of each color ?",the worst situation i only have one red glove $40+23+11=74$,Does not identify the latest draw needed to complete all pairs,the worst situation i only have one red glove $40+23+11=74$,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""74"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 12568, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""the worst situation i only have one red glove $40+23+11=74$"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""不可直接將所有數量和來當作抽取次數，應該要考慮最差情況為何，最糟的情況是先取 40 紅色，再取 22 綠色，再取 1 + 1 紅色 + 綠色，再取 2 橘色。 所以總共 40 + 22 + 2 + 2 = 66次"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Do not directly add up all the quantities as the number of draws. Instead, consider the worst-case scenario. The worst case is to first draw 40 red, then 22 green, then 1 + 1 red + green, and then 2 orange. Therefore, the total number of draws is 40 + 22 + 2 + 2 = 66.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 66 , b ) 67 , c ) 68 , d ) 69 , e ) 70"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""the worst case senario will be first take 40 red then take 22 green then take 1 + 1 red + green then take 2 orange . so total 40 + 22 + 2 + 2 = 66 answer : a"", ""error_equation"": ""the worst situation i only have one red glove $40+23+11=74$"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Do not directly add up all the quantities as the number of draws. Instead, consider the worst-case scenario. The worst case is to first draw 40 red, then 22 green, then 1 + 1 red + green, and then 2 orange. Therefore, the total number of draws is 40 + 22 + 2 + 2 = 66."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""不可直接將所有數量和來當作抽取次數，應該要考慮最差情況為何，最糟的情況是先取 40 紅色，再取 22 綠色，再取 1 + 1 紅色 + 綠色，再取 2 橘色。 所以總共 40 + 22 + 2 + 2 = 66次""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:53ceb4b5e186cda7,full,Unfinished answer,two stations p and q are 155 km apart on a straight track . one train starts from p at 7 a . m . and travels towards q at 20 kmph . another train starts from q at 8 a . m . and travels towards p at a speed of 25 kmph . at what time will they meet ?,\begin{aligned} & 155-20 \times 1=135 \\ & 135 \div(20+25)=3 \end{aligned},Fails to convert elapsed travel time into the requested clock time,135 \div(20+25)=3,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""3"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34750, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""有正確計算出所需的時間，但還需要算出他們在幾點相遇"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The time taken has been correctly calculated, but it is also necessary to find the time at which they meet.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 10 am , b ) 12 am , c ) 10.30 am , d ) 12.30 am , e ) 11 am"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""assume both trains meet after x hours after 7 am distance covered by train starting from p in x hours = 20 x km distance covered by train starting from q in ( x - 1 ) hours = 25 ( x - 1 ) total distance = 155 = > 20 x + 25 ( x - 1 ) = 155 = > 45 x = 180 = > x = 4 means , they meet after 3 hours after 7 am , ie , they meet at 11 am answer is e .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The time taken has been correctly calculated, but it is also necessary to find the time at which they meet."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""有正確計算出所需的時間，但還需要算出他們在幾點相遇""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:54b3fea580827339,full,Unfinished answer,"if n is a positive integer greater than 1 , then p ( n ) represents the product of all the prime numbers less than or equal to n . the second smallest prime factor of p ( 12 ) + 11 is","the prime numbers less than or equal to $12: 2.3,5,7,11$ $$ p(12)=2 \times 3 \times 5 \times 7 \times 11=2310 $$ the prime factor of 11 is 11 only. $$ p(12)+11=2310+11=2321 \# $$",Stops after computing the sum without finding its prime factors,p(12)+11=2310+11=2321 #,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,prime,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""2321"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 8637, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出p(12)+11的值，但還需求出他第二小的質因數"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To correctly calculate the value of p(12) + 11, you also need to find its second smallest prime factor.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 2 , b ) 11 , c ) 13 , d ) 17 , e ) 211"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""p ( 12 ) + 11 = 2 ∗ 3 ∗ 5 ∗ 7 ∗ 11 + 11 = 11 ( 2 ∗ 3 ∗ 5 ∗ 7 + 1 ) = 11 ∗ 211 . both 11 and 211 are primes : 11 is the smallest prime of p ( 12 ) + 11 and 211 is the second smallest prime of p ( 12 ) + 11 . answer : e ."", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To correctly calculate the value of p(12) + 11, you also need to find its second smallest prime factor."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確計算出p(12)+11的值，但還需求出他第二小的質因數""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:54f7718738a5a8d2,full,Algebraic error,the average weight of 8 persons increases by 3 kg when a new person comes in place of one of them weighing 65 kg . what might be the weight of the new person ?,assume the weight of the new person X kg original average weigh y $\mathrm{kg}$ $$ \begin{aligned} & y+3=\frac{8 y-65+x}{8} \\ & 8 y+3=8 y-65+x \\ & x=68(\mathrm{~kg}) \end{aligned} $$,Fails to multiply every term by the denominator when clearing fractions,& 8 y+3=8 y-65+x,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,when,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""68"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 11371, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Algebraic error"", ""error_equation"": ""y+3=\\frac{8 y-65+x}{8} \\\\ & 8 y+3=8 y-65+x"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式運算錯誤，等號左側的y+3在乘以八時運算錯誤，正確過程為8*(y+3) = 8y+24"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The left side of the equation, y+3, is multiplied by eight incorrectly. The correct calculation should be 8*(y+3) = 8y+24.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 75 kg , b ) 65 kg , c ) 55 kg , d ) 89 kg , e ) 25 kg"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""total weight increased = ( 8 x 3 ) kg = 24 kg . weight of new person = ( 65 + 24 ) kg = 89 kg . answer : d"", ""error_equation"": ""y+3=\\frac{8 y-65+x}{8} \\\\ & 8 y+3=8 y-65+x"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The left side of the equation, y+3, is multiplied by eight incorrectly. The correct calculation should be 8*(y+3) = 8y+24."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""方程式運算錯誤，等號左側的y+3在乘以八時運算錯誤，正確過程為8*(y+3) = 8y+24""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:560b6d8bcc938b06,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,if a man lost 4 % by selling oranges at the rate of 48 a rupee at how many a rupee must he sell them to gain 44 % ?,assume the cost $x$ $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{x-48}{48}=4 \% \\ & x=67.2 \end{aligned} $$ selling at y $$ \begin{aligned} & \frac{y-67-2}{y}=44 \% \\ & 0.56 y=67.2 \\ & y=120(rs) \end{aligned} $$,Applies percentage changes directly to a reciprocal rate instead of unit price.,\frac{x-48}{48}=4 \%,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""120"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 36341, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""selling at y $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y-67-2}{y}=44 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤比例的觀念錯誤，計算利潤時應將成本當作基準，而不是售價當作基準"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit margin is incorrect. When calculating profit, the cost should be used as the benchmark, not the selling price.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1 , b ) 8 , c ) 9 , d ) 4 , e ) 32"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""96 % - - - - 48 144 % - - - - ? 96 / 144 * 48 = 32 answer : e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""selling at y $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\frac{y-67-2}{y}=44 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept of calculating the profit margin is incorrect. When calculating profit, the cost should be used as the benchmark, not the selling price."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算利潤比例的觀念錯誤，計算利潤時應將成本當作基準，而不是售價當作基準""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5637f55fc70897af,full,Comprehension error,"a man ' s regular pay is $ 3 per hour up to 40 hours . overtime is twice the payment for regular time . if he was paid $ 168 , how many hours overtime did he work ?",over time $x$ hours $$ \begin{aligned} & 3  \times (40-x)+6 \times x=168 \\ & x=16 \end{aligned} $$,Subtracts overtime hours from regular hours instead of adding them,3  \times (40-x)+6 \times x=168,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"overtime, regular",True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""16"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 1611, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""over time $x$ hours $$ \\begin{aligned} & 3  \\times (40-x)+6 \\times x=168"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""40小時是指不包含加班的最大時數，因此正常工資的薪資應為3*40=120，加班薪資為168-120=2*3*x"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""40 hours is the maximum number of hours without overtime, so the regular pay should be 3*40=120. The overtime pay is 168-120=2*3*x""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 8 , b ) 21 , c ) 14 , d ) 12 , e ) 15"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""answer is : b at $ 3 per hour up to 40 hours , regular pay = $ 3 x 40 = $ 120 if total pay = $ 168 , overtime pay = $ 168 - $ 120 = $ 48 overtime rate ( twice regular ) = 2 x $ 3 = $ 6 per hour = > number of overtime hours = $ 48 / $ 6 = 8\"""", ""error_equation"": ""over time $x$ hours $$ \\begin{aligned} & 3  \\times (40-x)+6 \\times x=168"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""40 hours is the maximum number of hours without overtime, so the regular pay should be 3*40=120. The overtime pay is 168-120=2*3*x"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""40小時是指不包含加班的最大時數，因此正常工資的薪資應為3*40=120，加班薪資為168-120=2*3*x""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:563a7de2ad38766c,full,Arithmetical error,a bus 75 m long is running with a speed of 21 km / hr . in what time will it pass a woman who is walking at 3 km / hr in the direction opposite to that in which the bus is going ?,$21+3=24 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \Rightarrow$ the decrease of distance between the bus \& woman. $$ \begin{aligned} & 24 \mathrm{~km} / \mathrm{hr} \\ & =(2400 \div 60 \div 60) \mathrm{m} / \mathrm{sec} \\ & =\frac{20}{3} \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} \\ & 75 \div \frac{20}{3} \\ & =500 \text { seconds. } \end{aligned} $$,Makes an arithmetic error when dividing distance by relative speed,75 \div \frac{20}{3} =500 \text { seconds. },ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,False,5,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""500"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35099, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""75 \\div \\frac{20}{3} \\\\ & =500 \\text { seconds. } \\"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，同學把除號當成乘來運算，正確運算結果為11.25"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The student mistook the division sign for a multiplication sign. The correct result is 11.25.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 5.75 , b ) 7.62 , c ) 11.25 , d ) 4.25 , e ) 3.25"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""speed of bus relative to woman = 21 + 3 = 24 km / hr . = 24 * 5 / 18 = 20 / 3 m / sec . time taken to pass the woman = 75 * 3 / 20 = 11.25 sec . answer : c\"""", ""error_equation"": ""75 \\div \\frac{20}{3} \\\\ & =500 \\text { seconds. } \\"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The student mistook the division sign for a multiplication sign. The correct result is 11.25."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，同學把除號當成乘來運算，正確運算結果為11.25""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5641a39689dbcfec,full,Measurement error,area of a square is 1 / 2 hectare . the diagonal of the square is ?,the side length of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}}$ the diagonal of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}} \times \sqrt{2}=1$,Fails to convert area units into corresponding length units,the diagonal of the square is $\sqrt{\frac{1}{2}} \times \sqrt{2}=1$,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""1"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 15042, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Measurement error"", ""error_equation"": ""the side length of the square is $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}$"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""運算前應先進行單位轉換，轉換的比值為1公頃為10000平方公尺，因此1/2公頃為10000 / 2  = 5000 平方公尺，轉換後再進行對角線的運算"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Before calculation, unit conversion should be performed first. The conversion ratio is 1 hectare to 10,000 square meters. Therefore, 1/2 hectare is 10,000 / 2 = 5,000 square meters. After conversion, the diagonal calculation can be performed.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""['a ) 250 meter', 'b ) 100 meter', 'c ) 50 √ 2 meter', 'd ) 50 meter', 'e ) 35 meter']"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""geometry"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""area = 1 / 2 hectare = 10000 / 2 m 2 = 5000 m 2 again area = 1 / 2 x ( diagonal ) 2 so 1 / 2 x ( diagonal ) 2 = 5000 m 2 diagonal 2 = 10000 diagonal = 100 answer : b"", ""error_equation"": ""the side length of the square is $\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{2}}$"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Before calculation, unit conversion should be performed first. The conversion ratio is 1 hectare to 10,000 square meters. Therefore, 1/2 hectare is 10,000 / 2 = 5,000 square meters. After conversion, the diagonal calculation can be performed."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""運算前應先進行單位轉換，轉換的比值為1公頃為10000平方公尺，因此1/2公頃為10000 / 2  = 5000 平方公尺，轉換後再進行對角線的運算""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:566036ac5809fa3d,full,Unfinished answer,the s . i . on a certain sum of money for 5 years at 6 % per annum is half the c . i . on rs . 3000 for 2 years at 15 % per annum . the sum placed on s . i . is ?,\begin{aligned} & (3000) \times(1.15)^2 \\ & =3000 \times(1.3225) \\ & =3967.5 \end{aligned},Stops after finding a compound amount instead of completing the requested calculation,=3000 \times(1.3225) \\ & =3967.5,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""3967.5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 35142, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Unfinished answer"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確算出複利後的值，但還需繼續求出單利的本金為多少"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Calculate the correct value of compound interest first, and then continue to calculate the principal amount of simple interest.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 1525.2 , b ) 1256.3 , c ) 1612.5 , d ) 1548.5 , e ) 1254.5"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""c . i . = [ 3000 * ( 1 + 15 / 100 ) 2 - 3000 ] = ( 3000 * 23 / 20 * 23 / 20 - 3000 ) = rs . 967.5 . sum = ( 483.75 * 100 ) / ( 5 * 6 ) = rs . 1612.5 answer : c"", ""error_equation"": ""None"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Calculate the correct value of compound interest first, and then continue to calculate the principal amount of simple interest."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""正確算出複利後的值，但還需繼續求出單利的本金為多少""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:566e31cbe5deb2a5,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,a container contains 40 litres of milk . from this container 4 litres of milk was taken out and replaced by water . this process was repeated further two times . how much milk is now contained by the container ?,40-4 \times 3=28,Treats repeated replacement as simple subtraction instead of dilution,40-4 \times 3=28,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,repeated,True,1,"{""student_id"": 1, ""student_answer"": ""28"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 2024, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""40-4 \\times 3=28"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有考慮到加入水後，取出的四公溶液也會取到水，因此應計算出每次取出溶液中牛奶的比例才可得出正確答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not consider that after adding water, the four liters of solution taken out would also contain water. Therefore, the proportion of milk in the solution taken out each time should be calculated to obtain the correct answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 26.34 litres , b ) 27.36 litres , c ) 28 litres , d ) 29.16 litres , e ) 30 litres"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""d"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""amount of milk left after 3 operations = [ 40 ( 1 - 4 / 40 ) ^ 3 ] litres = 40 x 9 / 10 x 9 / 10 x 9 / 10 = 29.16 litres answer : d\"""", ""error_equation"": ""40-4 \\times 3=28"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not consider that after adding water, the four liters of solution taken out would also contain water. Therefore, the proportion of milk in the solution taken out each time should be calculated to obtain the correct answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有考慮到加入水後，取出的四公溶液也會取到水，因此應計算出每次取出溶液中牛奶的比例才可得出正確答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:59163c137d70538a,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in a fuel station the service costs $ 2.20 per vehicle and every liter of fuel costs $ 0.70 . assuming that you fill up 3 mini - vans and 2 trucks , what will be the total cost , if a mini - van ' s tank is 65 liters and a truck ' s tank is 120 % bigger and they are all empty ?",the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \times 120 \%=78$ $$ \begin{aligned} \text { the total cost } & =2.20(3+2)+0.7[(3 \times 65)+(2 \times 78)] \\ & =11+245.7 \\ & =256.7(\$) \end{aligned} $$,Treats a quantity that is 120% bigger as merely 120% of the original,the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \times 120 \%=78$,ok,ok,,10,False,False,True,"bigger, that",True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""256.7"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6610, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \\times 120 \\%=78"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""卡車油箱容量計算錯誤，一輛卡車的油箱較小型貨車的油箱大120%，因此卡科油箱為小貨車油箱的1+120%=2.2倍，而不是1.2倍"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the truck's tank capacity is incorrect. The tank of a truck is 120% larger than that of a mini-van, so the tank of a truck is 1 + 120% = 2.2 times that of a mini-van, not 1.2 times.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) $ 341.50 , b ) $ 344.60 , c ) $ 347.70 , d ) $ 350.80 , e ) $ 353.90"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""the service cost of 3 vans and 2 trucks is 5 * 2.20 $ 11.00 the fuel in 3 vans is 3 * 65 = 195 liters the fuel in 2 trucks is 2 * 65 * 2.2 = 286 liters the total fuel ( vans + trucks ) = 481 liters the total fuel cost is 481 * 0.7 = $ 336.70 the total cost is $ 336.70 + $ 11.00 = $ 347.70 the answer is c .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""the capacity of truck's tank $=65 \\times 120 \\%=78"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation of the truck's tank capacity is incorrect. The tank of a truck is 120% larger than that of a mini-van, so the tank of a truck is 1 + 120% = 2.2 times that of a mini-van, not 1.2 times."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""卡車油箱容量計算錯誤，一輛卡車的油箱較小型貨車的油箱大120%，因此卡科油箱為小貨車油箱的1+120%=2.2倍，而不是1.2倍""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:59421d3448ab2108,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,the average age of 8 men increases by 2 years when two women are included in place of two men of ages 20 and 10 years . find the average age of the women ?,\text { the average age of the women }=\frac{1}{2}(20+10)+2=17,Adds the average increase directly to the replaced values' average,the average age of the women =\frac{1}{2}(20+10)+2=17,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""17"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 8949, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\text { the average age of the women }=\\frac{1}{2}(20+10)+2=17"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""使八名男性平均年輪多兩歲，實際增加的年齡為2*8=16，不能直接將兩歲加上兩位女生的平均年齡，正確計算方法為：離開的兩位男生年齡和加上增加的年齡後除以2，(20+10+16)/2"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To increase the average age of 8 men by 2 years when two women are included in place of two men of ages 20 and 10 years, the actual increase in age is 2 * 8 = 16. It is incorrect to directly add the two years to the average age of the two women. The correct calculation method is to add the ages of the two departing men to the increased age and then divide by 2: (20 + 10 + 16) / 2""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 87 , b ) 98 , c ) 30 , d ) 28 , e ) 23"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""20 + 10 + 8 * 2 = 46 / 2 = 23 answer : e\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\text { the average age of the women }=\\frac{1}{2}(20+10)+2=17"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""To increase the average age of 8 men by 2 years when two women are included in place of two men of ages 20 and 10 years, the actual increase in age is 2 * 8 = 16. It is incorrect to directly add the two years to the average age of the two women. The correct calculation method is to add the ages of the two departing men to the increased age and then divide by 2: (20 + 10 + 16) / 2"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""使八名男性平均年輪多兩歲，實際增加的年齡為2*8=16，不能直接將兩歲加上兩位女生的平均年齡，正確計算方法為：離開的兩位男生年齡和加上增加的年齡後除以2，(20+10+16)/2""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:595b64cd678cefde,full,Comprehension error,if a person has two rectangular fields . the larger field has thrice the length and 4 times the width of the smaller field . if the smaller field has a length 50 % more than the width . if a person takes 20 minutes to complete one round of a smaller field then what is the time required to complete one round of a larger field ?,Assume the width of the smaller field is $x$ the length of the smaller field is $1.5 x$ the length of the larger field is $4.5 x$ the with of the larger field is $4 X$ the area of the smaller field $$ \Rightarrow x \cdot 1.5 x=1.5 x^2 $$ the area of the larger field $$ \begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow 4.5 x \cdot 4 x=18 x^2 \\ & 18 x^2 \div 1.5 x^2=12 \\ & 20 \times 12=240 \text { miss }  \end{aligned} $$,Uses area ratio instead of perimeter ratio to scale time for one round,18 x^2 \div 1.5 x^2=12 \quad 20 \times 12=240,ok,ok,,13,False,False,False,round,False,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""240"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 3987, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""the area of the smaller field $$ \\Rightarrow x \\cdot 1.5 x=1.5 x^2 $$ the area of the larger field $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 4.5 x \\cdot 4 x=18 x^2"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算相差倍數的想法正確，彈藥來比較的應為周長而不是面積"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The idea of calculating the difference in multiples is correct. However, the comparison should be based on perimeter, not area.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 69 minutes , b ) 68 minutes , c ) 58 minutes , d ) 48 minutes , e ) 67 minutes"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""let the width of the smaller rectangle is 4 units then , the length of the smaller rectangle is 6 units ( that is 50 % more than the width ) now the perimeter of the rectangle is 2 ( 6 + 4 ) = 20 units so , 20 units is covered in 20 units , implies covers one unit in one minute so now coming to the larger rectangle the width = 16 units , length = 18 units , perimeter = 2 ( 16 + 18 ) 68 units thus , to cover the larger field , 68 minutes required to cover the rectangle . answer : b"", ""error_equation"": ""the area of the smaller field $$ \\Rightarrow x \\cdot 1.5 x=1.5 x^2 $$ the area of the larger field $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 4.5 x \\cdot 4 x=18 x^2"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The idea of calculating the difference in multiples is correct. However, the comparison should be based on perimeter, not area."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算相差倍數的想法正確，彈藥來比較的應為周長而不是面積""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:59845fea25f4810a,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"an equal number of desks and bookcases are to be placed along a library wall that is 15 meters long . each desk is 2 meters long , and each bookshelf is 1.5 meters long . if the maximum possible number of desks and bookcases are to be placed along the wall , then the space along the wall that is left over will be how many meters k long ?","let the number of table $x$, of bookshelf $y$ $$ 2 x+1.5 y \leq 15 $$ \begin{tabular}{c|c|c} $x$ & $y$ & space left over \\ \hline 7 & 0 & 1 \\ 6 & 2 & 0 \\ 5 & & \end{tabular} Ans: 0 m",Fails to enforce that the two quantities must be equal,6 & 2 & 0,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"equal, that",True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""0"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9449, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{tabular}{c|c|c} $x$ & $y$ & space left over \\\\ \\hline 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & & \\end{tabular}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""答案不符合題目敘述，題數要求書桌和書櫃的數量必須相同，可以直接15除以書桌和書櫃的長度和，運算的餘數即為答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The answer does not match the description of the question. The question requires that the number of desks and bookcases be the same. You can directly divide 15 by the sum of the lengths of the desks and bookcases, and the remainder of the calculation is the answer.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 0.5 , b ) 1 , c ) 1.5 , d ) 2 , e ) 3"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""let x be the number of desks and bookcases that are placed along the library wall . 2 x + 1.5 x < 15 3.5 x < 15 since x is a non negative integer , the largest number x can be is 4 . when x is 4 , the desks and bookcases take up 3.5 * 4 = 14 m = k , leaving 1 m of empty space . thus , i believe the answer is b ) 1\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{tabular}{c|c|c} $x$ & $y$ & space left over \\\\ \\hline 7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & & \\end{tabular}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The answer does not match the description of the question. The question requires that the number of desks and bookcases be the same. You can directly divide 15 by the sum of the lengths of the desks and bookcases, and the remainder of the calculation is the answer."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""答案不符合題目敘述，題數要求書桌和書櫃的數量必須相同，可以直接15除以書桌和書櫃的長度和，運算的餘數即為答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5a1ca79d4c56d0e5,full,Arithmetical error,a trader sells 85 meters of cloth for rs . 8925 at the profit of rs . 10 per metre of cloth . what is the cost price of one metre of cloth ?,\begin{aligned} &\frac{8925}{85}=15\\ &15-10=5(rs) \end{aligned},Makes an incorrect division calculation,\frac{8925}{85}=15,ok,ok,,5,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 4, ""student_answer"": ""5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 10914, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""val"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Arithmetical error"", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{8925}{85}=15"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，8925/85的運算結果應為105而不是15，更正後即可求出正確答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The result of 8925/85 should be 105, not 15. After the correction, the correct answer can be obtained.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 26 , b ) 95 , c ) 90 , d ) 42 , e ) 22"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""b"", ""mathqa_category"": ""physics"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""sp of 1 m of cloth = 8925 / 85 = rs . 105 cp of 1 m of cloth = sp of 1 m of cloth - profit on 1 m of cloth = rs . 105 - rs . 10 = rs . 95 answer : b\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\frac{8925}{85}=15"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The calculation is incorrect. The result of 8925/85 should be 105, not 15. After the correction, the correct answer can be obtained."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""計算錯誤，8925/85的運算結果應為105而不是15，更正後即可求出正確答案""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5a3f142cd097040c,full,Careless error,peter ' s average ( arithmetic mean ) test score on 4 tests is 78 . what must be the student ' s score on a 5 th test for the peter ' s average score on the 5 tests to be 80 ?,80 \times 5-70 \times 4=120,Uses the wrong average to calculate the original total,80 \times 5-70 \times 4=120,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""120"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 11732, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Careless error"", ""error_equation"": ""80 \\times 5-70 \\times 4=120"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""粗心看錯題目數字，原來的平均為78而不是70，因此正確過程為80*5-78*4=88"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student seems to have misread the numbers in the question. The original average was 78, not 70. Therefore, the correct calculation should be: 80 * 5 - 78 * 4 = 88""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 80 , b ) 82 , c ) 84 , d ) 86 , e ) 88"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""e"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""e . 88 peter must score at least an 80 for sure . if he scores an 8 , then he will need to score 2 pots for each of the 4 other tests tomake upthe difference . they each were at 78 ( at least the average is , but this is a small point and does n ' t matter to the answer ) . so 4 tests that were each 2 points short of the 80 average that is desired means the next test must be 8 points higher than the desired average , so 80 + 8 = 88 ."", ""error_equation"": ""80 \\times 5-70 \\times 4=120"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student seems to have misread the numbers in the question. The original average was 78, not 70. Therefore, the correct calculation should be: 80 * 5 - 78 * 4 = 88"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""粗心看錯題目數字，原來的平均為78而不是70，因此正確過程為80*5-78*4=88""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5a6c6f0c046838ea,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"in a triangle abc , point d is on side ab and point e is on side ac , such that bced is a trapezium . de : bc = 3 : 5 . calculate the ratio of the area of triangle ade and the trapezium bced .","ratio of de: bc equal to the ratio of the area, Ans: 3:5",Confuses a length ratio with an area ratio,ratio of de: bc equal to the ratio of the area,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 5, ""student_answer"": ""3:5"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 9420, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""test"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""ratio of de: bc equal to the ratio of the area"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""觀念錯誤，還需考慮到兩者的高和三角形與梯形的面積公式不同的問題，由於de:bc=3:5因此兩者的高的比值為3:(5-3)=3:2，三角形ade的面積為3*3/2=9/2，而梯形debc的面積為(3+5)*2/2=8，因此面積比為(9/2)/8=9/16"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept is incorrect. You need to consider the different heights and the different area formulas for triangles and trapezoids. Since DE:BC = 3:5, the ratio of their heights is 3:(5-3) = 3:2. The area of triangle ADE is 3*3/2 = 9/2, and the area of trapezoid BCED is (3+5)*2/2 = 8. Therefore, the ratio of areas is (9/2)/8 = 9/16.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""['a ) 9 / 16', 'b ) 8 / 16', 'c ) 7 / 16', 'd ) 6 / 16', 'e ) 5 / 16']"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""geometry"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""area of tri ( ade ) / area of tri ( abc ) = de ^ 2 / bc ^ 2 since tri ( ade ) - tri ( abc ) area of tri ( ade ) / area of tri ( abc ) = 9 / 25 area of tri ( abc ) / area of tri ( ade ) = 25 / 9 area of tri ( abc ) = area of tri ( ade ) + area of trap ( bcde ) ( area of tri ( ade ) + area of trap ( bcde ) ) / area of tri ( ade ) = 25 / 9 1 + area of trap ( bcde ) / area of tri ( ade ) = 25 / 9 take 1 on both sides area of trap ( bcde ) / area of tri ( ade ) = ( 25 / 9 ) - 1 = 16 / 9 since question is asking for area of tri ( ade ) / area of trap ( bcde ) = 9 / 16 answer : a"", ""error_equation"": ""ratio of de: bc equal to the ratio of the area"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The concept is incorrect. You need to consider the different heights and the different area formulas for triangles and trapezoids. Since DE:BC = 3:5, the ratio of their heights is 3:(5-3) = 3:2. The area of triangle ADE is 3*3/2 = 9/2, and the area of trapezoid BCED is (3+5)*2/2 = 8. Therefore, the ratio of areas is (9/2)/8 = 9/16."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""觀念錯誤，還需考慮到兩者的高和三角形與梯形的面積公式不同的問題，由於de:bc=3:5因此兩者的高的比值為3:(5-3)=3:2，三角形ade的面積為3*3/2=9/2，而梯形debc的面積為(3+5)*2/2=8，因此面積比為(9/2)/8=9/16""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5a7ad9d09aa7cd56,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,a fair price shopkeeper takes 10 % profit on his goods . he lost 20 % goods during theft . his loss percent is :,"Assume the cost per goods is $\chi \&$ the number of goods is $y$ $$ \text { original revenue }=1.1 x y $$ revenue after 10 ss $20 \%$ goods $=1.1 X \cdot 0,8 y$ $$ =0.88 x y $$ $$ \begin{aligned} \text { the loss percent } & =\frac{1.1 x y-0.88 x y}{x y} \\ & =\frac{0.22 x y}{x y}=0.22 \\ & =22 \%  \end{aligned} $$",Confuses lost revenue with loss relative to total cost,the loss percent $ =\frac{1.1 x y-0.88 x y}{x y}$,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,"loss, lost",False,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""22"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6019, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\text { the loss percent } & =\\frac{1.1 x y-0.88 x y}{x y} \\\\ & =\\frac{0.22 x y}{x y}=0.22 \\\\ & =22 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""店主的損失百分比應由物品的成本價來計算，而不是由收益後的金額計算"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The shopkeeper's loss percentage should be calculated based on the cost price of the goods, not on the amount after profit.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 10 , b ) 13 , c ) 12 , d ) 18 , e ) 19"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""c"", ""mathqa_category"": ""gain"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""c 12 % suppose he has 100 items . let c . p . of each item be $ 1 . total cost = $ 100 . number of items left after theft = 80 . s . p . of each item = $ 1.10 total sale = 1.10 * 80 = $ 88 hence , loss % = 12 / 100 * 100 = 12 %\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\text { the loss percent } & =\\frac{1.1 x y-0.88 x y}{x y} \\\\ & =\\frac{0.22 x y}{x y}=0.22 \\\\ & =22 \\%"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The shopkeeper's loss percentage should be calculated based on the cost price of the goods, not on the amount after profit."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""店主的損失百分比應由物品的成本價來計算，而不是由收益後的金額計算""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5abaabbd099fc550,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,"each year for 4 years , a farmer increased the number of trees in a certain orchard by 1 / 4 of the number of trees in the orchard of the preceding year . if all of the trees thrived and there were 5625 trees in the orchard at the end of 4 year period , how many trees were in the orchard at the beginning of the 4 year period .",assume there were $x$ trees in the beginning. $$ \begin{aligned} \left(1+\frac{1}{4}\right)^3 x & =5625 \\ \left(\frac{5}{4}\right)^3 x & =5625 \\ \frac{125}{64} x & =5625 \\ x & =2880 \end{aligned} $$,Uses three growth periods instead of four,\left(1+\frac{1}{4}\right)^3 x =5625,ok,ok,,7,False,False,False,,False,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""2880"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 8822, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\left(1+\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^3 x & =5625"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""列式錯誤，題目是說經過了四年，每一年會增加為前一年的5/4倍，正確列式應為x*(5/4)^4=5625"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The problem states that each year, the number of trees increased by 1/4 of the number of trees in the orchard of the preceding year. Therefore, the correct equation should be: x*(5/4)^4 = 5625""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 2304 , b ) 2305 , c ) 2309 , d ) 2310 , e ) 2311"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""trees increase by 1 / 4 the number of trees in preceding year . hence , correct answer must be divisible by 4 . based on divisibility rules , if last 2 digits are divisible by 4 then the number is divisible by 4 . thus , we can eliminate b , c , d , e the answer to be a again , trees increase by 1 / 4 the number of trees in preceding year . hence , the number of trees increase by 5 / 4 times the number of trees the preceding year . if x = initial number of trees = 2304 year 1 = 5 / 4 x year 2 = ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) x year 3 = ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) x year 4 = ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) x only for answer d : ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) ( 5 / 4 ) 2304 = 5625 hence , correct answer = a\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\left(1+\\frac{1}{4}\\right)^3 x & =5625"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The equation is incorrect. The problem states that each year, the number of trees increased by 1/4 of the number of trees in the orchard of the preceding year. Therefore, the correct equation should be: x*(5/4)^4 = 5625"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""列式錯誤，題目是說經過了四年，每一年會增加為前一年的5/4倍，正確列式應為x*(5/4)^4=5625""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5acf75647d0e3b05,full,Wrong mathematical operation/concept,20 chess players take part in a tournament . every player plays twice with each of his opponents . how many games are to be played ?,\begin{aligned} & 19+18+17+\ldots+3+2+1 \\ & =19+\frac{18}{2}(18+1) \\ & =19 \times 10 \\ & =190  \end{aligned},Counts each pair only once instead of counting both games.,19+18+17+\ldots+3+2+1,ok,ok,,10,False,False,False,"each, games",True,1,"{""student_id"": 3, ""student_answer"": ""190"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 6247, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Wrong mathematical operation/concept"", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} & 19+18+17+\\ldots+3+2+1 \\\\ & =19+\\frac{18}{2}(18+1) \\\\ & =19 \\times 10 \\\\ & =190  \\end{aligned}"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""每個選手會與對手玩兩次不是一次，因此正確的計算方法應為19*2+18*2+---+1*2=380"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Each player will play twice with each of his opponents, not once. Therefore, the correct calculation should be 19*2+18*2+---+1*2=380.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 380 , b ) 470 , c ) 560 , d ) 650 , e ) 740"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""\""2 * 20 c 2 = 2 * 190 = 380 the answer is a .\"""", ""error_equation"": ""\\begin{aligned} & 19+18+17+\\ldots+3+2+1 \\\\ & =19+\\frac{18}{2}(18+1) \\\\ & =19 \\times 10 \\\\ & =190  \\end{aligned}"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""Each player will play twice with each of his opponents, not once. Therefore, the correct calculation should be 19*2+18*2+---+1*2=380."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""每個選手會與對手玩兩次不是一次，因此正確的計算方法應為19*2+18*2+---+1*2=380""}",,,,
mathedu,mathedu:5ba38ae4abaa10d1,full,Comprehension error,"how many 3 digit positive integers with distinct digits are there , which are not multiples of 10 ?","3 digit positive integers, which are multiples of 10 $$ \begin{aligned} & \Rightarrow 100,110,120,130, \cdots, 970,980,990 . \\ & \Rightarrow 90 \text { numbers } \\ & 100 \sim 999 \Rightarrow 900 \text { numbers. } \\ & 900-90=810  \end{aligned} $$",Ignores the distinct-digits restriction when counting the total,100 \sim 999 \Rightarrow 900 \text { numbers. },ok,ok,,8,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""student_id"": 2, ""student_answer"": ""810"", ""correct_or_not"": ""wrong"", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_ch"": """", ""the_reason_why_student_cant_solve_en"": """", ""mathedu_id"": 34828, ""mathedu_split_file"": ""train"", ""error_counts"": 1, ""teacher_review_errors"": [{""error_type"": ""Comprehension error"", ""error_equation"": ""3 digit positive integers, which are multiples of 10 $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 100,110,120,130, \\cdots, 970,980,990 . \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 90 \\text { numbers } \\\\ & 100 \\sim 999 \\Rightarrow 900 \\text { numbers. } \\\\ & 900-90=810  \\end{aligned} $$"", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有考慮到三個位數皆不相同的條件，可以將各個位數可能的數字總數相成來得出答案"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not consider the condition that all three digits are distinct. The answer can be obtained by multiplying the total number of possible digits for each position.""}], ""mathqa_options"": ""a ) 576 , b ) 520 , c ) 504 , d ) 432 , e ) 348"", ""mathqa_correct"": ""a"", ""mathqa_category"": ""general"", ""mathqa_rationale"": ""a number not to be a multiple of 10 should not have the units digit of 0 . xxx 9 options for the first digit ( from 1 to 9 inclusive ) . 8 options for the third digit ( from 1 to 9 inclusive minus the one we used for the first digit ) . 8 options for the second digit ( from 0 to 9 inclusive minus 2 digits we used for the first and the third digits ) 9 * 8 * 8 = 576 . answer : a ."", ""error_equation"": ""3 digit positive integers, which are multiples of 10 $$ \\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow 100,110,120,130, \\cdots, 970,980,990 . \\\\ & \\Rightarrow 90 \\text { numbers } \\\\ & 100 \\sim 999 \\Rightarrow 900 \\text { numbers. } \\\\ & 900-90=810  \\end{aligned} $$"", ""teacher_advice_en"": ""The student did not consider the condition that all three digits are distinct. The answer can be obtained by multiplying the total number of possible digits for each position."", ""teacher_advice_ch"": ""同學沒有考慮到三個位數皆不相同的條件，可以將各個位數可能的數字總數相成來得出答案""}",,,,
