And the total number of notes put into the complaints and compliments bins is 30 + 60 = 90.
 90",Omits the additional quantity when computing the overall total,And the total number of notes put into the complaints and compliments bins is 30 + 60 = 90.,ok,ok,,9,False,False,False,,True,1,"{""incorrect_index"": 3, ""incorrect_step"": ""And the total number of notes put into the complaints and compliments bins is 30 + 60 = 90."", ""error_description"": ""The 10 scattered notes have been omitted from the total."", ""reference_solution"": ""There are a total of 5 rows of red notes * 6 notes per row = 30 red notes on the board.\nThere are 2 blue notes per red notes * 30 red notes = 60 blue notes under the red notes.\nWith the other blue notes at the bottom of the board, there are a total of 60 + 10 = 70 blue notes.\nSo in total, there are 30 red notes + 70 blue notes = 100 notes in total.\n 100"", ""dialog_history"": [{""text"": ""Hi Ronny, You have made a mistake in your solution.  Please check your total number of blue notes."", ""user"": ""Teacher""}, {""text"": ""Oh, I see. The total number of blue notes is actually 70. So the total number of notes put into the complaints and compliments bins is 30 + 70 = 100."", ""user"": ""Student""}, {""text"": ""Yes, that's correct."", ""user"": ""Teacher""}], ""student_correct_response"": ""To find the total number of red notes, I multiplied the number of rows (5) by the number of notes in each row (6), which equals 30 red notes. Then, I found the number of blue notes under the red notes by multiplying 2 blue notes per red note by the total number of red notes, which equals 60 blue notes. Adding the 10 blue notes scattered at the bottom of the board to the 60 blue notes under the red notes gives a total of 70 blue notes. Finally, I added the total number of red notes (30) to the total number of blue notes (70) to get 100 notes in total."", ""topic"": ""Math Word Problem"", ""student_incorrect_solution_steps"": [""There are 5 x 6 = 30 red notes."", ""So there are 30 x 2 = 60 blue notes that were under the red notes."", ""Therefore the total number of blue notes is 60 + 10 = 70."", ""And the total number of notes put into the complaints and compliments bins is 30 + 60 = 90."", "" 90""]}",,,,
stepwise,stepwise:027e790b446c4ec4,full,Misunderstanding of a question,"James visits 20 houses to try and make a sale.  He manages to sell something in every house.  The next day he visits twice as many houses but only sold to 80% of houses.  If he sold two things at each house in each of the two days, how many items did he sell?","James sold 20 x 2 = 40 items on the first day.
