Therefore, the three companies paid a total of $36,000 for the ads combined.
 36,000",Fails to multiply the per-company total by the number of companies,The total area for 10 ad spaces is 60 x 10 = 600 square feet.,ok,ok,,11,False,False,False,companies,True,1,"{""incorrect_index"": 3, ""incorrect_step"": ""Therefore, the three companies paid a total of $36,000 for the ads combined."", ""error_description"": ""missed a final step"", ""reference_solution"": ""A size 12 foot by 5-foot rectangle ad takes 12*5 = 60 square feet since the area of a rectangle is l*w.\nIf each company bought 10 ad spaces, the total area that their ads took is 60*10 = 600 square feet.\nIf each square foot of ad space was charged at $60, 600 square feet of ads cost $60*600 = $36000\nIf all three companies each purchased an equal number of ad space, together they paid $36000*3 = $108000\n 108000"", ""dialog_history"": [{""text"": ""Hi Emily, can you walk me through your solution?"", ""user"": ""Teacher""}, {""text"": ""Sure! I started by calculating the total area of one ad space, which is 12 x 5 = 60 square feet. Then, I multiplied that by 10 ad spaces to get the total area of all 10 ad spaces, which is 600 square feet. Finally, I multiplied 600 square feet by $60 per square foot to get the total cost of $36,000."", ""user"": ""Student""}, {""text"": ""Excellent, so we know that each company bought 600 square feet of ad space for $60 per square foot making $36,000. If each company bought this what would the total cost be for all three?"", ""user"": ""Teacher""}], ""student_correct_response"": ""A size 12 foot by 5-foot rectangle ad takes 12*5 = 60 square feet since the area of a rectangle is l*w. If each company bought 10 ad spaces, the total area that their ads took is 60*10 = 600 square feet. If each square foot of ad space was charged at $60, 600 square feet of ads cost $60*600 = $36000. If all three companies each purchased an equal number of ad space, together they paid $36000*3 = $108000."", ""topic"": ""Math Word Problem"", ""student_incorrect_solution_steps"": [""The total area of one ad space is 12 x 5 = 60 square feet."", ""So the total area for 10 ad spaces is 60 x 10 = 600 square feet."", ""The total cost for 600 square feet at $60 per square foot is 600 x 60 = $36,000."", ""Therefore, the three companies paid a total of $36,000 for the ads combined."", "" 36,000""]}",,,,
stepwise,stepwise:662317903c4ae862,full,Missing / Wrong factual knowledge,"Sandy wants to lose as much weight as Joey does but needs 4 weeks to lose the same amount of weight that Joey loses in a single week. If Joey loses 8 pounds in 4 weeks, how many weeks will it take Sandy to lose the same amount of weight?","Joey loses 8 pounds in 4 weeks, so he loses 8/4 = 2 pounds per week.
